{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues","id":1518471,"title":"W5 Anti-Indigeneity and other Issues.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-21T18:40:10-07:00","id":1518471,"title":"W5 Anti-Indigeneity and other Issues.","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition-and-the-anti-indigeneity-in-the-gaming-industry.912221/#post-24879821\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...#post-24879821</a><br /> <br /> James has released his long promised post on his experiences. Theres a lot more than whats been released here but theres more than enough to get angry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T19:27:21-07:00","id":1518474,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the end. Time to perform the Rite of the Winter Wolf on this game, because only a spiritual sequel unaffiliated with the company seems like it could further where W:tA had actually been going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T23:25:21-07:00","id":1518482,"title":"","content":"So I was right with my theory... the whole Get-thing is a remnant of the first version. But then why did Justin Achilli go around talking about that other version that was all focused on how they couldn't figure out &quot;verbs&quot; for the Get of Fenris in W5...? That's just so bizarre...<br /> <br /> Also didn't expect that ultimately everything collapsed due to the vague umbrella-term of &quot;creative differences&quot;... I<br /> <br /> And <i>now </i>I'm really afraid of how the Get will be portrayed in this version... They really are going to go with the idea that in W5 the Swords Of Heimdall <i>are </i>the Get Of Fenris, won't they...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T23:26:55-07:00","id":1518483,"title":"","content":"....So, okay, few things;<br /> <br /> 1. The Swords of Heimindal bs. First of all it is clear the main guy did NOT know the game well at all. That and just the constant push to have them as a whole as nazi. I expected the issue to be that but I did not expect it to be IN HOUSE O.o<br /> <br /> 2. The Native Tribes rigmarole. First of all, holy shit with the Gale Stalkers mess. Second, it is quite tone-deaf to tell a person FROM that culture that they are a SJW, that the old tribe names are fine AND not listen when someone is telling you stuff you could not possibly know better.<br /> <br /> Honestly, given the Fenrir drama, it is no wonder they were made the bad guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T23:27:53-07:00","id":1518484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518482#post1518482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was right with my theory... the whole Get-thing is a remnant of the first version. But then why did Justin Achilli go around talking about that other version that was all focused on how they couldn't figure out &quot;verbs&quot; for the Get of Fenris in W5...? That's just so bizarre...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a lie to cover up the real reason, which they hoped to stay private.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T23:47:53-07:00","id":1518486,"title":"","content":"Forgive me but by reading Muammar's quotes and putting them into the context of what we know about W5 and what Sambrano says, I see enormous creative differences more than consistent anti-Indigenialism<br /> <br /> Besides the very shallow initial idea of killing off Younger Brother, which is really just facepalmish level of stupid, what is implied in their exchanges is that disconnecting tribes from real world ethnicities was already part of the original setting guidelines, a change Sambrano wasn't in line with.<br /> <br /> As he wasn't in line with using the Fenrir as an in-setting villain, in line with the new creative direction wanted to present political extremism as a real threat to societies.<br /> <br /> At one point, he and Muammar are basically saying to each other &quot;you are not bringing meaningful ideas to the setting, only your personal preferences&quot;: Muammar wanted no cultural tribes and a Werewolf villain, Sambrano wanted two really Indigenous tribes and a heroic Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> It's basically the rift we see in Reddit and forum discussions, but within the creative team. And if relations between them were so deteriorated, I'm fairly sure that bringing everything under Justin Achilli was basically what was needed to get the product moving and breaking the deadlock.<br /> <br /> I'm glad Sambrano's proposals on Indigenous names have mostly been kept, and hope he gets credited for his writing work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 07-22-2023, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T00:11:21-07:00","id":1518487,"title":"","content":"Two interesting tidbits that may or may not mean anything in relation to this:<br /> <br /> At one point in his post Sambrano says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While doing so, he also decided that it was appropriate to refer to this entirely Native American tribe by the word \u201csavages\u201d a slur that has been specifically used to dehumanize Native Americans, and then mocked my rewrite that focused on presenting them as stewards of the land using Indigenous methodologies and praxes, instead of the \u201csavage\u201d racist stereotypes they were presented as in previous editions. Further, as in the above quote, even after it was communicated that the use of this term was problematic, he kept doubling-down to use it to refer to the Tribe. </div> </div> </div>The reason this section caught my attention is that during the interview with Outstar in October of last year Justin Achilli talked about the cultural sensitivity reader they would employ to proofread their work. And the example he gave was that W5 wouldn't use the word &quot;savage&quot; at any point in the book.<br /> <br /> The other thing is about Justin Achilli leaving this January. Just think about it: This post is mostly about Karim Muammar, the editor of the WOD-team. Justin Achilli left after writing was done but <i>before </i>any editing took place. Might mean something or might not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T00:39:58-07:00","id":1518489,"title":"","content":"Reading the quotes from the correspondence from Karim Muammar are shocking, though hardly surprising. This is a game where editorial overview is being driven by people who do not even have the most basic skills required to do what they are required to do, and it shows. I don't agree with everything that James Sambrano says, but it is fairly clear that he has an understanding of some of the basic issues of representation which should be dealt with in a project like this. Karim ... well the most polite thing to say is that he isn't showing what might be the expected understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T00:42:17-07:00","id":1518490,"title":"","content":"So they made Get ,, one tribe, one wolf, one alpha&quot; shit? What the f...k is this?? HOW it is possible that one or two man ruined the game by lack of fundamental knowledge of setting and characters players can make??? What is wrong in company that they are trying make far wing political concepts as main bad enemies? In political view it might be as well far left and make Children of Gaia antagonists or monarchy and Silver Fangs??? What about making again evil camps like Masks or Nidhogg and what about the WYRM?? The cosmic entropy? <br /> I don't understand that degeneration of ideas presented in older editions. I am convinced that book of weaver wyrm and wyld would be total pack of nonsense I never encountered in my entire life.<br /> If there is some possibility that any of forum users have even the smallest chance of letting them know that after all they destroyed the game please do it for sake of mental stability of fanbase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T01:44:23-07:00","id":1518491,"title":"","content":"A awkward read but very interesting i almost wish i had a pen to circle the key points, this largely confirms some of my suspicions about wiping ethnicity from the tribes and why. What does surprise me was the plan just to kill off Wendigo which is outright dumb on a number of levels.<br /> <br /> Its also slightly alarming that the khelil was oblivious to get history especially with such a sensitive subject and when corrected on it he simply powered on with &quot;all get are nazis anyway.&quot; This guy outright shouldn't be writting the setting if true.<br /> <br /> <br /> The insensitivity on the subject of First nation people is also surprising as I recall he's previously accused other people if bigotry towards his own background so I'd presumed he'd be more sensitive about this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518482#post1518482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was right with my theory... the whole Get-thing is a remnant of the first version. But then why did Justin Achilli go around talking about that other version that was all focused on how they couldn't figure out &quot;verbs&quot; for the Get of Fenris in W5...? That's just so bizarre...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it was an obvious lie, like the one about how having the get as an enemy tribe was a way of expanding antagonists (you can just make more tribes if you're rebooting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T01:59:14-07:00","id":1518493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518486#post1518486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">