key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:00:35-07:00","id":1518495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518490#post1518490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they made Get ,, one tribe, one wolf, one alpha&quot; shit? What the f...k is this?? HOW it is possible that one or two man ruined the game by lack of fundamental knowledge of setting and characters players can make??? What is wrong in company that they are trying make far wing political concepts as main bad enemies? In political view it might be as well far left and make Children of Gaia antagonists or monarchy and Silver Fangs??? What about making again evil camps like Masks or Nidhogg and what about the WYRM?? The cosmic entropy?<br /> I don't understand that degeneration of ideas presented in older editions. I am convinced that book of weaver wyrm and wyld would be total pack of nonsense I never encountered in my entire life.<br /> If there is some possibility that any of forum users have even the smallest chance of letting them know that after all they destroyed the game please do it for sake of mental stability of fanbase.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't listen to their own writing team, consultants or playtesters why would they listen to us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:09:11-07:00","id":1518496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518487#post1518487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two interesting tidbits that may or may not mean anything in relation to this:<br /> <br /> At one point in his post Sambrano says:<br /> <br /> The reason this section caught my attention is that during the interview with Outstar in October of last year Justin Achilli talked about the cultural sensitivity reader they would employ to proofread their work. And the example he gave was that W5 wouldn't use the word &quot;savage&quot; at any point in the book.<br /> <br /> The other thing is about Justin Achilli leaving this January. Just think about it: This post is mostly about Karim Muammar, the editor of the WOD-team. Justin Achilli left after writing was done but <i>before </i>any editing took place. Might mean something or might not...</div> </div> </div> </div>For me a big part of it is the fact that the writers were having to tell the creative leads huge amounts of what I would consider Basic Setting Knowledge. You would think that those developing the game would have some sort of familiarity with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:30:24-07:00","id":1518499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518491#post1518491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also slightly alarming that the khelil was oblivious to get history especially with such a sensitive subject and when corrected on it he simply powered on with &quot;all get are nazis anyway.&quot; This guy outright shouldn't be writting the setting if true.<br /> <br /> <br /> The insensitivity on the subject of First nation people is also surprising as I recall he's previously accused other people if bigotry towards his own background so I'd presumed he'd be more sensitive about this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sambrano is talking about Karim Muammar, the one you have in mind is Khaldoun Kheklil, but the two of them are different authors <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:34:33-07:00","id":1518500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518493#post1518493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're just excusing and sweeping under the rug the blatantly racist and abusive behaviour by KM? Wow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In those quotes, I'm not seeing anything blatantly racist or abusive, he is writing that &quot;Wendigo was an ok name in 2018&quot; (I suppose, when Sambrano was working on W20), and that his idea for the Galestalkers was too much &quot;just Native Americans&quot;, and wildly different from &quot;Savage wolves of the Tundra&quot;, which is... err... a line about wolves, not about Indigenous people. <br /> <br /> So far, what I see is a very bad creative relationship, that I have no doubt escalated in a very non productive and vitriolic way. <br /> <br /> But it's one side of a story, and based just on those two or three Google Docs comments, I don't think we are seeing abuse so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:38:49-07:00","id":1518501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518499#post1518499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sambrano is talking about Karim Muammar, the one you have in mind is Khaldoun Kheklil, but the two of them are different authors <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oof My bad. My reading disability strikes again. Im not that familar with karim but his credits on white wolf wiki. hardly reflect well on him with the infamous carmarilla 5th ed sitting there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:40:23-07:00","id":1518502,"title":"","content":"Admittedly as someone who has seen more of the correspondence in question than whats in this document I'm judging it more harshly but just not seeing any issues with any of the language used at all is....something I cannot comprehend being done in good faith so probably best to just ignore each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:41:56-07:00","id":1518504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518500#post1518500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In those quotes, I'm not seeing anything blatantly racist or abusive, he is writing that &quot;Wendigo was an ok name in 2018&quot; (I suppose, when Sambrano was working on W20), and that his idea for the Galestalkers was too much &quot;just Native Americans&quot;, and wildly different from &quot;Savage wolves of the Tundra&quot;, which is... err... a line about wolves, not about Indigenous people.<br /> <br /> So far, what I see is a very bad creative relationship, that I have no doubt escalated in a very non productive and vitriolic way.<br /> <br /> But it's one side of a story, and based just on those two or three Google Docs comments, I don't think we are seeing abuse so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't think he's being deliberatly full on racist even i think he's a bad writter, he comes across as a bit of a jerk and his comments are poorly worded. I'd certainly like to hear his end of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:54:08-07:00","id":1518505,"title":"","content":"Oh lord. I've heard some rummaging about this, but this sounds like a rather unhealthy work environment. No wonder W5 is as all over the place as it is.<br /> I'm sorry for James's experience and would have loved to see his conception of the &quot;Winter Teeth&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:54:22-07:00","id":1518506,"title":"","content":"This is a bit outside of the core discussion, but:<br /> It would depend on the contract at the time whether this is legally possible, but I would be really interested in seeing James' write-ups for the Tribes, so I can fix up W20 where needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T03:04:37-07:00","id":1518507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518496#post1518496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me a big part of it is the fact that the writers were having to tell the creative leads huge amounts of what I would consider Basic Setting Knowledge. You would think that those developing the game would have some sort of familiarity with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just basic familiarity with the setting which is lacking; it's a lack of the kind of skills which anyone in an editorial position ought to have. Being an editor is hard; there is an assumption that editing is a glorified proof-reading role, where your job is to make sure that words and sentences are right, and to have opinions on what people are writing. Karim Muammar seems to have been very active in this latter activity. But, actually, editorial roles are about making sure texts work, on all levels that they have to work. Spelling and grammar is, of course, part of this, but working out what needs to be addressed, and how the writers working for you need to be guided to the end point is an essential function of this. You need, in broad terms, to have a better and broader understanding of the function of the text than the people whose work you are editing.<br /> <br /> This is what makes the exchanges quoted by Sambrano remarkable (and, as we can see them in the screenshots, I think we can have confidence as to what is being discussed by Sambrano is at least relatively accurate). So, an editor-in-chief should have some awareness of why cultural representation might matter to marginalised groups and how to discuss this with writers in a non-patronising manner. An editor-in-chief certainly should know that &quot;Native American&quot; needs capitalisation.<br /> <br /> In a proper industry, you would have an experienced person, with a history of appropriate past roles, as the editor-in-chief of a product line. Unfortunately, the gaming industry doesn't have the appropriate maturity to manage this, so we get end products like the upcoming edition of <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T03:09:34-07:00","id":1518508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518506#post1518506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit outside of the core discussion, but:<br /> It would depend on the contract at the time whether this is legally possible, but I would be really interested in seeing James' write-ups for the Tribes, so I can fix up W20 where needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, he signed an NDA with Paradox (or whatever the status of WOD5E was at that time) about the material he produced for the Hunter Entertainment version and that he wouldn't republish it elsewhere. But then his stuff is appearing in this version of W5 that is about to come out. So it's like Paradox are the ones who have broken the NDA first. The whole point of that was for that stuff to stay secret but since this new version of W5 has put it out into the public...<br /> <br /> But I'm not a lawyer so who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T03:21:16-07:00","id":1518509,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I just hope that when sometime in the future someone tries to develop W6 they will make the entire development team read the info on this debacle and inform it in no uncertain terms that this time this type of dumpster fire is not to take place.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T03:36:40-07:00","id":1518510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518509#post1518509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I just hope that when sometime in the future someone tries to develop W6 they will make the entire development team read the info on this debacle and inform it in no uncertain terms that this time this type of dumpster fire is not to take place.</span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an interesting subtext that we're already anticipating course correction with w6 and w5 isn't out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:03:30-07:00","id":1518513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518482#post1518482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was right with my theory... the whole Get-thing is a remnant of the first version. But then why did Justin Achilli go around talking about that other version that was all focused on how they couldn't figure out &quot;verbs&quot; for the Get of Fenris in W5...? That's just so bizarre...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I think that Achili was straight out lying to us. It's a PR excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:21:57-07:00","id":1518514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518513#post1518513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? I think that Achili was straight out lying to us. It's a PR excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is really an excuse as much as offering a much better option than &quot;The previous version had a big drama about Fenrir and the writing reflected that. There was a push to make all Fenrir into nazi from top down.&quot;<br /> <br /> The push for that plotline is BAFFLING, especially given the OTHER controversies WoD5 has had. As James says, Fenrir are VERY popular, it makes no sense to turn them into...that. Did the person pushing for it just see the glyph, nordic/germanic and decide that was good enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:38:24-07:00","id":1518516,"title":"","content":"As an aside, nothing shows how poorly Karim Muammar knew the setting than the push for the FENRIR to be the right-wing tribe. Because there exists a tribe in the game that ISN'T as willing to push back bad leaders and in older editions had systematic requirement FOR purity of bloodline.<br /> <br /> On top of that, Silver Fangs would fit the modern intellectual Right-Winger stereotype better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:45:22-07:00","id":1518517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518510#post1518510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its an interesting subtext that we're already anticipating course correction with w6 and w5 isn't out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine it's 2030, WOD5E is supposed to end and the creative team is looking for a concept. Then one cool guy is like &quot;Get this...&quot;. He stands up, walks to the whiteboard and writes WOD5. He looks around the room and says &quot;Now watch this...&quot;. He erases the 5 - and replaces it with... &quot;40th&quot;. &quot;The new edition is called World of Darkness 40th Anniversary Edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T05:19:46-07:00","id":1518518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518517#post1518517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine it's 2030, WOD5E is supposed to end and the creative team is looking for a concept. Then one cool guy is like &quot;Get this...&quot;. He stands up, walks to the whiteboard and writes WOD5. He looks around the room and says &quot;Now watch this...&quot;. He erases the 5 - and replaces it with... &quot;40th&quot;. &quot;The new edition is called World of Darkness 40th Anniversary Edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Brilliant! We'll get an ai to write half of it and we'll unfreeze mark's head to edit the rest and then use the budget as hush money.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T07:36:20-07:00","id":1518520,"title":"","content":"Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T07:41:46-07:00","id":1518521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518520#post1518520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I have my thread on these forums. W5 has some nice ideas (no nation, tribe names, potentially pariah dog shifters) that might work in a setting more designed for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T07:44:56-07:00","id":1518522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518520#post1518520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would someone put the energy into rebuilding an edition when there are serviceable editions available?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T07:45:48-07:00","id":1518523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518514#post1518514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is really an excuse as much as offering a much better option than &quot;The previous version had a big drama about Fenrir and the writing reflected that. There was a push to make all Fenrir into nazi from top down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which even then it seems...strange and also concerning that they didn't even lead with &quot;we got rid of the Get because of its long history of Nazi-coding&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518520#post1518520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as like a free supplement nothing is stopping people. But on official channels like Storyteller's Vault? No. It's explicit in their ToS that you can't publish brand new editions of a corebook on there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T07:53:55-07:00","id":1518524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518521#post1518521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I have my thread on these forums. W5 has some nice ideas (no nation, tribe names, potentially pariah dog shifters) that might work in a setting more designed for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, your approach is just a a new take on the material. Only problem is that you cannot really publish that due to how the license works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T08:06:52-07:00","id":1518526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518500#post1518500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In those quotes, I'm not seeing anything blatantly racist or abusive, he is writing that &quot;Wendigo was an ok name in 2018&quot; (I suppose, when Sambrano was working on W20), and that his idea for the Galestalkers was too much &quot;just Native Americans&quot;, and wildly different from &quot;Savage wolves of the Tundra&quot;, which is... err... a line about wolves, not about Indigenous people.<br /> <br /> So far, what I see is a very bad creative relationship, that I have no doubt escalated in a very non productive and vitriolic way.<br /> <br /> But it's one side of a story, and based just on those two or three Google Docs comments, I don't think we are seeing abuse so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you capitalized the words \u201cNative Americans\u201d there. There could be a number of reasons you correctly did that. You could have done it because you understand the cultural significance behind capitalization of the words, you could be following basic rules you were taught in school regarding the English language, etc.<br /> <br /> Karim didn\u2019t. There\u2019s a screenshot of it. Now I\u2019m going on the premise that he isn\u2019t horrible at his job as Editor In-Chief and is aware of how to properly use the English language. It could have been a mistake, but writing out the word \u201camerican\u201d in lower case is going to autocorrect to capitalized on any mobile device and on a computer if you type the word in lower case you\u2019re getting a red squiggly line below the word telling you it should be capitalized. <br /> <br /> With that being said, it\u2019s difficult to look at his use of lower case as anything but a deliberate attempt to minimize Native American folks. Micro aggressions like that, especially when directed to an Indigenous person, seems like abusive behavior to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T08:10:19-07:00","id":1518528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518520#post1518520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering one of if not the first Hunter: The Reckoning STV releases was bringing back the Imbued, I would think it\u2019s a possibility for a Fan-made W5 book to be done, if not there certainly Dark Pack (free) is an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:26:49-07:00","id":1518546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518520#post1518520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... I'm already being boring with this subject, but I'll have to ask again: Are you sure it's not possible to create a Fan-made W5, like a W5.5 or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhj, I don't think wta is popular to create a pathfinder situation.<br /> <br /> That said I've no doubt story teller vault is going to have rules for fianna, uktena, wendigo, gof and stargazers shortly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:47:42-07:00","id":1518548,"title":"","content":"The thing that most annoys me the most about his refusal to listen to Sammbrano has to be the fact that Muammar seemed to think he knew better. To me, if you are discussing someone's cultural/lived experience, you should try to be humble enough to admit you don't know what it was like.<br /> <br /> Plus, the &quot;the name was fine in 2018&quot; ignores that the name was never fine, there just wasn't enough push to change it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:59:04-07:00","id":1518551,"title":"","content":"Please someone explain me cause I've been missing this all the time, what's wrong with Wendigo and Uktena tribe names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:23:54-07:00","id":1518557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518551#post1518551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please someone explain me cause I've been missing this all the time, what's wrong with Wendigo and Uktena tribe names?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, they are names that are not to be used lightly. ESPECIALLY the Younger Brother one. The creature it references is less like a deer+ghoul people depict it as and more like a completely evil spirit of greed. One which name is taboo.<br /> <br /> Older brother's creature is, as far as I know, just not a positive spirit to be used like that.<br /> <br /> PLEASE correct me if I get these wrong ^^''","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:14:31-07:00","id":1518562,"title":"","content":"Seriously I thought that it some kind of nonsense and name is just a name cause it's something borrowed from myths/legend/tales and put into fiction. But You know what? It convinced me and now I understand the issue. <br /> It is like naming a tribe Abbadon or Lucifer or something like that. It quite serious, maby more then I it looks like. I was listening to one man who run the black metal festivals and similar stuff who (after bad things) returned to the church and his tale about demonic names used by bands and yelled by masses during concerts was quite scary and convincing too. It is both- Wendigo and his tale- the same problem but in different religions.<br /> Heavy s..t.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:46:33-07:00","id":1518566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518491#post1518491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A awkward read but very interesting i almost wish i had a pen to circle the key points, this largely confirms some of my suspicions about wiping ethnicity from the tribes and why. What does surprise me was the plan just to kill off Wendigo which is outright dumb on a number of levels.<br /> <br /> Its also slightly alarming that the khelil was oblivious to get history especially with such a sensitive subject and when corrected on it he simply powered on with &quot;all get are nazis anyway.&quot; This guy outright shouldn't be writting the setting if true.<br /> <br /> <br /> The insensitivity on the subject of First nation people is also surprising as I recall he's previously accused other people if bigotry towards his own background so I'd presumed he'd be more sensitive about this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it reminds me of how some of the most homophobic people have been exposed to be gay themselves or are heavily suspected to be gay. And I have encountered here in Canada over the years people who are of a minority group who are themselves quite bigoted towards certain other minority groups, primarily the LGBTQ and Indigenous communities. Some times even more than bigoted white people I've encountered. In high school I had a friend who's family was from the Philippines and his mother utterly HATED the First Nations and would say awful things about them. It apparently got really bad for him when he started dating a Metis girl.<br /> <br /> I've long since learned that just because a person is of a minority group doesn't mean they are sympathetic to other minority groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well it was an obvious lie, like the one about how having the get as an enemy tribe was a way of expanding antagonists (you can just make more tribes if you're rebooting.) </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. Back when they first revealed that and what the new Get were supposed to be, I pointed out how it would have made far more sense for them to have been not a single Tribe but a hardline movement within the Garou Nation that broke away from it and formed their own Tribe/Nation.<br /> <br /> And you know what, that could have been an interesting concept that would have filled a role separate from existing WtA antagonists. Hardline fanatics who believe that there's no more room for middle ground and that most extreme actions to protect Gaia are not just justified but <i>needed</i> would be an interesting foe for the Garou as they look around at the unending damage being done to the world by Man. And not just in fighting people that share your beliefs, albeit taken to the extreme, but with the more subtle whisper of 'What if they are right? The world is dying. Can we afford to be wrong?'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518528#post1518528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering one of if not the first Hunter: The Reckoning STV releases was bringing back the Imbued, I would think it\u2019s a possibility for a Fan-made W5 book to be done, if not there certainly Dark Pack (free) is an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the V5 Kindred of the East STV book that came out a few months ago. So yeah, people could do it, they just have to use the mechanical framework of W5 which admittedly means one has to buy W5 but honestly if someone does create such a book and it's good, well-written book that fixes some problems with W5, I would be willing to bite the bullet and by the W5 PDF.\u200b Of course it wouldn't be as painful if Renegade was willing to do sales on DriveThruRPG like everyone else. Like as for as little interest I have H5 or the recent V5 books, I might have picked them up eventually on PDF if they were ever on sale but they're not and they're frankly outrageously overpriced, especially the V5 ones.<br /> <br /> Hell I wouldn't be surprised if here and other WOD/TTRPG forums following W5's release, sees threads about rewriting/reworking W5 which in turn eventually leads to the creation of such a book.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T15:11:19-07:00","id":1518573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518522#post1518522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would someone put the energy into rebuilding an edition when there are serviceable editions available?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason that a lot of people make fan material about pretty much anything, they don't like what's been done in sequels and invent to do something and in all cases if you think about it coldly it doesn't make sense to make any of that material, but they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T15:38:34-07:00","id":1518575,"title":"","content":"Oof, that was a rough read. Glad I already decided to skip W5. Sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T17:19:32-07:00","id":1518584,"title":"","content":"Well, this seals it, I am definitely not going to be entertaining 5th edition ever again. As long as the World of Darkness remains in these kinds of hands, there's honestly no point to ever move on from 20th Anniversary. Ever.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T17:39:49-07:00","id":1518586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518516#post1518516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, nothing shows how poorly Karim Muammar knew the setting than the push for the FENRIR to be the right-wing tribe. Because there exists a tribe in the game that ISN'T as willing to push back bad leaders and in older editions had systematic requirement FOR purity of bloodline.<br /> <br /> On top of that, Silver Fangs would fit the modern intellectual Right-Winger stereotype better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, there's a lot about monarchists I wish I could say, but where I live making the primary antagonists the Silver Fangs would feel too much like playing mundane republicans (that's 'we should become a republic' not 'the more right wing party'). To me the Get being antagonists makes the game different because there's this new(ish) BNP-like group whereas the Silver Fangs being villains is all 'yeah, nobles are bad, down with the aristocracy, hey when are we going to do stuff we aren't doing in real life'.<br /> <br /> Although considering the way W5 is going it probably should have been the Silver Fangs anyway.<br /> <br /> More seriously it should have been something closer to a multi-Tribe Camp than a single Tribe falling. Have the Get, the strongest of the strong, have to deal with the fact that they e fallen to the bottom because they're seen as starting all this? (Did they? It doesn't matter, we can stack the Garou Nationalist Camp leadership to pin the blame, but they're probably not solely to bland.)<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of all this, yeah I was still a bit on the fence because maybe the mechanics could have been houseruled into something that works, but after the Shapeshifting rules and all this I think it's time to stop waiting for the reviews and start investing in CofD and Scion again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T17:51:00-07:00","id":1518588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518573#post1518573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the same reason that a lot of people make fan material about pretty much anything, they don't like what's been done in sequels and invent to do something and in all cases if you think about it coldly it doesn't make sense to make any of that material, but they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you put in your energy and time to fix something someone else broke, and then you get to share any money you'd make from that with the people who broke it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T18:15:23-07:00","id":1518590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518526#post1518526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see you capitalized the words \u201cNative Americans\u201d there. There could be a number of reasons you correctly did that. You could have done it because you understand the cultural significance behind capitalization of the words, you could be following basic rules you were taught in school regarding the English language, etc.<br /> <br /> Karim didn\u2019t. There\u2019s a screenshot of it. Now I\u2019m going on the premise that he isn\u2019t horrible at his job as Editor In-Chief and is aware of how to properly use the English language. It could have been a mistake, but writing out the word \u201camerican\u201d in lower case is going to autocorrect to capitalized on any mobile device and on a computer if you type the word in lower case you\u2019re getting a red squiggly line below the word telling you it should be capitalized.<br /> <br /> With that being said, it\u2019s difficult to look at his use of lower case as anything but a deliberate attempt to minimize Native American folks. Micro aggressions like that, especially when directed to an Indigenous person, seems like abusive behavior to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would slightly disagree with the last sentence; a microaggression is something that is supposed to fly under the radar as it is objectionable only in a particular context. The fairly explicit dismissiveness to Native Americans, and why they might have particular viewpoints on parts of <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i>, is a pretty explicit aggression. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T18:25:23-07:00","id":1518592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically in part they went okay let's take a camp that was killed off in an edition almost thirty ago...then make all the Get like that and one of the big villains of the new setting. On top of killing off the aboriginal American representation and this is the group that is &quot;saving&quot; WtA? Jesus bloody Christ. That is insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's especially frustrating IMO because of what it signals. The Get of Fenris cleaned house editions ago. They took a hugely awful but numerically small camp within their Tribe, and they dealt with it themselves. Karim saying that white supremacist faction, that they <i>got rid of</i> was actually the entire identity of the Get of Fenris Tribe as a whole, is such a terrible takeaway. Like, &quot;Don't bother trying to root out the rot in your community, it doesn't matter, it's not worth the effort and energy, you'll just all be painted like the very infection you purged&quot;? The Get actually <i>did the right thing, and did it successfully, </i>which is a decently rare story in World of Darkness and amongst the Tribes. They didn't dig in their heels, they just took a break from stealing other people's Caerns to do some excellent work being responsible for their own problems, in their own house. That was strong, wonderful signaling. (I still think they should have also changed the Tribe Glyph in the process, but still.) The signaling with this lead direction reeks of white guilt, and burying problems rather than confronting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T18:35:21-07:00","id":1518594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518562#post1518562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously I thought that it some kind of nonsense and name is just a name cause it's something borrowed from myths/legend/tales and put into fiction. But You know what? It convinced me and now I understand the issue.<br /> It is like naming a tribe Abbadon or Lucifer or something like that. It quite serious, maby more then I it looks like. I was listening to one man who run the black metal festivals and similar stuff who (after bad things) returned to the church and his tale about demonic names used by bands and yelled by masses during concerts was quite scary and convincing too. It is both- Wendigo and his tale- the same problem but in different religions.<br /> Heavy s..t.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reality is that the use of the word &quot;Wendigo&quot; is quite complex, and the objection is fairly specific to circumstances. One of the running issues is that roleplaying games have borrowed from literature and mythology in a fairly decontextualised manner since the first edition of <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> in the 1970s. The way in which this occurs is now so ingrained within gaming, and has spread out from tabletop games to other areas, that most people never really think about it in much detail. However, the gaming use of literature and myth tends to rob monsters of their meaning (and even the term &quot;monster&quot; is quite significant; it has an origin in the word &quot;monstrum&quot; and is supposed to denote that the appearance of an unnatural creature is a portent, a sign of divine displeasure or the fact that something has gone wrong in the world), so they end up being window dressing for a mechanical challenge, a set of stats which define an encounter and ultimately how much loot, in gold and experience, one gains within the game. <br /> <br /> Quite a bit of this comes from an American, middle-class view of the world, in which culture is something which exists for no reason other than consumption, and myths are something which it is fair game to adapt in any suitable or convenient way, because no-one really believes in them, right? The problem is that one may not actually believe in the real existence of the wendigo (or basiliks, or rakshasas or whatever) but still have a deep-seated attachment to this as part of one's culture. Thus, seeing a term used lightly, or inappropriately, or whatever can end up being offensive. Thus, for a Native American to see the word &quot;wendigo&quot; being applied to the name of a Werewolf tribe is less a respectful use of Native American culture, than a white American deciding &quot;cool name, bro!&quot; Could &quot;wendigo&quot; be used reasonably and respectfully within a game? I think so, but, given that there are Native Americans within the conversation, maybe it's a good idea to ask them?<br /> <br /> (It's worth noting that I find some of the use of European folklore in roleplaying games offensive for exactly the reasons outlined above. An example that very readily springs to mind is the black dog, which features in the Onyx path published <i>Dark Ages Companion</i> from 2017. The black dog is an interesting bit of folklore; in medieval, and into early modern times, it existed in British folklore as a stand-in for the Devil. Post the Reformation, the black dog starts to shift into a more generic sign of menace. The most common legend goes that seeing a spectral black dog means that a close relative will die within the next year. It is a monster in the original sense of the word, an unnatural portent, signifier of an unstoppable event which the observer is powerless to prevent. The <i>Dark Ages Companion</i> turns it into a monster in the <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons </i>sense. It has no cultural meaning, and is something that will go away if you hit it enough times with a sword.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T23:57:34-07:00","id":1518614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518586#post1518586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, there's a lot about monarchists I wish I could say, but where I live making the primary antagonists the Silver Fangs would feel too much like playing mundane republicans (that's 'we should become a republic' not 'the more right wing party'). To me the Get being antagonists makes the game different because there's this new(ish) BNP-like group whereas the Silver Fangs being villains is all 'yeah, nobles are bad, down with the aristocracy, hey when are we going to do stuff we aren't doing in real life'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly focusing on the way the tribe functions and how it HASN'T cleaned house and still requires 3 purebreed (out of 5 total dots!) to join in.<br /> <br /> Basically, if I were to look for a group that I'd peg as Right Wing, Fangs would be higher on the list than Fenrir. Because Fenrir at least have methods of taking out a bad leader.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that a multi-tribal group would be a better option in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518592#post1518592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The signaling with this lead direction reeks of white guilt, and burying problems rather than confronting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why googling is important because I was wondering on the amount of white guilt in Muammar's suggestions. Then I googled what he looked like and though he most likely is just white-passing, dude LOOKS very white.<br /> <br /> But I feel this is something of a trap that is easy to fall into even if you try to be open-minded. It is easy to erase the problematic factions over addressing them. Or deny any Striders/Stargazers/Gale Stalkers/Ghost Council/etc. because of expected racism.<br /> <br /> I myself do not feel comfortable using either Native American tribe in my chronicles, but I do see how it is burying the issue over addressing it.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T01:44:05-07:00","id":1518618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically in part they went okay let's take a camp that was killed off in an edition almost thirty ago...then make all the Get like that and one of the big villains of the new setting. On top of killing off the aboriginal American representation and this is the group that is &quot;saving&quot; WtA? Jesus bloody Christ. That is insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theirs a lot of bad faith guys in the community who embellish and keep the idea going. The actual big divide genrallly is between people who want go wipe the tribe of ethnic backgrounds and those who want ethnicity done better. Their are outliers with more dramatic outlooks such as people who arnt open to any lore changes but more genrally you'll see people who openly state the entire get were litteral nazis/fascists from top to bottom from day one amoung other out of touch statements. For example I remember a guy on w5 Discord who said everyone who liked previous editions of werewolf were ultimately bigots. Or a guy I saw who claimed anyone who liked the get was an irk nazi (although his definition of nazi was so vague 99% of humanity counts)<br /> <br /> Now these sort of guys don't really represent concensus but theyre very loud and hard/unpleasent to argue against if you're a left winger or moderate so saturate the culture with the idea. Ensuring a minor plot point dominates dialogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2023, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T02:09:35-07:00","id":1518619,"title":"","content":"The Get-thing is weird because there KM is of the opinion that not having them be a white supremacist fantasy would rob them of their identity and yet with the Native American Tribes his take was that tying them to localized cultures is too much of a hassle and therefore should be removed. Especially once you're at the point where you're actively scrutinizing the writing for signs of Native American representation in order to remove them, you should wonder where you've taken a wrong turn in the development. This should've been a moment to cause some serious self-reflection.<br /> <br /> Also, this discrepancy is even still in this version. After all, with this version the names of the Native American Tribes has been changed, the cultural ties to human culture have been removed (including with the Fianna after some backlash)... BUT what is one of the central new concepts of W5 called...? Hauglosk... a Norwegian word. And who's most representative of Hauglosk...? The Get Of Fenris. So the white supremacist Norse Nazi identity of Get was protected and preserved while with everything else it was &quot;Let's go full steam ahead with erasure!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another issue with Hauglosk I have there is the idea of Hauglosk being this phenomenon that turned the Get into these Nazis as it emphasized all the worst qualities of the Garou Nation. Now James Sambrano's post is focused on thereby pushing people who still want to try playing Get of Fenris (out of nostalgia for their past characters) into associating themselves with what is now essentially a bunch of Nazis. A different problem I see here is Hauglosk. In W5 every PC can suffer from Hauglosk. So if you have an entire faction that tells you that being affected by Hauglosk might lead to things like thinking Nazis are cool, then you're indirectly telling players that one valid way to portray Hauglosk with their characters is to act like a Nazi/white supremacist. Like, the idea is this &quot;extreme urgency&quot; of Hauglosk can be expressed by engaging in extremely reactionary political stances like believing in white supremacy. And in my opinion that's a huge issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T02:35:32-07:00","id":1518621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518619#post1518619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get-thing is weird because there KM is of the opinion that not having them be a white supremacist fantasy would rob them of their identity and yet with the Native American Tribes his take was that tying them to localized cultures is too much of a hassle and therefore should be removed. Especially once you're at the point where you're actively scrutinizing the writing for signs of Native American representation in order to remove them, you should wonder where you've taken a wrong turn in the development. This should've been a moment to cause some serious reflection .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theirs a tendancy in modern fiction to be blind to western coding of groups while being very mindful of how other groups are presented. This is particularly true in 5th wod were non germanic european groups have effectively had their identity wiped but the designers are oblivious to how other groups are coded, you can see this in the ventrue for example who draw very very heavily on European ideas on prestige and power or the Tremere who draw on our ideas of what a mystic is and isn't. In contrast to say the formally coptic setites who now draw more generic cults in western pop culture as the ministry so effectively the Egyptian/coptic clan is gone and replaced with a white one.<br /> <br /> It ultimatly works on the problem that the groups we see as univeral are often coded quite strongly but we don't see it because it's our culture.<br /> <br /> this seems to apply to w5 were euro centric nazi get remain wereas first nation groups are purged. The blind spot is probably one of the more extreme examples. I suspect we'll see it more subtly with the silver fangs and shadow lords where the slavic nature of these tribes will be accidently replaced by western because its incorrectly as more generic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2023, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T08:56:53-07:00","id":1518640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518618#post1518618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theirs a lot of bad faith guys in the community who embellish and keep the idea going. The actual big divide genrallly is between people who want go wipe the tribe of ethnic backgrounds and those who want ethnicity done better. Their are outliers with more dramatic outlooks such as people who arnt open to any lore changes but more genrally you'll see people who openly state the entire get were litteral nazis/fascists from top to bottom from day one amoung other out of touch statements. For example I remember a guy on w5 Discord who said everyone who liked previous editions of werewolf were ultimately bigots. Or a guy I saw who claimed anyone who liked the get was an irk nazi (although his definition of nazi was so vague 99% of humanity counts)<br /> <br /> Now these sort of guys don't really represent concensus but theyre very loud and hard/unpleasent to argue against if you're a left winger or moderate so saturate the culture with the idea. Ensuring a minor plot point dominates dialogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main issue is that a number of folks that hold said opinions are official WoD Discord Mods and their opinions are not challenged by any other official voices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T08:59:48-07:00","id":1518641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518619#post1518619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another issue with Hauglosk I have there is the idea of Hauglosk being this phenomenon that turned the Get into these Nazis as it emphasized all the worst qualities of the Garou Nation. Now James Sambrano's post is focused on thereby pushing people who still want to try playing Get of Fenris (out of nostalgia for their past characters) into associating themselves with what is now essentially a bunch of Nazis. A different problem I see here is Hauglosk. In W5 every PC can suffer from Hauglosk. So if you have an entire faction that tells you that being affected by Hauglosk might lead to things like thinking Nazis are cool, then you're indirectly telling players that one valid way to portray Hauglosk with their characters is to act like a Nazi/white supremacist. Like, the idea is this &quot;extreme urgency&quot; of Hauglosk can be expressed by engaging in extremely reactionary political stances like believing in white supremacy. And in my opinion that's a huge issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its interesting.....being extremely urgent and willing to push the envelope in order to save the planet=Nazi is not a mental leap I ever would have made but apparently its one that Paradox did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T10:31:58-07:00","id":1518645,"title":"","content":"Eco-fash is a thing, but with execution here it's still a load of mental gymnastics that would be very impressive in the Olympics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T10:52:15-07:00","id":1518647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518645#post1518645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eco-fash is a thing, but with execution here it's still a load of mental gymnastics that would be very impressive in the Olympics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm just more used to the Fash emblems being on the counter-protesters trying to kick my head in at environmental rallies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T11:10:54-07:00","id":1518650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518645#post1518645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eco-fash is a thing, but with execution here it's still a load of mental gymnastics that would be very impressive in the Olympics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had the same thought. Eco-fascism would be an updated idea of what rightwing-radicalization could look like in the Garou-Nation in the face of the Apocalypse. Although there we're broadly talking about fascism in the context of climate change (and its consequences). And what Karim said in those posts we saw... That just seems more like the old-school-idea of WWII-era Nazism and somehow an entire Tribe has now signed up for that set of beliefs (somehow...).<br /> <br /> Another reason why turning the Get into fascists doesn't really work, though, is the Wyrm. The bad guy of WtA is the Wyrm which is this abstract spiritual entity that is an expression of the state of the world but also influences things in the material world. But this setup with Hauglosk and GoF-Garou as Nazis you're simply setting up a super uncomfortable question for this setting: What is worse - a BSD-Garou who serves the Wyrm or a GoF-Garou who wants to kill the Wyrm but is a Nazi...? And with the Get being secondary antagonists like hunter-orgs in H5 are, they're set up as secondary antagonists. The setup isn't &quot;The situation is bad and complicated but with some effort, we can make this work!&quot;, it's just yet another faction that wants to do the same thing the PCs want to do but they're doing it wrong which means that you shouldn't work with them (let alone allow anybody to play them at the table, of course, because that would be badwrongfun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T12:35:20-07:00","id":1518656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518640#post1518640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main issue is that a number of folks that hold said opinions are official WoD Discord Mods and their opinions are not challenged by any other official voices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yean I anticipated at much from the posts over their. Its why im aware the concensus over their should be taken with a pinch of salt. I tend to strongly frown on mods whose politics and beliefs shape their modding (even when it's my own), they don't even benifit from it since you loose all sense of perspective and look like a smug idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2023, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T15:37:09-07:00","id":1518665,"title":"","content":"Ouch Sambrano got lambasted on the official discord for having ulterior motives and how come he didn't report this in 2021.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T18:35:48-07:00","id":1518672,"title":"","content":"Demands for perfection from a victim, and would probably still blame them even if those criteria were met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T18:49:29-07:00","id":1518673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518665#post1518665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ouch Sambrano got lambasted on the official discord for having ulterior motives and how come he didn't report this in 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are completely blind to what contractual obligations mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T20:12:23-07:00","id":1518676,"title":"","content":"The official Paradox run Discord is also a place that concentrates individuals that feel like they need to defend Paradox reflexively because they like the WoD5 material in general and it's easier to attack Sambrano than to confront that a game you like was built on bad behavior. Something we've seen in past incidents. Discord servers are inherently drivers of echo chambers because Discord was designed around being a way to chat with your teammates while playing multiplayer video games; not being a broader type of social media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:54:50-07:00","id":1518685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518673#post1518673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People are completely blind to what contractual obligations mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and just general good manners. Sambrano said in their post that he had hoped to wait until W5 was released, but the situation with WoD5 was too much to stay quiet.<br /> <br /> Even if the project sucked, you don't want to throw the people you worked with under the bus, yanno.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T01:43:21-07:00","id":1518689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518676#post1518676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official Paradox run Discord is also a place that concentrates individuals that feel like they need to defend Paradox reflexively because they like the WoD5 material in general and it's easier to attack Sambrano than to confront that a game you like was built on bad behavior. Something we've seen in past incidents. Discord servers are inherently drivers of echo chambers because Discord was designed around being a way to chat with your teammates while playing multiplayer video games; not being a broader type of social media.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what a I recall they didn't even like constructive feedback on mechanics to the point basic math is unacceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T02:53:41-07:00","id":1518690,"title":"","content":"There's also the bigger issue of crediting the writers from the Hunter Entertainment version. The reason Sambrano came forward this year was because of the strange circumstances surrounding this second iteration. Previously, it seems like Paradox had just unceremoniously pulled the plug on the first iteration of W5 as they restructured the development-process by having an in-house team develop the core-books. I assumed this meant development for W5 had restarted from 0 (and it's not like anybody who developed this second iteration explained how the first iteration has been used as a basis for development here). But as the previews started coming out last October Sambrano realized that this second iteration was borrowing stuff from the first iteration. Now that we know more about Sambrano's time with the Hunter Entertainment version, it's clear how he could've realized that. And since this second iteration has been developed on the foundation of the first one which had all sorts of bad vibes he came forward in exposing what was going on behind the scenes back then.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we're going to get any official response to this... With the art-debacle, they apologized for using Tame Iti's face and then when it turned out that there was even more art in the previews that turned out to be questionable tracings of photos, they simply said that they're gonna look into it... and since then we have heard nothing from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T03:37:47-07:00","id":1518691,"title":"","content":"Ethan Skemp, former developer of WtA over on rpg.net-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't find a lot to say about this beyond my utter sympathy for and support of J. F. Sambrano. Thank you so much for sharing this. It was a painful and sobering read, but so necessary.<br /> <br /> I acknowledge that we fucked up a lot in our time shepherding the line back in the '90s and aughts. Sometimes we recognized those fuckups and tried to do better. Not often enough, I'll admit. I feel sorrow for not doing more at the time, and I apologize for my portion of that general well-meaning but frequently painful cluelessness and failure to do sufficient amounts of legwork.<br /> <br /> That said, it's horrible to see the desire to do right by people <i>not</i> being part the vision of some of the people in control of this game. The splatterpunk edgelord portion of Werewolf's DNA is undeniable. It's just gross when somebody decides that it's the <i>skeleton </i>of the game, and should be prioritized over respect and decency for its actual players. </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T03:53:34-07:00","id":1518692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518691#post1518691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ethan Skemp, former developer of WtA over on rpg.net-<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always found Mr. Skemp to be a great guy. This is a good response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T08:35:11-07:00","id":1518704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518665#post1518665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ouch Sambrano got lambasted on the official discord for having ulterior motives and how come he didn't report this in 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, apparently they're really going for the character-assassination-angle here - and worse than that, they're making shit up to support those claims. Not only that but seemingly Mods are doing it even. Someone on Reddit talked about two false claims that are making the rounds now: One is about JS supposedly having repeatedly gone to the Discord Server solely to shit on W5. And the other is that he only recently even joined the Discord server in order to complain about W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T11:00:38-07:00","id":1518714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518704#post1518704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, apparently they're really going for the character-assassination-angle here - and worse than that, they're making shit up to support those claims. Not only that but seemingly Mods are doing it even. Someone on Reddit talked about two false claims that are making the rounds now: One is about JS supposedly having repeatedly gone to the Discord Server solely to shit on W5. And the other is that he only recently even joined the Discord server in order to complain about W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah followed that one.....luckily they use pretty much the exact same phrasing on both reddit and Discord so their pretty easy to pick out and debunk....though looks like they had a tanty and taken their bat and ball home on the sub. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 07-27-2023, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T18:08:37-07:00","id":1518861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518640#post1518640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main issue is that a number of folks that hold said opinions are official WoD Discord Mods and their opinions are not challenged by any other official voices.</div> </div> </div> </div>one of the opinions I keep seeing there (and other places) is that Sambrano got what he deserved for being so antagonistic to the idea that they should erase all of the cultural ties of the Garou. <br /> <br /> But he pointed something out here and I am wondering why this has not come up at all in those discussions defending how right Paradox is to do this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1684315669561593856?s=46&amp;t=Hqf2FEGoDHMRrhwFmVerZw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1684315669561593856?s=46&amp;t=Hqf2FEGoDHMRrhwFmVerZw\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1684315669561593856?s=46&amp;t=Hqf2FEGoDHMRrhwFmVerZw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1684315669561593856?s=46&amp;t=Hqf2FEGoDHMRrhwFmVerZw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27995-last-apple-blossom","name":"Last Apple Blossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T23:48:16-07:00","id":1518876,"title":"","content":"James Sambrano made another <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition-and-the-anti-indigeneity-in-the-gaming-industry.912221/page-12#post-24885725\" target=\"_blank\">post</a> giving some more detail on the early development-direction of the first version of W5:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been debating getting into the discussion here, although I have been reading what everyone has had to say. My original thought was that it would be best to present my story and evidence and let the community come to their own conclusions.<br /> <br /> But there's two things I'd really like to say and the first one is to thank everyone who came in here to show me support and sympathy. I am touched by every last one of you but I need to make a special note that I'm touched by Ethan because of how much time, energy, and love I know he's put into this broad work.<br /> <br /> It means a lot to me that even though I do have criticisms of the original material that you are still supportive. Thank you. I wouldn't even have had the opportunity to attempt to improve it if not for what was already done (and a lot was positive!)<br /> <br /> The other thing I wanted to do was clear up a couple of misconceptions. There seems to be this idea from the outset that the plan was to write a culturally clean W5 and that is not entirely the case. That became a firm decision after the game was moved in-house but when it came to us, in some cases we were given the opportunity to suggest alternatives.<br /> <br /> For example, Winter's Teeth (as I had written them) went through a total of five revisions. The first one was the proposed genocide. When we resisted that I pitched three alternatives. One of those alternatives was a version where in the Apocalypse, Turtle had reawakened (as was prophesied) and subsumed Younger Brother's Rage. The Tribe shifted toward taking on both theirs and Middle Brother's responsibilities. It was an answer to &quot;what major change does this Tribe go through because Gaia is dead&quot;<br /> <br /> There were two other versions and none of them were only Native American. There was then the final version I wrote but didn't submit before we were let go.<br /> <br /> I had been given flat approval for Older Brother to retain its Indigenous history.<br /> <br /> So it's simply not the case that this version was entirely culturally agnostic.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that turning the Fenrir as a whole into the Sword of Heimdall flies in the face of the supposition that it was.<br /> <br /> The truth is that the suggestion was that the Tribes should be less focused on &quot;human politics&quot; (they also mandated that the Furies would no longer ascribe to feminism) but the Fenrir being all Sword of Heimdall (and as you've seen in his own words, taking that away would rob of them of their heritage) was a push to remain connected to human culture.<br /> <br /> He only wanted to remove things like Indigeneity and feminism. But he wanted to keep white supremacy and Nazis.<br /> <br /> That's the issue. That's how white supremacists normalize white supremacy.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T00:08:58-07:00","id":1518879,"title":"","content":"Aw, Turtle waking up to a post-apocalyptic shitshow would have had so much potential for upheaval.<br /> <br /> I think my head-canon for the Get will be that the purge of the SoH created an ideological rift that teeters the edge of civil war within the Tribe; nothing says Werewolf politics like missing the point completely and sabotaging themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T00:29:54-07:00","id":1518882,"title":"","content":"And this reveals again another weird way Karim Muammar dealt with the Tribes. The focus on womanhood/feminism of the Black Furies was removed in order to make the Tribes less about &quot;human politics&quot;. And yet, he wanted the whole Tribe of the Get to be Nazis/white supremacists...<br /> <br /> The reawakening of Turtle would also work already well because it would be a change connected to the mid-Apocalypse/Gaia is dead/dying-setting. We've seen three Tribe-sections in the previews and none of them have anything that directly spells out how the Apocalypse/fall of the Garou-Nation has impacted those Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T01:45:37-07:00","id":1518888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James Sambrano</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth is that the suggestion was that the Tribes should be less focused on &quot;human politics&quot; (they also mandated that the Furies would no longer ascribe to feminism) but the Fenrir being all Sword of Heimdall (and as you've seen in his own words, taking that away would rob of them of their heritage) was a push to remain connected to human culture.<br /> <br /> He only wanted to remove things like Indigeneity and feminism. But he wanted to keep white supremacy and Nazis.<br /> <br /> That's the issue. That's how white supremacists normalize white supremacy.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus <i>tapdancing</i> <i><b>Christ</b></i>.<br /> <br /> See, this is something that really makes me uncomfortable about ParaWolf. They focus on the worst stuff in a game ALREADY about dark things, as if the setting in itself lacks it. That V5 playtest, that genocide oops and now this. Have these people read the source material at all?<br /> <br /> Though I think JS is missing one thing; Muammar clearly wanted the Fenrir to become strawwolves that could be easily defeated and so 'address' the rise of the alt.right. Given Muammar's profile is p\u00e5 svenska, I get the feeling he is drawing from his own experiences with Swedish racism and right wingers. Which is fair, but it isn't ALL there is to us Nordic people.<br /> <br /> And still, the removal of Black Fury feminism is...baffling. Just cut the tribe if that bothers you so much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 07-27-2023, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T02:31:24-07:00","id":1518893,"title":"","content":"See, this is something that really makes me uncomfortable about ParaWolf. They focus on the worst stuff in a game ALREADY about dark things, as if the setting in itself lacks it. That V5 playtest, that genocide oops and now this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T02:33:16-07:00","id":1518894,"title":"","content":"Slightly odd he wants the nazi stuff in their and have it subsume get identity. I really do think a lot of these writters are trying to work through anxiety with the surge in right wing voices counterculture and surge in far right politics.<br /> <br /> Sadly catharsis is bull and doomerism is juvenile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-27-2023, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T02:56:36-07:00","id":1518899,"title":"","content":"So. I wasn't sure about posting this here, because I felt it might be too inflammatory, but after the way people have just dismissed Mr. Sambrano just a while ago, I feel I need to show this to someone sensible. These are the screenshots from the WoD discord over the past few days including people, mods and Mr. Sambrano himself.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"798\" height=\"259\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe</a> -&gt; For the full discussions<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T03:12:04-07:00","id":1518903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518899#post1518899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. I wasn't sure about posting this here, because I felt it might be too inflammatory, but after the way people have just dismissed Mr. Sambrano just a while ago, I feel I need to show this to someone sensible. These are the screenshots from the WoD discord over the past few days including people, mods and Mr. Sambrano himself.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"798\" height=\"259\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe</a> -&gt; For the full discussions<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it takes a certain kind of entitled white dude ( check profile pics of most of the commenters) to call an indigenous bloke who has both professionally and personally gone to bat over and over again for Womens, LGBTQ+ and Disadvantaged Peoples rights ' hateful and bigoted'.<br /> <br /> Paradox needs to clean house over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T03:25:23-07:00","id":1518905,"title":"","content":"Its interesting that these internal disputes are framed in context of socially concious framework-&quot;your side are the bigots&quot;. I recall the zack sabbath shit flinging saga was the same and khelil accused Dawkins of racism In response to his accusations<br /> it ads an extra layer of obfuscation considering everyone involved is so 'woke' they could be riding a sandworm to work while mumbling about the spice. Meaning you not only have to discern who is correct but are also having to 2nd guess peoples sincerity on socially concious issues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-27-2023, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T03:55:31-07:00","id":1518912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518899#post1518899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. I wasn't sure about posting this here, because I felt it might be too inflammatory, but after the way people have just dismissed Mr. Sambrano just a while ago, I feel I need to show this to someone sensible. These are the screenshots from the WoD discord over the past few days including people, mods and Mr. Sambrano himself.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"798\" height=\"259\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cMXLfUg.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/a/hZW46Qe</a> -&gt; For the full discussions<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Man, what a depressing read... Those texts really bear all the hallmarks of victim-blaming, don't they? Saying that James Sambrano has released his statements the wrong way (&quot;why not in 2021?&quot;, &quot;why before the release of the book?&quot;). That he's guilty by association (&quot;you talked to a person who's friends with someone else who says mean stuff to WOD-staff.&quot;). That he must have done something bad as well for Karim Muammar to have acted this way (&quot;I need to see both sides before I buy into this narrative&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:18:28-07:00","id":1518919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518665#post1518665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ouch Sambrano got lambasted on the official discord for having ulterior motives and how come he didn't report this in 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, there were bans over the whole situation.<br /> <br /> Tbh this whole affair has absolutely soured me on new books from Paradox. There's already a massive section of their video game Fandom that's racist as hell (with reports of people being banned from groups for being nonwhite, the whole Deus Vult affair, a streamer being harassed nonstop for having a non-white ex girlfriend).<br /> <br /> Seeing how the whole situation has been handled just.... yeah. I'm fine with W20 and Revised. I don't want to pay this company if this is how they treat people.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone defended Sambrano in the discord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T10:48:47-07:00","id":1518941,"title":"","content":"Well that's a tough read, having to work really hard to read it considering it begins with accusations of conspiracy and then immediately moves on to wildly inaccurate claims (I think someone says JS wanted to keep the W-word as the Tribe name?).<br /> <br /> Like JS has definitely caused W5 to lose sales, one of my favourite RPGs is no longer on my list (I was going to give it a look on January after the dust had settled and I had RPG budget not already allocated). But none of the sales he's caused Paradox to lose are people incredibly excited about the game, and any cancelled pre orders are most likely from people who were buying in full knowledge they'd complain about it on their forum of choice. It's also possible that, as much as people on the WoD discord like W5, it might just not have sold well anyway (most of my friends are in their 20s and play TTRPGs, I'm the only one who knows anything about it. I've had to explain it to some who does have basic familiarity with <i>Exalted</i>).<br /> <br /> <br /> But really what was nice to read was JS's second post on early W5 development. His previous post could have been read as him not toeing the official brief*, now I have the context to understand the entire Winter's Teeth debarkle and how it seems to be an active attempt to avoid the game being 'too woke'. Which I honestly suspect is at least partially lacking the life experience that makes this obvious (being white and male presenting).<br /> <br /> I'm also amused as I had a brief exchange on another forum yesterday about the latest CofD book's disability representation and my personal love of the Cephalist picture.<br /> <br /> * As a separate thing to the more clear issues, such as Karim insisting that proper nouns shouldn't get their capital letters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T11:30:22-07:00","id":1518945,"title":"","content":"Something I want to note since I am a Nordic person and news from Sweden does trickle here as well.<br /> <br /> It is entirely possible that KM's push to have Fenrir as SoH has to do with his own experiences with racism and alt-right in Sweden. Things are not exactly great there in terms of racial relationships, especially in Stockholm where his Linkedin says he currently is.<br /> <br /> This does not justify the way he pushed for all Fenrir to be SoH-like, but given this <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/BavmMZQ.png\" target=\"_blank\">screenshot</a> I get the feeling KM is coming from a very different context than JS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T12:00:32-07:00","id":1518949,"title":"","content":"Honestly just straight up bringing the SoH back wouldn't have been the worst move, especially as there's also a strong argument to be made about the Get and toxic masculinity. It would also be worth going through all of the Tribes and explicitly detailing how some members go too far (such as Silver Fangs who demand power instead of earning it, techno-fetishist GWs, Black Fury Misandry, and so on). Let the Tribes be a diverse spectrum, and let there be Get who live up to everything the Tribe should be as well as those who live down to everything that's expected of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:05:51-07:00","id":1518959,"title":"","content":"Nah, the Swords were always a bad thing to have around. If you want Camps in the Get to represent them at their worst, there's still Mjolnir's Thunder which takes their militant views of strength to a maximal degree without the inherent racism; they simply live to kill, and kill to live to see another day of killing. Mjolnir's Thunder was already what W5 is making the Get into as a whole. Plus you have The Glorious Fist of Wotan who want to genocide humanity as humans are a cancer spreading the Wyrm and Weaver and the only cure left it excision.<br /> <br /> I mean, by Revised and 20th, WtA has a pretty decent amount of information on the diversity of individuals within each Tribe regarding how they live up to their Tribal ideals, the Garou's larger ideals, and how it stacks up to our human ideals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:23:27-07:00","id":1518960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518949#post1518949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly just straight up bringing the SoH back wouldn't have been the worst move, especially as there's also a strong argument to be made about the Get and toxic masculinity. It would also be worth going through all of the Tribes and explicitly detailing how some members go too far (such as Silver Fangs who demand power instead of earning it, techno-fetishist GWs, Black Fury Misandry, and so on). Let the Tribes be a diverse spectrum, and let there be Get who live up to everything the Tribe should be as well as those who live down to everything that's expected of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are they going to recruit from? They're an exclusionary camp in an exclusionary Tribe. They won't take in women or lupus, in addition to insisting that anyone who lines up be as white as possible. Going off of Revised, they've also been living in some pretty deep shadows for an entire generation, and probably losing numbers to simple attrition. They're also not likely to like Fenris on account of how the rest of the tribe that follows him killed almost all of them, so a new source of recruits is highly questionable and also largely out of their reach. And if anyone suspects that leftover Swords are around, they're likely to gather up a temporary pack of other Fenrir to go and kill the Nazis so that, if anyone does find out about the Swords, they can continue to hold their heads high and declare with simply truth, &quot;We killed all the Nazis who thought that they could hide in our tribe.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:35:56-07:00","id":1518963,"title":"","content":"I am happy to confirm I am not crazy. Looking at those images and reading those toxic comments make it blatanty obvious that the white knights defenders of x5 are in the wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T01:04:39-07:00","id":1518996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518941#post1518941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like JS has definitely caused W5 to lose sales, one of my favourite RPGs is no longer on my list (I was going to give it a look on January after the dust had settled and I had RPG budget not already allocated). But none of the sales he's caused Paradox to lose are people incredibly excited about the game, and any cancelled pre orders are most likely from people who were buying in full knowledge they'd complain about it on their forum of choice. It's also possible that, as much as people on the WoD discord like W5, it might just not have sold well anyway (most of my friends are in their 20s and play TTRPGs, I'm the only one who knows anything about it. I've had to explain it to some who does have basic familiarity with <i>Exalted</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they lost some sales due to JS but I think W5 has probably sold really well so far. The only thing is how the larger community will react once they have the book in their hands (or the pdf on their computer). Because I don't think the majority has followed the previews as closely as we have here on this forum. So I think for a large number of people getting the book will be the first time they hear of things like &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, &quot;Get are antagonist-only&quot;, &quot;The Native American Tribes have been renamed and lost their connection to human culture.&quot; etc. In terms of advertisement for W5, not a lot has happened over the last couple of months. Of course, this is due to things like Outstar having been on holiday during that time. She deserves to have a holiday but what's actually bizarre is that without her apparently things like the WOD-news-show simply don't happen. So Renegade kept dropping those preview-images on the product-page and at some point, the WOD-account even stopped tweeting about the weekly release of these preview-pages. Of course, this may have been due to them having to do a public apology at the start of the previews for the tracing of a photo from Tame Iti.<br /> <br /> But my point is that the discussions will take on a different tone once the book comes out as a lot of people will find out about things that we, here on the forum, have known about for months now.<br /> <br /> And we'll see whether I'm right or wrong on this pretty soon: The pre-order pdf of the W5 corebook comes out next Wednesday.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T04:12:39-07:00","id":1518999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518959#post1518959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, the Swords were always a bad thing to have around.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's value to having and interrogating these ideas in games, even if they're uncomfortable and appeal to people who hold those beliefs. There's many ways to handle bringing back the SoH from retconning their destruction to making them a remnant in hiding and dying out as they're unable to recruit new members.<br /> <br /> At best it would probably have been an okay move, but I honestly think it would have been better than 'Alall GoF are fascists' or 'the Get have all fallen to their Rage and are fighting the Get wrong'. Even better would have been a new multi-Tribe far right movement.<br /> <br /> As to the diversity of the Tribes yes there's a lot there, but as there's probably a significant number of people who do/will only buy the corebook it's important to make it clear there. Longer Tribe sections of 4+ pages with examples of the Tribe in different cultures and probably some kind of 'when we fail' section. <i>Especially</i> as W5 is throwing out a lot of the old lore and history in favour of more archetypal Tribes and can't rely on the cultural links that did the heavy lifting in earlier editions' corebook writeups.<br /> <br /> Like the GW aren't the most adaptable Tribe who have integrated themselves with humanity anymore (as made clear by them ditching Cockroach). They're now the werewolves who work the system if you're being generous, or the tech-fucker wolves if you're not. So I definitely could have made myself clearer, but I think the intent of that part of my post is valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T04:42:01-07:00","id":1519001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518999#post1518999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's value to having and interrogating these ideas in games, even if they're uncomfortable and appeal to people who hold those beliefs. There's many ways to handle bringing back the SoH from retconning their destruction to making them a remnant in hiding and dying out as they're unable to recruit new members.<br /> <br /> At best it would probably have been an okay move, but I honestly think it would have been better than 'Alall GoF are fascists' or 'the Get have all fallen to their Rage and are fighting the Get wrong'. Even better would have been a new multi-Tribe far right movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise this was done already? In W20 they restored the Swords, and he current witch hunts started with that when people started looking into that. Restoring the Swords led to nothing good for Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:02:45-07:00","id":1519009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519001#post1519001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise this was done already? In W20 they restored the Swords, and he current witch hunts started with that when people started looking into that. Restoring the Swords led to nothing good for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and you have to consider what environment you are publishing the book into. It is entirely different to publish a book discussing neo-nazi when there is not a huge surge of alt-right than when there is a huge surge of them. People are more open to shades of grey discussions when they don't have to actively think about the subject outside the game.<br /> <br /> This is why I feel KM's opinions are so tone-deaf, because SoH-Fenrir would not create discussions. It would just either make the tribe banned OR as JS warned, endorsing making a nazi character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:26:48-07:00","id":1519014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519001#post1519001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise this was done already? In W20 they restored the Swords, and he current witch hunts started with that when people started looking into that. Restoring the Swords led to nothing good for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know W20 brought them back and then didn't do anything with them. But at this point I think we have to accept that we have two different points of view on this coming from two different sets of life experiences and just agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> I will however agree that KM's propositions probably aren't the way of doing it. I'm just not overly fond of the idea of 'no you can't interrogate this idea, it might be dangerous'.<br /> <br /> Hell I'd argue a period of active fascism only makes the interrogation and deconstruction of fascism more important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:38:53-07:00","id":1519018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519014#post1519014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell I'd argue a period of active fascism only makes the interrogation and deconstruction of fascism more important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with you if the audience had the capacity to indulge in a creative interrogation of fascism and the challenges it presents instead of reactionary baying for blood. It's one of those &quot;This is why we cannot have nice things&quot;. Concept of nuance and reading comprehension are out of the door when you've only got tribalist shit flinging over an idea that fits into 180 characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:43:54-07:00","id":1519021,"title":"","content":"There's also the issue that you're not provoking discussions on the rise of extreme right-wing politics or making that a central theme of the game. The Get-Tribe is an <i>antagonist</i>-faction. It's unlikely your PCs are gonna sit down with them and have philosophical discussions. Now if this topic were something like... an extremist multi-tribal faction within the Garou-Nation then I could see how this topic could be brought into the game via Sept-politics as it ties to the question of the fate of the Garou-Nation.<br /> <br /> With the Get as antagonists and all of them being Nazis/white supremacists, all you're getting is that the setting of W5 has a faction of Nordic Nazi-werewolves you occasionally will fight against. And by also insisting that in this one instance, the cultural ties should be maintained, the concept projects an image of white blonde blue-eyed Nazis with Norse pagan symbols... If you present this to anybody who knows absolutely nothing about WtA, they will just see a really campy idea of an antagonist. After all, we're looking at them in the context of the old lore of the Get of Fenris and how the Swords of Heimdall were explained in the past. Anybody new to the game will just hear that one of the enemy-types you face in the game are Nazi-werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T14:12:19-07:00","id":1519048,"title":"","content":"OK, so lets make an important distinction: Mature gaming vs. &quot;mature&quot; gaming.<br /> <br /> Mature gaming is something I think we all want, or we wouldn't be here. Mature games are games that provide the space to discuss and interrogate heavy topics at the safety of the gaming table. The provide not just a setting where it makes sense for such topics to come up, but tools to guide players and groups into ensuring that this topics are handled with the care they deserve,and other people at the table will need to handle all these in a productive and very importantly fun fashion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mature&quot; gaming is where games include material that mainstream society deem inappropriate for younger audiences to be able to explore in a healthy fashion: sex, drug abuse, violence, etc. This is the same thing as a movie getting rated R/16+ (or whichever standard your country uses), or video games rated M, or whatever. They could be deep character studies that are also mature games. They could be escapist fantasies aimed at adults (and lets face it aimed at kids that want the thrill of seeing taboo material). They could be wildly offensive with little to no redeeming value as artistic criticism of anything.<br /> <br /> And let's be honest. The WoD games have always aimed to be mature, but very frequently fallen into just being &quot;mature&quot; instead. WtA is one of the worst offenders because of the heavily splatterpunk influences in its aesthetics. The early WoD books succeeded in being mature when they did frequently despite themselves, with only a few books really showing off what mature gaming can look like when games are crafted with care. No book that's talked about the Swords of Heimdall has elevated them from &quot;mature&quot; to mature. They're not necessary to addressing neo-Nazis and the new rise of fascism in Western liberal democracies. The idea of turning the whole Get Tribe into the SoH and making them an antagonist faction doesn't accomplish this either. Games where I get to punch Nazis are fun, but that' doesn't make them serious interrogations of why there are still Nazis around. <br /> <br /> Sambrano's experience is just another entry in a bad trend of revelations that Paradox is not interested in the work of making a mature game, but also wants credit for moving the WoD away from being a &quot;mature&quot; gaming world. The results are what we've seen for ourselves: increasing blandness. The repeated unwillingness to do the work of engaging with serious topics means they're just getting cut from the books. The repeated PR disasters has just lead to more and more risk-avoidance as corporate policy. W5 is not going to be a game where WtA's legacy of elevating Indigenous issues to core themes of a game escapes its past missteps. The book is going to just cut such issues out as core elements and let them slide back into character quirks where some Black Furies or Children of Gaia happen to focus on Indigenous issues over the plethora of other ills in human society. There's no reason to assume W5 can handle fascism and Nazism as themes the game will actually enable mature gaming around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T15:34:16-07:00","id":1519052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518945#post1518945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible that KM's push to have Fenrir as SoH has to do with his own experiences with racism and alt-right in Sweden. Things are not exactly great there in terms of racial relationships, especially in Stockholm where his Linkedin says he currently is.<br /> <br /> This does not justify the way he pushed for all Fenrir to be SoH-like, but given this <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/BavmMZQ.png\" target=\"_blank\">screenshot</a> I get the feeling KM is coming from a very different context than JS.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, a fictional tribe of werewolves got shafted because of KM's RL encounters with bigots? I'm sure this will teach the bigots not to mess with KM ever again! /s</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":83,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","user":"evolved_lupus","date":". 07-29-2023, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T16:24:13-07:00","id":1519055,"title":"","content":"I was writing something cool and provocative, giving support to our friend J.F. <i>Sambrano </i>and firing up against the company's nonpartisan stances (but being nonpartisan is actually just being conservative with a guilt or desire to cloak in fictional neutrality), that are just for capitalist profit. But.... the browser crasshed and this forum doesn't have a save and I should've made one myself. So I'll just go with &quot;I agree with most that has been said here. I thank for the workers and fans who have not let this go down quietly. And also wish WoD would not try to burry its fundamental identity of being 'political' and relevant to real-world issues, as many of its games originally were.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is all for now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T16:42:02-07:00","id":1519056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519014#post1519014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know W20 brought them back and then didn't do anything with them. But at this point I think we have to accept that we have two different points of view on this coming from two different sets of life experiences and just agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because W20 is metaplot agnostic like the other 20th games. It basically allows you to control what events have or have not happened yet.<br /> <br /> I myself tend to adhere pretty closely to the official timeline.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T17:19:51-07:00","id":1519058,"title":"","content":"Another issue of making the entirety of the GoF into Nazis is worldbuilding. When the story is set in WWII, you can make your Nazi villain the most over-the-top mustache-twirling villain imaginable and yet you got the history of WWII and the Nazis during that time to back it up. You know that they were evil people with power doing evil things. So how are you going to explain an entire Tribe of Nazi-werewolves in the W5-setting? As a faction in the game... they're just around. And does it even matter if the werewolf-antagonist-pack in your game is a GoF- or a BSD-pack? At least with the hunter-orgs in H5 the core-book was pushing hard for the idea that hunter-orgs and everybody working for them is bad but at least you could picture having the same goals as them. Here, it's Nazis and Wyrm-worshippers... why would your PC-Garou-pack's goals ever align with those two factions...?!<br /> <br /> Also, in terms of origins... If you're saying that the GoF have always been this way and they've only started doing their own thing because of the Apocalypse, you're saying there used to be a time Garou like the PCs used to work with these Nazi-werewolves. If you're saying the Apocalypse plus Hauglosk turned everybody in this particular Tribe into Nazis then you get the downright immature portrayal of rightwing-radicalization by the portrayal of it being akin to flipping a light switch. In that version, you also have the issue of PCs also potentially suffering from Hauglosk during play and... yeah, what would this origin-story say about how players could portray their Hauglosk-behavior...?<br /> <br /> And the nuanced version is already out the window because this idea presupposes treating a Tribe like a monolith. Especially with the new Garou-Kin-dynamic Garou-Tribes should tend to be the complete opposite of that and yet...<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> on this that the WOD-team not putting in the effort to present a truly <i>mature </i>game just results in a lot of blandness and the occasional controversies due to a lack of research and/or care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T17:42:02-07:00","id":1519060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519056#post1519056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because W20 is metaplot agnostic like the other 20th games. It basically allows you to control what events have or have not happened yet.<br /> <br /> I myself tend to adhere pretty closely to the official timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that has both strengths and weaknesses. Honestly if you're not going to do anything with the SoH it's best to leave them out, and I'm not sure Werewolf's ever actually done anything with them beyond wiping them out.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that WoD was a pretty early step into mature gaming, hence it often missing the mark. It also suffers with the 'edgy=mature' issue that's so prevalent, which makes it easy to overlook some of the more legitimately mature takes. It's also kind of stuck in rules that were originally designed for combat heavy games because the Devs didn't really know better (and because combat games are fun), and has arguably been overtaken by other games exploring similar themes (with Unknown Armies 3e being the really low hanging fruit). M5 has always been the one that's actually going to be interesting, and for all the wrong reasons (it's probably the one that evolved to have the most legitimately mature and nuanced take on its core conflict).<br /> <br /> But honestly, I'll agree that I don't trust Paradox to make mature games. They've shown reluctance to engage with the themes of Werewolf, their first response was to bring back the SoH and turn all Get into them (this removing the distinctions that would be the only worthwhile fucking reason to bring them back), then went to 'well all Get are basically the SoH anyway'. I half expect the eventual M5 previews to reveal that they've turned the Technocracy into The New Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T22:46:12-07:00","id":1519074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519052#post1519052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, a fictional tribe of werewolves got shafted because of KM's RL encounters with bigots? I'm sure this will teach the bigots not mess with KM ever again! /s</span></div> </div> </div> </div>More like a tribe based on the area KM lives in naturally would reflect his own experience with the Indigenous majority culture. Because the tribe is from the area, he would not have as much attachment to its depiction even aside from the glyph and tribal culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T23:34:30-07:00","id":1519076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519058#post1519058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in terms of origins... If you're saying that the GoF have always been this way and they've only started doing their own thing because of the Apocalypse, you're saying there used to be a time Garou like the PCs used to work with these Nazi-werewolves. If you're saying the Apocalypse plus Hauglosk turned everybody in this particular Tribe into Nazis then you get the downright immature portrayal of rightwing-radicalization by the portrayal of it being akin to flipping a light switch. In that version, you also have the issue of PCs also potentially suffering from Hauglosk during play and... yeah, what would this origin-story say about how players could portray their Hauglosk-behavior...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they just wanted to make an enemy that was indisputably evil and somehow current. As for the tribe's history, I don't think it's hard to find a cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T00:00:06-07:00","id":1519077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519076#post1519076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they just wanted to make an enemy that was indisputably evil and somehow current. As for the tribe's history, I don't think it's hard to find a cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is already more than enough as an evil force you're combating in the game. And I would say climate change is very current as an issue as well. So the game wasn't lacking in those two departments, to begin with. So it isn't like Nazi-werewolves are filling a void in the game's setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T02:47:28-07:00","id":1519086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519076#post1519076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they just wanted to make an enemy that was indisputably evil and somehow current. As for the tribe's history, I don't think it's hard to find a cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs exist, BSD kinfolk exist and fomori exist. BSDs would be more than willing to be neo-nazi and some even have ancestor who were actual nazi. You don't need to turn another tribe into pure evil, you already have a flexible tribe that can do it all and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T02:59:26-07:00","id":1519087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519086#post1519086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BSDs exist, BSD kinfolk exist and fomori exist. BSDs would be more than willing to be neo-nazi and some even have ancestor who were actual nazi. You don't need to turn another tribe into pure evil, you already have a flexible tribe that can do it all and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the more proof that KM's decision regarding the status of the Get of Fenris in W5 was a knee-jerk reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:14:16-07:00","id":1519088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519076#post1519076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they just wanted to make an enemy that was indisputably evil and somehow current. As for the tribe's history, I don't think it's hard to find a cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. That's now what was in the books. The Swords were never the dominant strain of the Get. Even in WW2 the Get were fighting Nazis. How this mutated into &quot;Get have always been and always will be Nazis&quot; is down to a game of broken telephone.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:22:25-07:00","id":1519089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519088#post1519088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again. That's now what was in the books. The Swords were never the dominant strain of the Get. Even in WW2 the Get were fighting Nazis. How this mutated into &quot;Get have always been and always will be Nazis&quot; is down to a game of broken telephone.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The way KM talked about the Tribes, he seemed to have a very flattened conception of pretty much all of them. Black Furies are the &quot;feminist Tribe&quot;, the Younger and Older Brother Tribe are just those two Native American Tribes (which &quot;inspired&quot; him to think that maybe one should be removed because why would you have two Native American Tribes in the game...). And the GoF are just the Norse white supremacist Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:24:49-07:00","id":1519090,"title":"","content":"Double post delete please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:24:49-07:00","id":1519091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519077#post1519077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wyrm is already more than enough as an evil force you're combating in the game. And I would say climate change is very current as an issue as well. So the game wasn't lacking in those two departments, to begin with. So it isn't like Nazi-werewolves are filling a void in the game's setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression they were part of the larger rotten camp plot point, were they make sense since you're going to have a broad variety of awful to go at.<br /> <br /> They're more part of the &quot;the garou nation has a lot of internal problems&quot; plot point rather than nazi werewolves as a standalone. Dying cubs are just as repulsive and their are several which are arguably more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-29-2023, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:40:57-07:00","id":1519092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519089#post1519089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Younger and Older Brother Tribe are just those two Native American Tribes (which &quot;inspired&quot; him to think that maybe one should be removed because why would you have two Native American Tribes in the game...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Its probably worth noting their are two slavic tribes and two celtic tribes if you count the spirals. Its just the coding is less visible.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:47:39-07:00","id":1519093,"title":"","content":"Personally, if I had to pick a foe for a new edition, I would put more emphasis on the Weaver. She has been profiting immensely from the Garou's focus on moustache-twirling villains, all the while building up the infrastructure that enables the Wyrm in the first place. Politically and physically, she is pretty much responsible for Gaia's decline in the past 200 years.<br /> <br /> Since highly authoritarian political structures are also a Weaver hallmark, you can easily mesh that up with the rise of the alt-right and fascism if you want. The Wyrm sits on top of the throne the Weaver has built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T03:53:39-07:00","id":1519095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519091#post1519091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the impression they were part of the larger rotten camp plot point, were they make sense since you're going to have a broad variety of awful to go at.<br /> <br /> They're more part of the &quot;the garou nation has a lot of internal problems&quot; plot point rather than nazi werewolves as a standalone. Dying cubs are just as repulsive and their are several which are arguably more dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wonder if the first iteration already had &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; as a story-point for its new status-quo. I assume even if the first iteration didn't, when the second iteration introduced &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot;, KM (since he was still on the developer-team) still made the same case for him being unable to envision GoF as anything other than white supremacists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its probably worth noting their are two slavic tribes and two celtic tribes if you count the spirals. Its just the coding is less visible. </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, you know how it is... &quot;Fianna's just a word.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T08:09:29-07:00","id":1519111,"title":"","content":"Just clarifying, yes I know that there are BSD and Formori and they would fulfill this role, and very well, but these antagonists didn't seem interesting for their proposal, I agree that they could, but let me explain my point, besides that they need to explain what are the BSD, the Fomori and what they do to new players, using the GoF which generates an easy explanation that they &quot;are&quot; Nazi-Werewolf they don't need to elaborate much further as it's something the people already know, so it's easier and faster, basically they are making a parallel with current causes, you know what I'm talking about, they could adapt the BSD and the Formori for this context, but they would have to elaborate on the which is Formori and BSD and guessing KM would be willing to read something abot them, and again that was the easier way out, and then if they still want to insert an explanation of BSD they can make a supplement and sell more. As for the problem of the Garou nation, from the explanations that people have been commenting on them I can come to the conclusion that they want to put the Garou nation as problematic and use a Retcon that the GoF have always been like this, the other tribes knew that, but only chose to ignore, maybe not wanting to solve the problem of the other tribes, or because they could be useful in the fight, or any other excuse they can give, the point is that they can say that they were always a problem and that becomes one more point for younger Garou don't care about the downfall of the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is all a conclusion I was able to reach based on the sparse information and comments, so when W5 is released I could be dead wrong and I problaly am and to be quite honest, I just think they wanted to get rid of any controversy involving GoF. I don't know what transpired in this text, but I'm just really frustrated.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T08:46:05-07:00","id":1519112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519111#post1519111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just clarifying, yes I know that there are BSD and Formori and they would fulfill this role, and very well, but these antagonists didn't seem interesting for their proposal, I agree that they could, but let me explain my point, besides that they need to explain what are the BSD, the Fomori and what they do to new players, using the GoF which generates an easy explanation that they &quot;are&quot; Nazi-Werewolf they don't need to elaborate much further as it's something the people already know, so it's easier and faster, basically they are making a parallel with current causes, you know what I'm talking about, they could adapt the BSD and the Formori for this context, but they would have to elaborate on the which is Formori and BSD and guessing KM would be willing to read something abot them, and again that was the easier way out, and then if they still want to insert an explanation of BSD they can make a supplement and sell more. .\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Really goes to show the surface-level reading of the setting from what we've seen. Though one thing confuses me; Over the Fenrir, Red Talons are seen as really bad and since they are lupus-only it creates some... choice thoughts about them. Yet they are kept while Gale stalkers and Fenrir are under the axe.<br /> <br /> While I get the Fenrir somewhat with the nordic history and tribal glyph, I have seen way more critique of the Talons over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T11:37:22-07:00","id":1519121,"title":"","content":"I've always felt like the Black Spiral Dancers were the epitome of &quot;the path of zealotry, the way of ultimate blind rage, the fate of the vainglorious hero&quot;<br /> I think it should be more like a rallying point for all the fallen Garou in a way<br /> And a good melting pot for storytellers to show a reflection of werewolves worst facets<br /> <br /> Maybe not a simple label to mark a Garou group who is getting wonky and fascisty, but definitely the dangerous place to which any Garou may fall... And I don't mean &quot;oh, let's sit and have a heartwarming and understanding conversation with nazi lupines&quot;. I rather have this hubris threat more evident, and have plots of Garou instead of being The Batman Vengeance, being The Batman Hope, who lets not their brothers and sisters fall to Rage, nor to Hauglosk or Harano. We and Garous have many hazards around, but we also have lots of allies and friends whom we must not forget.<br /> <br /> Garou shouldn't just care for Earth because there is a big confirmed God telling them. They should love and care, lookout for one another, and fight for this. You must have a reason to Rage after all. So yeah, dealing with the fanatism of the &quot;Garou Nation&quot;, should also be an important thread of the game. This means dealing with extremists that can yet sit and dialogue, means organizing, and not ... you know... having entire tribes wiped out or turning total evil. <br /> These are the world parallels I would like to see more, and this begs for representation of real-world groups and ideas. It is impossible for Werewolf the Apocalypse (in any iteration, cuz this is axis to the setting) to be devoid of human concerns and issues. The whole game is about modern world frustrations and the rage of feeling powerless since the beginning. And hell yeah we are feeling the Rage in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T12:47:28-07:00","id":1519123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519112#post1519112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really goes to show the surface-level reading of the setting from what we've seen. Though one thing confuses me; Over the Fenrir, Red Talons are seen as really bad and since they are lupus-only it creates some... choice thoughts about them. Yet they are kept while Gale stalkers and Fenrir are under the axe.<br /> <br /> While I get the Fenrir somewhat with the nordic history and tribal glyph, I have seen way more critique of the Talons over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because they don't parallel anything human, just wild animals and that's apparently ignored, and who knows if they won't change in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T12:50:44-07:00","id":1519124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519121#post1519121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt like the Black Spiral Dancers were the epitome of &quot;the path of zealotry, the way of ultimate blind rage, the fate of the vainglorious hero&quot;<br /> I think it should be more like a rallying point for all the fallen Garou in a way<br /> And a good melting pot for storytellers to show a reflection of werewolves worst facets<br /> <br /> Maybe not a simple label to mark a Garou group who is getting wonky and fascisty, but definitely the dangerous place to which any Garou may fall... And I don't mean &quot;oh, let's sit and have a heartwarming and understanding conversation with nazi lupines&quot;. I rather have this hubris threat more evident, and have plots of Garou instead of being The Batman Vengeance, being The Batman Hope, who lets not their brothers and sisters fall to Rage, nor to Hauglosk or Harano. We and Garous have many hazards around, but we also have lots of allies and friends whom we must not forget.<br /> <br /> Garou shouldn't just care for Earth because there is a big confirmed God telling them. They should love and care, lookout for one another, and fight for this. You must have a reason to Rage after all. So yeah, dealing with the fanatism of the &quot;Garou Nation&quot;, should also be an important thread of the game. This means dealing with extremists that can yet sit and dialogue, means organizing, and not ... you know... having entire tribes wiped out or turning total evil.<br /> These are the world parallels I would like to see more, and this begs for representation of real-world groups and ideas. It is impossible for Werewolf the Apocalypse (in any iteration, cuz this is axis to the setting) to be devoid of human concerns and issues. The whole game is about modern world frustrations and the rage of feeling powerless since the beginning. And hell yeah we are feeling the Rage in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, today's world doesn't want to solve problems in conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T16:44:35-07:00","id":1519134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519095#post1519095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I wonder if the first iteration already had &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; as a story-point for its new status-quo. I assume even if the first iteration didn't, when the second iteration introduced &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot;, KM (since he was still on the developer-team) still made the same case for him being unable to envision GoF as anything other than white supremacists...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter\u2019s Entertainment created a blog post, presumably before it taken in house, giving a tease for what their version had in store. Based on what I\u2019ve seen setting wise from W5 I\u2019m not sure much had changed from the original direction Karim had given for the book. Besides the whole decoupling tribes from cultures thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_2000,h_1125,al_c,q_95,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: The Apocalypse - 5th Edition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A Storytelling Game of Savage Resistance Have you ever taken a moment to just stop, observe the world around you, and see the injustice of it all? You can see it, the scars and sores of the land. You can smell it, the degradation and decay in the air. You can feel it, the fever and tremors of a dying world. The question is: When will you rage? At its heart, Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a Storytelling game of Savage Resistance. What does that mean? It means that Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a gam </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth noting Werewolf: The Apocalypse Heart of the Forest was announced a couple of weeks before Justin Achilli was announced as the World of Darkness Brand Creative Lead and came out right around the time WoD announced Hunter: The Reckoning and W5 being done in house. I would imagine by the time Justin came one the game would have been mostly written without time for rewrites. Which would indicate similar to the Hunters team, any story direction would likely have come from Karim.<br /> <br /> If you watched Justin\u2019s announcement, you may remember this was when it was first publicly made known W5 would be a reimagining of WtA. WoD had stated publicly HotF would be cannon. So when Justin said one of the tribes had fallen to whatever they\u2019re calling it, anyone played HotF knew it was the Get as the game described them as Garou Fascist.<br /> <br /> I feel like I\u2019m rambling so my TLDR, it\u2019s quite possible Justin had no part in the \u201cAll Get are Fascist thing\u201d and it\u2019s been part of direction given by Karim the entire time. When the Hunters team wouldn\u2019t right it they pulled it in house to find someone who would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25049,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","user":"ZakRulz","date":".  Accidental Emoji 07-29-2023, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T22:46:55-07:00","id":1519156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519124#post1519124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, today's world doesn't want to solve problems in conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>was it someday?<br /> was any great and good change made by sitting and talking?<br /> but even one can't fight alone, nor one fights against a single unitary thing. Garou are no different in my eyes. I love pack dynamics, and wish there was more cultural practices (be it from Tribe or general) around them. I mean, how the Sabbath still is the sect with the most rich practices, codes and cultures (in the session-to-session play) baffles me to this day. <br /> <br /> But yeah, Werewolf isn't the game to sit and talk, but it can't be fight all the time. First is not kill Wyrm/Weaver, but Save Gaia. That means saving people and making the world better too, and besides ripping the dominant power apart and ending the tools of oppression, there isn't much fighting to do those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T05:56:25-07:00","id":1519166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519123#post1519123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's because they don't parallel anything human, just wild animals and that's apparently ignored, and who knows if they won't change in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, if we go by quick kneejerk reactions, wouldn't a tribe that's motto is stereotyped as &quot;Kill all humans&quot; be the most likely to be cut? Or is the lack of political ties enough to make them not as good to use as the Fenrir?<br /> <br /> Regardless, I really wish paradox's writers weren't going for the easiest option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T12:30:41-07:00","id":1519194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519111#post1519111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just clarifying, yes I know that there are BSD and Formori and they would fulfill this role, and very well, but these antagonists didn't seem interesting for their proposal, I agree that they could, but let me explain my point, besides that they need to explain what are the BSD, the Fomori and what they do to new players, using the GoF which generates an easy explanation that they &quot;are&quot; Nazi-Werewolf they don't need to elaborate much further as it's something the people already know, so it's easier and faster, basically they are making a parallel with current causes, you know what I'm talking about, they could adapt the BSD and the Formori for this context, but they would have to elaborate on the which is Formori and BSD and guessing KM would be willing to read something abot them, and again that was the easier way out, and then if they still want to insert an explanation of BSD they can make a supplement and sell more.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this game is the fifth edition of WtA. This corebook <i>has to</i> explain BSD, Formori and the Wyrm. The game's legacy creates boundaries for what is possible here. So wanting there to be this other werewolf-antagonist-faction with no ties to the Wyrm means you have to situate in the conflict with the Wyrm. And saying that you can picture the GoF be Nazis isn't really good enough. All that's about is somebody commenting on past editions. The bigger question is how this fits into W5 as a game. What theme is the ST supposed to pursue by putting GoF-Nazi-werewolves in their game? And what does it add that the bigger story-beat of the war against the Wyrm can't provide...?<br /> <br /> Additionally, this choice for an antagonist-faction means that to follow through on that premise things like antisemitism, racism, eugenics, holocaust-denial etc. can become part of a W5 game. Having a dedicated Nazi/white-supremacist faction means that the corebook has to take responsibility for instructing STs on how to handle NPCs with such extreme political beliefs. Especially since missteps with a sensitive and serious topic like that can be catastrophic. If this version that's about to come out still is this direct in painting the GoF as Nazis/white supremacists then this book better have a far bigger section on this topic than the &quot;Fascism In Play&quot;-bit from the V5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that if the idea is to have a werewolf-antagonist-faction untied to the Wyrm because the game wants more werewolf vs werewolf conflict... then there's only one thing to say to that: &quot;Werwolf the Forsaken did it first - and better.&quot; The Pure are certainly a better concept/antagonist than the idea of this one Tribe being full of Nazis...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519111#post1519111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the problem of the Garou nation, from the explanations that people have been commenting on them I can come to the conclusion that they want to put the Garou nation as problematic and use a Retcon that the GoF have always been like this, the other tribes knew that, but only chose to ignore, maybe not wanting to solve the problem of the other tribes, or because they could be useful in the fight, or any other excuse they can give, the point is that they can say that they were always a problem and that becomes one more point for younger Garou don't care about the downfall of the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is all a conclusion I was able to reach based on the sparse information and comments, so when W5 is released I could be dead wrong and I problaly am and to be quite honest, I just think they wanted to get rid of any controversy involving GoF. I don't know what transpired in this text, but I'm just really frustrated.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right on that count. We're gonna see in a couple of days how well the worldbuilding holds up once we have the full text. I just keep thinking of H5 and how invested it was in talking about how bad hunter-orgs are. With H5, though, the &quot;big bad&quot; was just the vague notion of &quot;supernatural monsters&quot; in general. And I simply can't picture this same dynamic working well where the book constantly tells you how bad the Garou-Nation was (with an undertone of &quot;Just look at the GoF if you don't get it...&quot;) but with the difference that the &quot;big bad&quot; in this case is the Wyrm - that's about to destroy the world (the setting is mid-Apocalypse, after all). The moral calculus of what matters changes somewhat in that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T13:45:46-07:00","id":1519199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519194#post1519194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're probably right on that count. We're gonna see in a couple of days how well the worldbuilding holds up once we have the full text. I just keep thinking of H5 and how invested it was in talking about how bad hunter-orgs are. With H5, though, the &quot;big bad&quot; was just the vague notion of &quot;supernatural monsters&quot; in general. And I simply can't picture this same dynamic working well where the book constantly tells you how bad the Garou-Nation was (with an undertone of &quot;Just look at the GoF if you don't get it...&quot;) but with the difference that the &quot;big bad&quot; in this case is the Wyrm - that's about to destroy the world (the setting is mid-Apocalypse, after all). The moral calculus of what matters changes somewhat in that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that, since we are using 'skimmed the corebook' readings here, the Wyrm isn't an attractive bad guy because it is just a 'captain planet villain.' Having a more personal foe in the Fenrir with the added political tone of right wingers might have been more interesting.<br /> <br /> But that is a poor reading of not just the Wyrm, but the BSDs as well. After all, since the game focuses on non-Nation aligned young garou, you don't have to state that the neo nazi werewolves are BSDs or serving the Wyrm. They could be, but the characters would not know it. And that is if the BSDs are openly threatening, they could easily be encouraging the young garou to be free all the while continuing their deeds.<br /> <br /> It all just needs an understanding of the tools in use, rather than creating new ones.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T00:46:31-07:00","id":1519228,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much contemporary anxieties on far right resurgence are clouding the developers and parawolfs judgement on the Get? Either through fear of nazism or fear of/irritation at the surge of fascist and Conservative presence in nerd culture both extreme and otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T02:10:18-07:00","id":1519231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519199#post1519199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling that, since we are using 'skimmed the corebook' readings here, the Wyrm isn't an attractive bad guy because it is just a 'captain planet villain.' Having a more personal foe in the Fenrir with the added political tone of right wingers might have been more interesting.<br /> <br /> But that is a poor reading of not just the Wyrm, but the BSDs as well. After all, since the game focuses on non-Nation aligned young garou, you don't have to state that the neo nazi werewolves are BSDs or serving the Wyrm. They could be, but the characters would not know it. And that is if the BSDs are openly threatening, they could easily be encouraging the young garou to be free all the while continuing their deeds.<br /> <br /> It all just needs an understanding of the tools in use, rather than creating new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519228#post1519228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much contemporary anxieties on far right resurgence are clouding the developers and parawolfs judgement on the Get? Either through fear of nazism or fear of/irritation at the surge of fascist and Conservative presence in nerd culture both extreme and otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a limit to just how &quot;real&quot; you can get with the real-world-issues that you bring into the game. At some point, the contrast between the real-world-issues and the genre-conventions at the heart of a WOD-game will simply become too stark. And a good example of that is the V5-controversy and the way WOD-fiction and real-world-issues were interwoven. Like, imagine if we had the Nazi-GoF and one paragraph off-handedly talks about their role in the January 6 insurrection...? Or that Pentex was involved in the Deepwater Horizon oil-spill. Those two events would be good examples of &quot;rise of right-wing extremism&quot; and &quot;bad corporate behavior/environmental catastrophe&quot; that would fit this game. But the moment you get too literal and on-the-nose in how you link these topics with a WOD-game, the whole thing becomes weird and potentially even upsetting. Because sure, these topics could figure into the setting of W5 and would fit the themes - but at the end of the day, this is still a game about werewolves with spirit-powers. Like, instead of talking about straight-up Nazism, let's imagine a multi-tribal faction believing that all you need to turn things around is a second Impergium. And under that umbrella you can mention that werewolves with some right-wing extremist beliefs are a part of this faction. Also, this game's system isn't set up to create deep, nuanced conversations about things like right-wing-extremism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T05:53:42-07:00","id":1519243,"title":"","content":"The new edition has also doubled down on 'too much rage=bad' (which was previously much more minor) and linked that idea to the GoF. Which leads to the implication that anybody with too much anger inside them is at risk of becoming part of the alt-right. Which isn't an inherently bad idea for a game, but it's weird when it's coming from a franchise previously defined by the anger of the left.<br /> <br /> However I like the idea of an Impergium 2.0 faction gaining traction, even if it could also be do e poorly (it is a position held by a lot of Red Talons). It allows you to explore a lot of similar ideas without having to explicitly deal with real world political movements","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T06:39:57-07:00","id":1519246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519231#post1519231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a limit to just how &quot;real&quot; you can get with the real-world-issues that you bring into the game. At some point, the contrast between the real-world-issues and the genre-conventions at the heart of a WOD-game will simply become too stark. And a good example of that is the V5-controversy and the way WOD-fiction and real-world-issues were interwoven. Like, imagine if we had the Nazi-GoF and one paragraph off-handedly talks about their role in the January 6 insurrection...? Or that Pentex was involved in the Deepwater Horizon oil-spill. Those two events would be good examples of &quot;rise of right-wing extremism&quot; and &quot;bad corporate behavior/environmental catastrophe&quot; that would fit this game. But the moment you get too literal and on-the-nose in how you link these topics with a WOD-game, the whole thing becomes weird and potentially even upsetting. Because sure, these topics could figure into the setting of W5 and would fit the themes - but at the end of the day, this is still a game about werewolves with spirit-powers. Like, instead of talking about straight-up Nazism, let's imagine a multi-tribal faction believing that all you need to turn things around is a second Impergium. And under that umbrella you can mention that werewolves with some right-wing extremist beliefs are a part of this faction. Also, this game's system isn't set up to create deep, nuanced conversations about things like right-wing-extremism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really had a problem with irl stuff influencing supernatural it ultimately benited the setting by grounding them. The rule by revised was the supernatural groups react to it rather than instigate worked fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T08:07:34-07:00","id":1519250,"title":"","content":"The issue with Impergium 2.0 is that its a non-starter. There are simply too many people and too few Garou for any real impact unless they move to Ratkin methods of population control......and even those are having less and less of an impact as time goes on.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T08:40:27-07:00","id":1519253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519246#post1519246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never really had a problem with irl stuff influencing supernatural it ultimately benited the setting by grounding them. The rule by revised was the supernatural groups react to it rather than instigate worked fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I mean by these things having a limit. You include irl-references but there's always at least some separation between the real thing and the fantasy-equivalent. You're not setting things up like &quot;Not every member of the alt-right is a GoF-Garou - but every GoF-Garou is a member of the alt-right.&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519250#post1519250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with Impergium 2.0 is that its a non-starter. There are simply too many people and too few Garou for any real impact unless they move to Ratkin methods of population control......and even those are having less and less of an impact as time goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I don't think that would be an issue. We're just talking about a reactionary belief caused by Gaia being dead/dying. Like, there are plenty of QAnon-beliefs that realistically should be non-starters but you still got people believing in it. It's not about it actually being a solution, it's about an appealing belief (&quot;If we kill x number of humans, everything will be fine.&quot;) that has a following. And I think that as an allegory for a rise in conspiracy-theories and right-wing-extremism (because those particular extremists might believe &quot;If we kill x number of a specific sub-set of humans, everything will be fine.&quot;) works better than just taking a faction and describing them as Nazis/white supremacists. And I'd rather have discussions of Impergium 2.0 at the table as an allegory of these real-world-issues than have players engage with straight-up Nazi-NPCs. Also, because on one hand, such a serious and heavy topic might not be for everyone (a player might use the X-Card or an equivalent along those lines) and on the other hand, I as an ST wouldn't want to downplay the severity/evilness of Nazi-NPCs either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:04:13-07:00","id":1519269,"title":"","content":"So uh, guess what guys? Second Impegrium WAS in the cards for W5. This thread: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...houghts-on-wta</a><br /> <br /> Shows just how long this process has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:39:22-07:00","id":1519273,"title":"","content":"I've also just had this idea... Could it be that this is related to V5? For V5 they introduced a new antagonist-faction with the Second Inquisition. So could it be that one of the development-goals for W5 was to somehow create a new antagonist-faction similar to the Second Inquisition...? And with that goal in mind, that's when the idea came into play to make the GoF Nazis/white supremacists and a new antagonist-faction. Like, design-wise it was taken as a given that W5 <i>needed </i>a new antagonist-faction. And that's where KM's take on the GoF comes into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T13:44:25-07:00","id":1519281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519269#post1519269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So uh, guess what guys? Second Impegrium WAS in the cards for W5. This thread: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...houghts-on-wta</a><br /> <br /> Shows just how long this process has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I totally forgot I was giving a rundown of that Ken and Robin talk about stuff... 6 years ago!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T14:12:20-07:00","id":1519283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519269#post1519269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So uh, guess what guys? Second Impegrium WAS in the cards for W5. This thread: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...houghts-on-wta</a><br /> <br /> Shows just how long this process has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a slow-motion train crash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:59:21-07:00","id":1519295,"title":"","content":"I'm currently 41.... Werewolf: The Apocalpyse was literally the first RPG I ever played, when I was 12 years old. While it's not my favorite WoD game (That's Mage) It's still special and close to my heart.<br /> <br /> My two favorite tribes have always been &quot;The Get of Fenris&quot; and &quot;The Children of Gaia&quot;, (Odd Dichotomy, I know).<br /> <br /> I loved the Get for two reasons... One, is the 'positive' part of them. The fact the Get were one of the most accepting of Metis (Don't hate the result of the sin) and were very 'progressive' (at least the Good parts of them) in the sense they didn't care who you were, what your gender identity or racial background was... As long as you were Brave, and you fought. I loved that about the Get. The part of them that wasn't tied up in the Nazi stuff (a faction clearly meant to be Villains) but that they were the Tribe that said, &quot;Are you fighting with everything that you have? You're one of us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially with them being the &quot;Germanic&quot; tribe, having them presented with this ideal, your bravery, your willingness to Fight mattered more than anything, was awesome.<br /> <br /> My Great Grandfather was a soldier in the German army during WW2. He was in fact, a &quot;Nazi&quot;. He died, leaving my Great Grandmother a widow, and my Grandfather, fatherless. Towards the end of the war, my Great Grandmother had to hide my Grandfather in the barn to stop the Army from conscripting him to fight a losing battle. The remnants of the army also took the majority of their farm harvest for the war effort, starving them as well.<br /> <br /> When the war was over, my Grandfather came to America, joined the army, and served in the Korean War. When he died, he was given a 21 Gun salute.<br /> <br /> I'm married to a Jewish woman... and someone today literally told me, &quot;Your ancestors are rolling in their grave.&quot; Because of that.<br /> <br /> My Grandfather was a victim of the Nazi regime, and had no love for it. It took his father from him, and made life difficult for his Mother, himself, and his younger brothers.<br /> <br /> The fact the Tribe with the Germanic origins is going to be presented as pure Villains and Nazis is like.... Really, Really, fucking shitty.<br /> <br /> Rather than following the Modern Get whose ranks were more multi-racial, expanding beyond their Germanic origin but keeping their fighting ethos... Rather than having that be the awesome twist that W20 was building to... Yeah, the Germanic Tribe is the one that doesn't care about your Skin Color, Your Sexuality, Your Gender Identity... They just want you to be Brave and to Fight...<br /> <br /> They're just going to be fucking Nazis.<br /> <br /> Yay.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, all the stuff with the Elder Brother and Younger Brother Tribes is shitty too. Werewolf fans would have been more than accommodating in retconning the names)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T18:20:22-07:00","id":1519300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519273#post1519273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also just had this idea... Could it be that this is related to V5? For V5 they introduced a new antagonist-faction with the Second Inquisition. So could it be that one of the development-goals for W5 was to somehow create a new antagonist-faction similar to the Second Inquisition...? And with that goal in mind, that's when the idea came into play to make the GoF Nazis/white supremacists and a new antagonist-faction. Like, design-wise it was taken as a given that W5 <i>needed </i>a new antagonist-faction. And that's where KM's take on the GoF comes into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Second Inquisition is mostly a consolidation of existing enemies under one umbrella and given an increase in importance (as the Sabbat were pushed out of focus for years). It actually arguably reduces the variety in enemy factions by tying the Society of Leopold to Government Agents. I suspect it's existence is less 'let's have a new enemy faction' and more 'justify returning hunters to the prominence they enjoyed in 1e.<br /> <br /> Werewolf never really had the same shifting of focus with its enemies, probably because villainous werewolves were already a big part of the Wyrm's forces. At best the new Fenrir represent the increased importance of friction within the Nation, except that <i>apparently the Garou Nation doesn't really exist anymore</i>.<br /> <br /> Really if I really needed a new big antagonist faction for W5 I'd promote one of the other Fera to the role. They've decided the time of the Garou is over, that their methods are actively harmful, and it would be better if they get exterminated before they kill off more changing breeds. But that kind of feels really unnecessary when the book already needs to cover human actors, spirits, formori, and Black Spiral Dancers in the antagonist section (and human actors should probably cover independents as well as Pentex). Sure Forsaken has a slightly longer list of core adversaries (humans, other werewolves, spirits, claimed, and hosts) but it also doesn't have to detail just what the Wyrm is, how they're trying to free themself, or anything with as many subsidiaries as Pentex has,*.<br /> <br /> Most likely the new Fenrir (urgh, can't we give them a new name, Land's Fangs or something like that?) are going to be rage possessed monsters indiscriminately destroying anything, or a Pure knock-off with the multiple factions. Neither of which really add much to the setting.<br /> <br /> * I wonder if Black Dog is going to be reworked into or replaced by a video games company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T20:11:18-07:00","id":1519312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519250#post1519250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with Impergium 2.0 is that its a non-starter. There are simply too many people and too few Garou for any real impact unless they move to Ratkin methods of population control......and even those are having less and less of an impact as time goes on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's not really an issue. Garous desiring a new impergium are not limited to killing people one by one. The &quot;fallen tribe&quot; section of the book Apocalypse shows how each tribe could wreck humanity. <br /> <br /> From mandating incarnae of earthquakes or the seas to destroy the main cities of earth, systematically wrecking the weaver's web needed for infrastructure, starting wars by influencing leaders and generals to bringing upon spirits of plagues on mankind, they have lots of choices.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> after all, if a few humans with nuclear codes have the potential to erase humanity, there's no reason a few supernaturally gifted beig with access to the strings of material reality can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:08:30-07:00","id":1519323,"title":"","content":"The problem with that, is that isn't an Impergium, that's a global extinction event. You're not talking about wiping out humans, you're talking about trying to clean slate everything back to pelagic invertebrates. Trying to use large scale natural disasters (which would cause wars even if you didn't provoke them anyway) doesn't just target humans. You'd also be starting a spiritual anarchy as the web of pact and alliances between spirits, the shifters, and various other mystics get shredded. Do you think all the Incarnae of things that you're trying to get other Incarnae to wipe out are just going to sit back and take it? There's a big difference between what could be done, in theory, when things are so bad that no such consequence could really be worse, and what can be done when you're asking being to go to war because you can't actually fix shit yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're considering an interconnected WoD... vampires and mages tend to have a rather large advantage in trying to stop these sorts of tactics, and a vested interest in through everything at keeping extinction happy Garou from going nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:30:54-07:00","id":1519327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519323#post1519323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that, is that isn't an Impergium, that's a global extinction event. You're not talking about wiping out humans, you're talking about trying to clean slate everything back to pelagic invertebrates. Trying to use large scale natural disasters (which would cause wars even if you didn't provoke them anyway) doesn't just target humans. You'd also be starting a spiritual anarchy as the web of pact and alliances between spirits, the shifters, and various other mystics get shredded. Do you think all the Incarnae of things that you're trying to get other Incarnae to wipe out are just going to sit back and take it? There's a big difference between what could be done, in theory, when things are so bad that no such consequence could really be worse, and what can be done when you're asking being to go to war because you can't actually fix shit yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're considering an interconnected WoD... vampires and mages tend to have a rather large advantage in trying to stop these sorts of tactics, and a vested interest in through everything at keeping extinction happy Garou from going nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is exactly what Saur Ops meant. Just because the Fera can cause apocalyptic destruction isn't the same as restarting the impergium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T09:10:29-07:00","id":1519346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519327#post1519327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is exactly what Saur Ops meant. Just because the Fera can cause apocalyptic destruction isn't the same as restarting the impergium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that was Damian May's post. I was busy being a salt mine about the persistence of Paradox's team pushing it over the past 8 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:11:00-07:00","id":1519362,"title":"","content":"I was largely addressing Nyremne's post anyway? Since that was and escalation of Damian's post including &quot;Ratkin methods,&quot; and those not even being that effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:35:07-07:00","id":1519365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519323#post1519323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that, is that isn't an Impergium, that's a global extinction event. You're not talking about wiping out humans, you're talking about trying to clean slate everything back to pelagic invertebrates. Trying to use large scale natural disasters (which would cause wars even if you didn't provoke them anyway) doesn't just target humans. You'd also be starting a spiritual anarchy as the web of pact and alliances between spirits, the shifters, and various other mystics get shredded. Do you think all the Incarnae of things that you're trying to get other Incarnae to wipe out are just going to sit back and take it? There's a big difference between what could be done, in theory, when things are so bad that no such consequence could really be worse, and what can be done when you're asking being to go to war because you can't actually fix shit yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're considering an interconnected WoD... vampires and mages tend to have a rather large advantage in trying to stop these sorts of tactics, and a vested interest in through everything at keeping extinction happy Garou from going nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's hardly a global exctinction. Say the impergium minded people makes a pact with the incarnae of tides and seas from across the world to drown the world's coastal cities.<br /> It would kill an immense ammount of of humans, but it wouldn't be a wiping out of humanity.<br /> <br /> As for the potential war of incarnae willing to cull humanity and those who need them and their creation, well it's already the case. The incarnae of marine lifes will clearly be hostile to incarnae of plastic.<br /> also, incarnae are not equals in strenght or ability to influence the physical world. An incarnae of tides is a geologically old being and causing a tsunami is part of what they could do, since it's part of their nature. In contrast, what could the spirits of concrete, plastic, informatic or the city spirits of the coastal cities facing the tsunami could do to stop it? They are all pretty yound incarnae, and their range of abilities couldn't prevent the wave from hiting them.<br /> <br /> So a war will happen, but the garou in question can then fight these incarnae. In the same way that garou are fightig incarnae willing to cause massive destruction.<br /> <br /> I would also avoid trying to consider an interconnected wod, since such a thing, if considered seriously, wreck the setting of each games and notably their respective stakes.<br /> <br /> For exemple, wto is based on the ongoing advance of oblivion, and being trapped in a dark afterlife with one's darker self. But mages can (and I'm not extrapolating since it's mentioned in at least one mta's book) take forcefully a wraith to the other umbrae, avoiding oblivion, and forcefully silence their shadow.<br /> <br /> And the same goes with wta. The apocalypse would hardly be a thing since even the technocracy consider climate change something to stop, and are fighting fomori and banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 08-01-2023, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:51:21-07:00","id":1519367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519365#post1519365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hardly a global exctinction. Say the impergium minded people makes a pact with the incarnae of tides and seas from across the world to drown the world's coastal cities.<br /> It would kill an immense ammount of of humans, but it wouldn't be a wiping out of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the &quot;A Tribe Falls Scenarios&quot;. There are some reall doomsday scenarios there, and the terrifying thing is that they're not THAT hard to pull off.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T16:16:56-07:00","id":1519379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519365#post1519365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hardly a global exctinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you actually thinking out the consequences of what you're talking about?<br /> <br /> How do you wipe out Hobbart without killing dozens of species unique to Tasmania? How do you target Wellington, Auckland, Sydney, Perth, Jakarta, Surabaya, etc. etc. without killing thousand of species unique to island nations where this isn't some vast hospitable inland area for animals to flee to (Keeping in mind that very few Australian species can just run into the central desert and survive compared to more life-friendly spaces like inland Europe or the US).<br /> <br /> There are whole biomes you're destroying in all of this: marshlands, wetlands, estuaries, brackish water, coral reefs, mangrove nurseries... etc. You can't target tsunamis, earthquakes, volcanoes, and so on to just the cities and not all the sensitive (esp. because of cities) biomes around them. And the damage doesn't stop there. If you take out the coastal biomes in and out of the water, you're dooming the in-land biomes in time too. Migratory birds and fish die, species that rely on them die, species that rely on those die, etc. No salmon nurseries because you destroyed them all to wipe out Pacific cities, no salmon runs for bears and other apex predators to eat, killing them, and exploding the population of their unaffected prey until those die from overpopulation. Nothing is spreading seeds and fertilizers that wild plants need wiping out whole forests of species that can't survive the collapsing of animals populations. Etc.<br /> <br /> Life is interconnected. You can't do the kind of damage you're talking about without devastating life on Earth.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that's not even getting into the human waste issue. You aren't taking into account, at all, the kind of pollution you'd be unleashing into the environment. Billions of humans worth of natural waste, garbage, industrial waste, etc. all getting strewn into the environment with nobody around to clean it up in time. Think about how many nuclear reactors would go critical without anyone to run them. They're not designed to withstand this. Imagine 100 Fukushimas all going off at the same time, without the human infrastructures to stop them, and then 200 more a few months later as backup systems start to fail and nobody is around to fix them.<br /> <br /> So yes, what you're talking about is a global extinction event. Because the damage will not stop with humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say the impergium minded people makes a pact with the incarnae of tides and seas from across the world to drown the world's coastal cities.<br /> It would kill an immense ammount of of humans, but it wouldn't be a wiping out of humanity. </div> </div> </div>80% of humanity lives in range of that, and the rest of the 20% aren't all self-sustaining communities that can endure without the rest of humanity without massive population loss as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the potential war of incarnae willing to cull humanity and those who need them and their creation, well it's already the case. The incarnae of marine lifes will clearly be hostile to incarnae of plastic. </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about spirits that rely on humans to exist at all. I'm talking about Heron not wanting all herons to go extinct at the hands of an attempt to genocide humanity, and rallying all the other bird Incarnae against this effort (which shouldn't be hard, Falcon's brood is full of coastal predators that would die off in this scenario too).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a war will happen, but the garou in question can then fight these incarnae. In the same way that garou are fightig incarnae willing to cause massive destruction. </div> </div> </div>What happens when their own patron spirits side against the genocide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T16:51:44-07:00","id":1519381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519379#post1519379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you actually thinking out the consequences of what you're talking about?<br /> <br /> How do you wipe out Hobbart without killing dozens of species unique to Tasmania? How do you target Wellington, Auckland, Sydney, Perth, Jakarta, Surabaya, etc. etc. without killing thousand of species unique to island nations where this isn't some vast hospitable inland area for animals to flee to (Keeping in mind that very few Australian species can just run into the central desert and survive compared to more life-friendly spaces like inland Europe or the US).<br /> <br /> There are whole biomes you're destroying in all of this: marshlands, wetlands, estuaries, brackish water, coral reefs, mangrove nurseries... etc. You can't target tsunamis, earthquakes, volcanoes, and so on to just the cities and not all the sensitive (esp. because of cities) biomes around them. And the damage doesn't stop there. If you take out the coastal biomes in and out of the water, you're dooming the in-land biomes in time too. Migratory birds and fish die, species that rely on them die, species that rely on those die, etc. No salmon nurseries because you destroyed them all to wipe out Pacific cities, no salmon runs for bears and other apex predators to eat, killing them, and exploding the population of their unaffected prey until those die from overpopulation. Nothing is spreading seeds and fertilizers that wild plants need wiping out whole forests of species that can't survive the collapsing of animals populations. Etc.<br /> <br /> Life is interconnected. You can't do the kind of damage you're talking about without devastating life on Earth.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that's not even getting into the human waste issue. You aren't taking into account, at all, the kind of pollution you'd be unleashing into the environment. Billions of humans worth of natural waste, garbage, industrial waste, etc. all getting strewn into the environment with nobody around to clean it up in time. Think about how many nuclear reactors would go critical without anyone to run them. They're not designed to withstand this. Imagine 100 Fukushimas all going off at the same time, without the human infrastructures to stop them, and then 200 more a few months later as backup systems start to fail and nobody is around to fix them.<br /> <br /> So yes, what you're talking about is a global extinction event. Because the damage will not stop with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>we're talking about werewolf the apocalypse. The world is at an end. These species are already doomed. So it's not hard of a stretch that impergium minded garou would consider that sacrificing already doomed species to protect those that can still be saved.<br /> <br /> Would such garou like it? Clearly not, but then, y's a bit late now to cull humanity without consequences. And seeing how many garou camps contain members having sympathies for the idea of a second impergium, this &quot;we'll have to do it, even if the cost is terrible&quot; mindset is not out of canon, especially considering garous ready to sabotage power plants whose destruction would harm many lifeforms.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519379#post1519379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 80% of humanity lives in range of that, and the rest of the 20% aren't all self-sustaining communities that can endure without the rest of humanity without massive population loss as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How would that be a problem for impergium adherents? The human population 100 000 years ago, so the period durig which the time of the impergium happened, was of around 10 millions humans.<br /> <br /> So why would the new impergium garou cares about destroying 90 or even 98% of the population? That's litterally their goal!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519379#post1519379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about spirits that rely on humans to exist at all. I'm talking about Heron not wanting all herons to go extinct at the hands of an attempt to genocide humanity, and rallying all the other bird Incarnae against this effort (which shouldn't be hard, Falcon's brood is full of coastal predators that would die off in this scenario too).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What happens when their own patron spirits side against the genocide?</div> </div> </div> </div>And how could they stops the waves? Incarnae of tides are the tides, causing a tsunami is the equivalent of rolling over. If they want to do it, they could do it in an hour all across the world.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Falcon and co cannot stop the spirits of tides to moves, he doesn't have that power, nor would most spirits. There's been wars as old as gaia between elemental spirits, and there's a reason for why none can take over the others, while their nature push them to war, they are unable to vainuish each others.<br /> <br /> As for what happens when your tribe's totem sides against you. Well, if you believes the world is ending unless you do someting your tribe and totem disapproves, you'd be ready to lose their support and even possibly banished from the tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T17:03:40-07:00","id":1519382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519381#post1519381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're talking about werewolf the apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and in a thread specifically about W5 (where the end of the world is not and immediate event where there's no hope and any method is acceptable), and the treatment of an Indigenous author by Paradox, who wanted to use better representation of Indigenous cultures as sources of ways for Garou to more holistically fight the Apocalypse instead of resorting to mass genocide.<br /> <br /> To remind you what thread we're in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's not hard of a stretch that impergium minded garou would consider that sacrificing already doomed species to protect those that can still be saved. </div> </div> </div>The methods you're proposing don't save 99% of multicellular life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would that be a problem for impergium adherents? </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't. But that's why those Garou are idiots at best, and just as bad as the BSDs at a more even handed statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And how could they stops the waves? </div> </div> </div>You're arguing against your own premise. The spirits of the tides aren't of the mind to just wipe out humanity. Someone needs to convince them to do that. If they can be convinced to do it, they could also be convinced not to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T17:24:42-07:00","id":1519383,"title":"","content":"Using the tides would be pretty difficult without chiminage beyond the reach of a splinter faction of Garou. You'd need to rather exactingly scour and reshape the coastal shelves with the aid of Earth spirits first to produce the tidal resonance that you get in locations like the Bay of Fundy.<br /> <br /> But.<br /> <br /> See.<br /> <br /> That's probably something that either BSDs, Balefire Sharks, or Chulorviah are doing. If they're doing it, you probably shouldn't be, unless you're Bringers of Light and trying to infiltrate them so that you can take them down from the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T21:46:16-07:00","id":1519393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519381#post1519381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're talking about werewolf the apocalypse. The world is at an end. These species are already doomed. So it's not hard of a stretch that impergium minded garou would consider that sacrificing already doomed species to protect those that can still be saved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could certainly see pro-Impergium werewolves making that sort of argument. &quot;Do this and 3/4ths of all life on Earth will die. Do nothing and all life will die, or worse, be twisted by the Wyrm and then death would be a blessing.&quot; Of course how accurate that is is questionable, but I don't imagine many werewolves who are interested in restarting the Impergium would let a little thing like facts get in their way. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T23:37:01-07:00","id":1519399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519295#post1519295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently 41.... Werewolf: The Apocalpyse was literally the first RPG I ever played, when I was 12 years old. While it's not my favorite WoD game (That's Mage) It's still special and close to my heart.<br /> <br /> My two favorite tribes have always been &quot;The Get of Fenris&quot; and &quot;The Children of Gaia&quot;, (Odd Dichotomy, I know).<br /> <br /> I loved the Get for two reasons... One, is the 'positive' part of them. The fact the Get were one of the most accepting of Metis (Don't hate the result of the sin) and were very 'progressive' (at least the Good parts of them) in the sense they didn't care who you were, what your gender identity or racial background was... As long as you were Brave, and you fought. I loved that about the Get. The part of them that wasn't tied up in the Nazi stuff (a faction clearly meant to be Villains) but that they were the Tribe that said, &quot;Are you fighting with everything that you have? You're one of us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially with them being the &quot;Germanic&quot; tribe, having them presented with this ideal, your bravery, your willingness to Fight mattered more than anything, was awesome.<br /> <br /> My Great Grandfather was a soldier in the German army during WW2. He was in fact, a &quot;Nazi&quot;. He died, leaving my Great Grandmother a widow, and my Grandfather, fatherless. Towards the end of the war, my Great Grandmother had to hide my Grandfather in the barn to stop the Army from conscripting him to fight a losing battle. The remnants of the army also took the majority of their farm harvest for the war effort, starving them as well.<br /> <br /> When the war was over, my Grandfather came to America, joined the army, and served in the Korean War. When he died, he was given a 21 Gun salute.<br /> <br /> I'm married to a Jewish woman... and someone today literally told me, &quot;Your ancestors are rolling in their grave.&quot; Because of that.<br /> <br /> My Grandfather was a victim of the Nazi regime, and had no love for it. It took his father from him, and made life difficult for his Mother, himself, and his younger brothers.<br /> <br /> The fact the Tribe with the Germanic origins is going to be presented as pure Villains and Nazis is like.... Really, Really, fucking shitty.<br /> <br /> Rather than following the Modern Get whose ranks were more multi-racial, expanding beyond their Germanic origin but keeping their fighting ethos... Rather than having that be the awesome twist that W20 was building to... Yeah, the Germanic Tribe is the one that doesn't care about your Skin Color, Your Sexuality, Your Gender Identity... They just want you to be Brave and to Fight...<br /> <br /> They're just going to be fucking Nazis.<br /> <br /> Yay.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, all the stuff with the Elder Brother and Younger Brother Tribes is shitty too. Werewolf fans would have been more than accommodating in retconning the names)</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more. The whole German/Norse = Nazi vibe is really pushing my buttons. Especially when you remove all the cultural ties in the tribes, but leave this one. It is purposeful and I just don't have words right now to fully describe how I feel about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:12:03-07:00","id":1519415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519399#post1519399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I couldn't agree more. The whole German/Norse = Nazi vibe is really pushing my buttons. Especially when you remove all the cultural ties in the tribes, but leave this one. It is purposeful and I just don't have words right now to fully describe how I feel about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, it's complete bullshit and worse, it's boring.<br /> <br /> &quot;None of the tribes have direct ties to cultures or specific geographic regions. Except for the Get. All of them are now white, germanic aryan neo-nazis.&quot; I don't agree with the idea of turning the Get into NPCs in the first place, but only focusing on white supremacy just turns them into cardboard cutouts and makes it feel like the rest of the world outside of Europe and the US doesn't matter. The reality is, there are racial supremacist groups in many parts of the world. Ethnic supremacists aren't limited to only white neo-nazis. There are places that practice ongoing eugenics (hello North Korea). There are countries in Africa and East Asia where you see genocide being carried out, completely absent of any white germanic neo-Nazis.<br /> <br /> If they decided they wanted to have a tribe that was all about eugenics, racial supremacy and genocide (which I think is stupid in the first place), it would have been more in keeping with Werewolf: the Apocalypse, a game that has always had a heavy focus on non-America/European parts of the world, to include the rest of the world in that tribal concept.<br /> <br /> In the end, the decision to do this with Get was bullshit, but they carried it out in the most boring, hamfisted way possible. What role are the Get going to have if you set a game in or Asia or the Middle East or Africa or South America, places in the world that don't have white supremacist movements? All the other Tribes will be there, but not them, even though the bullshit they're supposed to &quot;represent&quot; is happening in those parts of the world. Basically instead of writing about a tribe that is engaged in the worst actions of humans, and actually looking at how you see those actions carried out in every part of the world, they just took the most easy and lame path, said, &quot;they're Nazis&quot; and then patted themselves on the back and bragged about how mature they were being.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's bullshit. But even worse than being bullshit, it's just boring and needlessly limiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:17:42-07:00","id":1519416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519382#post1519382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A<br /> Yeah, and in a thread specifically about W5 (where the end of the world is not and immediate event where there's no hope and any method is acceptable), and the treatment of an Indigenous author by Paradox, who wanted to use better representation of Indigenous cultures as sources of ways for Garou to more holistically fight the Apocalypse instead of resorting to mass genocide.<br /> <br /> To remind you what thread we're in.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where does that come from? You do relize that the discussion when to the recuring idea of a second impergium since at least three pages?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIf you want to go back to the original topic, you do you. But please don't answer to someone's argument with something enrelated to the argument in question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519382#post1519382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> The methods you're proposing don't save 99% of multicellular life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does that come from (bis)?<br /> Targetted floods on coastal cities wouldn't kill 99% of life. Hell, even the last mass exctinction event only went to around 96% in around 60 000 years according to paleontologists and geologists.<br /> <br /> Even the inland flooding following the end of the last ice age would have been more violent than &quot;all human cities on earth took a tsunami punch in the face.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519382#post1519382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> It wouldn't. But that's why those Garou are idiots at best, and just as bad as the BSDs at a more even handed statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they idiots? The goal of the garou is to save Gaia, who's threated by the Wyrm and the Weaver. And humanity is the main sourve of influence for both of them, with the destruction of Gaia directly linking to both the accelerated progress of humanity's ability to uses space and ressources and our growing number.<br /> <br /> So vastly reducing our numbers is a possible solution to the issue of the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> As for how bad the impergium adherents are, it's disigeneous of you to put them on the same scale as BSDs.<br /> <br /> From a humanistic point of view, both are bad.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b But from a garou perspective, the main focus of morality is Gaia. That's why despite being presented as a general minority (outside of the red talons) garou speaking for a new impergium are wholly member of garou society and the subject is regularly brought during discussions of the future of their fight.<br /> <br /> impergium minded garou are willing to cull humanity as a last resort to save the very soul of life and the planet, which is the only reason of the existence of their species. (And something spirits never berated the garou who practiced the original impergium, and something Gaia must at least approve to a level, otherwise she wouldn't have created the ratkin)<br /> <br /> BSDs on the other side are beig who deliberatly twist their own self by absorbing the essence of everything wrong in existence, wants to kill the world (in a painful way preferrably) and to satisfy their urge to murder, torture, despoil and rape.<br /> <br /> They're not on the same scale at all. Hell, Garou who wants a new impergium are not even on the same scale as Red Talons, whose majority wants to exterminate us purely and simply. (And who are never rejected by gaian spirits or the garou nation despite this genocidal desire).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519382#post1519382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> You're arguing against your own premise. The spirits of the tides aren't of the mind to just wipe out humanity. Someone needs to convince them to do that. If they can be convinced to do it, they could also be convinced not to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that coming from(third)?<br /> <br /> You're answering to me saying Falcon and co don't have the power to stop incarnae of tides even if they wanted with &quot;but the spirits of the tides needs convincing&quot;. Those are two unrelated issues, there's no contradiction between them.<br /> <br /> Plus we know that spirits of the seas are agreeable to the idea of drowing humanity. Since we're talking about W5, a common mention in many news and posts for W5 includes the line (when describing the state of the world) &quot;Sea is rising, devoring more and more land as the poles melt&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if Sea have issue with taking away land with the rising of sea level, it's not a stretch to thing he or his servants are open to the idea of flooding specific areas.<br /> <br /> If anything, from books like the rokea breedbook or Blood Tides, Sea is clearly not described as a friend of mankind.<br /> <br /> Things incarnae of tides would already be doing since tsunamis are an occurence. You would simply ask them to do it on all cities at the same time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:21:43-07:00","id":1519417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519383#post1519383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the tides would be pretty difficult without chiminage beyond the reach of a splinter faction of Garou. You'd need to rather exactingly scour and reshape the coastal shelves with the aid of Earth spirits first to produce the tidal resonance that you get in locations like the Bay of Fundy.<br /> <br /> But.<br /> <br /> See.<br /> <br /> That's probably something that either BSDs, Balefire Sharks, or Chulorviah are doing. If they're doing it, you probably shouldn't be, unless you're Bringers of Light and trying to infiltrate them so that you can take them down from the inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>The desired outcome makes the action not on the level of these charming people you're listing.<br /> <br /> BSDs would rise sea level to destroy the earth more and more. Balefire sharks would do so to expand their territory and corrupt a larger portion of the world, and chulorviah would also do so for territory gain, although since their main tactic is to possess humans, killing humans at large doesn't sound like a ting they would do.<br /> <br /> Imnew impergium garou would try it to save gaia from the weaver and wyrm influence massively allowed by humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:26:22-07:00","id":1519419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519399#post1519399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I couldn't agree more. The whole German/Norse = Nazi vibe is really pushing my buttons. Especially when you remove all the cultural ties in the tribes, but leave this one. It is purposeful and I just don't have words right now to fully describe how I feel about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. That's some terrible this that W5 writers seems to forget. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIf &quot;the Get had some nazi in their ranks, so we'll make them ennemies since people would associate them with nazis due to this past splinter faction&quot; wav always the reason, which seems likely, then the message sent is awfully like &quot;the german had nazis as a defining moment of their recent history, so everything german would be associated with nazis&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bDoubly terrible when, as you just said, they cut most if not all cultural ties of the past editions. And triply terrible in an ironic way when they patted themselves on trying to undo cultural insensibility with the native american tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:51:57-07:00","id":1519437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1518517#post1518517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine it's 2030, WOD5E is supposed to end and the creative team is looking for a concept. Then one cool guy is like &quot;Get this...&quot;. He stands up, walks to the whiteboard and writes WOD5. He looks around the room and says &quot;Now watch this...&quot;. He erases the 5 - and replaces it with... &quot;40th&quot;. &quot;The new edition is called World of Darkness 40th Anniversary Edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, we're at a point where I've come to the conclusion that the best way to do WoD6 is just fully retcon all of the setting and mechanical changes from 5th Edition and revert back to the metaplot-neutral X20 settings in a hard reset (maybe with a few minor changes to adjust to the tech differences between the early 2010's when V20 was released to whenever WoD6 could be released) and even do a big press release and a media push that amounts to the RPG version of this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YpYrWWL_XyU\" data-code=\"YpYrWWL_XyU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YpYrWWL_XyU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Just go full hard reset and declare Beckett's Jyhad Diary and all of WoD5 non-canon, be it V5, W5, H5, or any of the other 5th Edition lines that might be in the pipeline. Maybe they can keep it around as an alternate &quot;What If?&quot; setting to be supported by the Storytellers Vault so V5 fans can still make what they want but that's it.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I doubt Paradox would ever do something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:58:47-07:00","id":1519440,"title":"","content":"The pdf came out, look at this... such a sharp rusted-tipped irony<br /> <br /> &quot;Every werewolf makes a journey on which they come to<br /> understand the world in the Garou way. As their senses<br /> sharpen, they also acquire an understanding of what\u2019s<br /> happening in the world, why it\u2019s important, and how to<br /> interpret new information about it. They learn to disregard the well-paid PR flacks justifying the unjustifiable<br /> and to listen to those voices speaking about Gaia with<br /> the same urgency the Garou themselves feel, whether it<br /> comes from scientists, activists, or indigenous people.<br /> Eventually this path leads to a view that the world<br /> is in a catastrophic state and the time to act may have<br /> passed. This generation of Garou dwells in the midst of<br /> Apocalypse. It\u2019s too late to avert the end.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> page 10 (12); Welcome to a Dying World sector <br /> <br /> <br /> Man... I wasn't expecting to such a paradox to hit so freaking soon and so hard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:09:14-07:00","id":1519443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519437#post1519437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, we're at a point where I've come to the conclusion that the best way to do WoD6 is just fully retcon all of the setting and mechanical changes from 5th Edition and revert back to the metaplot-neutral X20 settings in a hard reset (maybe with a few minor changes to adjust to the tech differences between the early 2010's when V20 was released to whenever WoD6 could be released) and even do a big press release and a media push that amounts to the RPG version of this...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but getting rid of the changes to the core system are a pretty bad move, it's just better than the X20 system. Rolling back the Rage/Hunger rules, or at least making them them les spunishing, and tweaking default target numbers is almost a necessity (particularly if they want to do a Hunter #the Viliging '6e') but the core rules are fine. Moving to Storytelling or Storypath would be even better, but I don't see that happening (particularly the latter).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind a rollback to a split between Merits and Backgrounds, if only because not having one makes it too easy to have characters with no ties to the world. Or maybe something like the Paths from Storypath that deal with what Backgrounds did in a much looser way.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise, I think we'll either see a soft rollback (and we'll all pretend the pyramid never splintered...) or a third World of Darkness. I don't think we'll see a full reset, but who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:23:11-07:00","id":1519446,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the actual topic. Am I the only one ticked off by today's design journal? After Mr. Sambrano's heartfelt expose this really feels...ick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Points of Origin</b><br /> Our goal for this Werewolf reboot was a bold separation from previous editions. Work was done early on by various contributors to help us create this separation, and that work became foundational for the 5th edition. However, we realized that the best way to accomplish this goal was to bring everything in-house, under our creative team\u2019s vision. We engaged a large team of writers and consultants from diverse backgrounds to make sure Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th Edition represents sensitive topics with care. Indigenous writers in particular were present in the writing process from the outline stage, and took part in the development both as consultants and writers.<br /> <br /> <b>Key Intentions</b><br /> World of Darkness 5th Edition presents its character groups with a focus on regional and individual traits, not as monolithic organizations with identical backgrounds and views. This applies as much to the tribes of Werewolf as it does to Kindred and Hunters. You can be a trans Black Fury, Indigenous American Silent Strider or Namibian Silver Fang, because the tribes in W5 are no longer fused to any one particular culture, gender or geographic region. Most importantly, you can enjoy playing each tribe no matter where you are from. You needn\u2019t worry about being locked into playing a particular \u201ctype\u201d based on your or your character\u2019s origin, or misrepresenting or appropriating another culture through your tribe choice.<br /> <br /> This, however, does not remove real world cultures from Werewolf: The Apocalypse. The game Werewolf is set in our modern world, and many of its themes reflect struggles of indigenous, unprivileged, and/or climate change-affected communities worldwide. The writers took care to highlight the visceral and rage-fueled response to these injustices, and didn\u2019t shy away from direct references to real world issues.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:56:45-07:00","id":1519458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519446#post1519446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the actual topic. Am I the only one ticked off by today's design journal? After Mr. Sambrano's heartfelt expose this really feels...ick.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What they meant by &quot;This, however, does not remove real world cultures from Werewolf: The Apocalypse.&quot; is that W5 tells readers &quot;This is a diverse game... aaand that's all we have to say. You go figure out the rest.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:32:08-07:00","id":1519463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519417#post1519417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The desired outcome makes the action not on the level of these charming people you're listing.<br /> <br /> BSDs would rise sea level to destroy the earth more and more. Balefire sharks would do so to expand their territory and corrupt a larger portion of the world, and chulorviah would also do so for territory gain, although since their main tactic is to possess humans, killing humans at large doesn't sound like a ting they would do.<br /> <br /> Imnew impergium garou would try it to save gaia from the weaver and wyrm influence massively allowed by humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty words if you can't control the end result. Also, the Chulorviah are enacting a long-term plan that's nebulous and may involve flooding the land so that it's more hospitable to them; the entire reason that they possessed someone to get Project: Deep Water moving is because it allowed them freer access to more people. They could probably make a deal with all of the people who are in the path of the onlap; they could whisper that they have the solution. The hypothetical pro-Impergium faction, here, would be playing right into their arms and tentacles; not only are they doing the work of the Chulorviah for them, the Chulorviah get a PR bonanza in that <i>they weren't the ones at fault</i>. They can just point to the Garou and say &quot;They did it&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it'll be 100% true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:36:57-07:00","id":1519464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519458#post1519458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What they meant by &quot;This, however, does not remove real world cultures from Werewolf: The Apocalypse.&quot; is that W5 tells readers &quot;This is a diverse game... aaand that's all we have to say. You go figure out the rest.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the game still has cultural ties, just by the myths/legends it decides to draw from. This is why stuff like the CofD books giving specific examples of the splats in other cultures is important, because the games tend to skew towards non-Indigenous American and European cultural ties. The presented 'default' Courts in 2e Lost are still the European Seasonal Courts, which ties the game as presented to certain parts of the world (although Changeling as a whole is pretty good at giving alternative social splats).<br /> <br /> Maybe W5 will be similar and they've got big plans to showcase how the Tribes adapt to different cultures in supplements, ideally helmed by members of those cultures. Although if I believed that I'd have invested in Lunar real estate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:38:05-07:00","id":1519465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519443#post1519443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but getting rid of the changes to the core system are a pretty bad move, it's just better than the X20 system. Rolling back the Rage/Hunger rules, or at least making them them les spunishing, and tweaking default target numbers is almost a necessity (particularly if they want to do a Hunter #the Viliging '6e') but the core rules are fine. Moving to Storytelling or Storypath would be even better, but I don't see that happening (particularly the latter).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind a rollback to a split between Merits and Backgrounds, if only because not having one makes it too easy to have characters with no ties to the world. Or maybe something like the Paths from Storypath that deal with what Backgrounds did in a much looser way.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise, I think we'll either see a soft rollback (and we'll all pretend the pyramid never splintered...) or a third World of Darkness. I don't think we'll see a full reset, but who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate the WoD 5th edition so very much I couldn't disagree with you more. Blood dice and Rage Dice are so freaking clunky as mechanics compared to the pure simplicity of a spending system. Capping every single attribute and ability at 5 dots led to Underwhelming Vampire Elders that could get destroyed by a gang of mortals with some guns. It's also why the Shifting system and alternate forms are so inelegant in 5th edition Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Not to mention all the shit they just stole from Chronicles of Darkness and shoe-horned in.<br /> <br /> I'm sure we could clean up the Classic WoD system further... but the direction 5th edition took is a branch that needs to pruned and forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:43:42-07:00","id":1519468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519464#post1519464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet the game still has cultural ties, just by the myths/legends it decides to draw from. This is why stuff like the CofD books giving specific examples of the splats in other cultures is important, because the games tend to skew towards non-Indigenous American and European cultural ties. The presented 'default' Courts in 2e Lost are still the European Seasonal Courts, which ties the game as presented to certain parts of the world (although Changeling as a whole is pretty good at giving alternative social splats).<br /> <br /> Maybe W5 will be similar and they've got big plans to showcase how the Tribes adapt to different cultures in supplements, ideally helmed by members of those cultures. Although if I believed that I'd have invested in Lunar real estate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they talked about it last October how supplements would delve into the regional variants of Tribes. But the approach to diversity and human culture is kinda expressed by this sidebar on &quot;Spirit Veracity&quot;, I think:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures. Through the Garou lens, all of them are true, all of them are \u201cthe\u201d Horned Serpent, even if all of them are different. The same reasoning stands for Gorgon, the common interpretation of whom is decidedly Greek\u2026 or even the inchoate Fenris\u2026.\u200b </div> </div> </div>So in the core book, it's more like the WtF-Tribes in how they are Garou-specific but also universal in how they're connected to human culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:53:12-07:00","id":1519472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519443#post1519443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but getting rid of the changes to the core system are a pretty bad move, it's just better than the X20 system. Rolling back the Rage/Hunger rules, or at least making them them les spunishing, and tweaking default target numbers is almost a necessity (particularly if they want to do a Hunter #the Viliging '6e') but the core rules are fine. Moving to Storytelling or Storypath would be even better, but I don't see that happening (particularly the latter).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind a rollback to a split between Merits and Backgrounds, if only because not having one makes it too easy to have characters with no ties to the world. Or maybe something like the Paths from Storypath that deal with what Backgrounds did in a much looser way.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise, I think we'll either see a soft rollback (and we'll all pretend the pyramid never splintered...) or a third World of Darkness. I don't think we'll see a full reset, but who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the Rage mechanic will be better if the chance to enter in frenzy it's not ruled but how much Rage the character have, but the character's aupicious and the moon phase? Or a combination of both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:43:22-07:00","id":1519485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can be a trans Black Fury, Indigenous American Silent Strider or Namibian Silver Fang, </div> </div> </div>Yep, and that has been the case since circa 2000.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:57:45-07:00","id":1519486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519440#post1519440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pdf came out, look at this... such a sharp rusted-tipped irony<br /> <br /> &quot;Every werewolf makes a journey on which they come to<br /> understand the world in the Garou way. As their senses<br /> sharpen, they also acquire an understanding of what\u2019s<br /> happening in the world, why it\u2019s important, and how to<br /> interpret new information about it. They learn to disregard the well-paid PR flacks justifying the unjustifiable<br /> and to listen to those voices speaking about Gaia with<br /> the same urgency the Garou themselves feel, whether it<br /> comes from scientists, activists, or indigenous people.<br /> Eventually this path leads to a view that the world<br /> is in a catastrophic state and the time to act may have<br /> passed. This generation of Garou dwells in the midst of<br /> Apocalypse. It\u2019s too late to avert the end.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> page 10 (12); Welcome to a Dying World sector<br /> <br /> <br /> Man... I wasn't expecting to such a paradox to hit so freaking soon and so hard</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's such a stupid paradox that it hurts. So every werewolf will inevitably learn how to disregard &quot;PR justifying the unjustifiable&quot; and &quot;how to interpret new information&quot;.<br /> <br /> Theeeeeeeeen, dear W5 writers, how do you justify the way you portrayed the Fenrir? Or the BSD? Because if this paragraph is true, garou should inevitably learn to avoid bad ideas and know what is actually important.<br /> <br /> So that means that no garou are ever going to have bad ideas or triffle uselessly about matters unrelated to the well being of the world.<br /> <br /> Yep, the garou are now all ultra wise beig in becoming, and the actions of even the worst tribes and camps will by definition be justified since they now disregard &quot;PR flacks justifying the unjustifyable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, why would garou ever listen to activists? Their culture knows, on a scale impossible to touch for mundane human, the state of the world since their origin. Listening to, say, a climate activist would be like listening to someone trying to explain to you how physics works after one high school class while you're a nobel prize winner with 50 years of advanced research on the field.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It seems that despite officially not being whitewolf any longuer, the authors of parawolf have not lost their obsession with walls of texts appeared Deep(tm) but in the end totally void of meaning for the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 08-02-2023, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:02:35-07:00","id":1519488,"title":"","content":"&quot;Garou learn to disregard well-paid PR flacks...&quot;<br /> <br /> Indeed. Let's get metatextual and turn this paper pulp into a more useful book, shall we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:37:48-07:00","id":1519493,"title":"","content":"While I like the game system, this is irrelevant to this thread, and all cultural elements has been entirely wiped out. Just as has been prophesized. <br /> I just can't understand. (ok, there are rational and materialistic reasons for corporations to be this shit; and that is why they must end)<br /> <br /> Why not call a feminist to write Black Furries. Someone with Ngo or syndicate background to write Children of Gaia. An ecology activist writer for Red Talons. .... and you know... an indigenous writer for the erased native-american tribes that were??? <br /> Damn, it was the perfect edition for this sort of diversity and affirmation. But nan, mediocrity for the Tribes<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:41:54-07:00","id":1519494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519493#post1519493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like the game system, this is irrelevant to this thread, and all cultural elements has been entirely wiped out. Just as has been prophesized.<br /> I just can't understand. (ok, there are rational and materialistic reasons for corporations to be this shit; and that is why they must end)<br /> <br /> Why not call a feminist to write Black Furries. Someone with Ngo or syndicate background to write Children of Gaia. An ecology activist writer for Red Talons. .... and you know... an indigenous writer for the erased native-american tribes that were???<br /> Damn, it was the perfect edition for this sort of diversity and affirmation. But nan, mediocrity for the Tribes</div> </div> </div> </div>Re. the system. I'm getting a few H5 flashbacks, a lot of it doesn't seem to hang together very well and it seems a large percentage of the heavy lifting to make the system function has been foisted off onto individual STs. Especially the way Rage interacts with almost every subsystem in negative ways that can only be mitigated in specific circumstances........strikes me as unfun to play and kind of a nightmare to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:57:32-07:00","id":1519498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519440#post1519440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pdf came out, look at this... such a sharp rusted-tipped irony<br /> <br /> &quot;Every werewolf makes a journey on which they come to<br /> understand the world in the Garou way. As their senses<br /> sharpen, they also acquire an understanding of what\u2019s<br /> happening in the world, why it\u2019s important, and how to<br /> interpret new information about it. They learn to disregard the well-paid PR flacks justifying the unjustifiable<br /> and to listen to those voices speaking about Gaia with<br /> the same urgency the Garou themselves feel, whether it<br /> comes from scientists, activists, or indigenous people.<br /> Eventually this path leads to a view that the world<br /> is in a catastrophic state and the time to act may have<br /> passed. This generation of Garou dwells in the midst of<br /> Apocalypse. It\u2019s too late to avert the end.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> page 10 (12); Welcome to a Dying World sector<br /> <br /> <br /> Man... I wasn't expecting to such a paradox to hit so freaking soon and so hard</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the stupid, it hurts.<br /> <br /> So now garou will inevitably dismiss &quot;PR flacks justifying the unjustifiable&quot; and know how to &quot;interpret new information&quot;<br /> <br /> Theeeeeeeen, dear W5 writers, how do you justify your depictio of the Fenrir as being extremists? Aren't they supposed, as garou, to know not to listen to those justifying the unjustifiable?<br /> <br /> I guess now garou's misshaps, lacks of comprehension of situations no longuer exist, since they'll inevitably learn to interpre. New information.<br /> <br /> <br /> And why would garou listen to activists? They know, on a level that no mundane human can touch, how the world fares. Listening to a climate activist wouod be like listening to someone trying to teach you physics after having an hour log middle school class while you're a nobel prize with 50 years of research in the field.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seems that for all the talk about parawolf not being whitewolf anymore, their writers sure kept the habit of making pseudo profound textwalls which makes no sense with the setting described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:22:16-07:00","id":1519502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>damian may</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519494#post1519494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> re. The system. I'm getting a few h5 flashbacks, a lot of it doesn't seem to hang together very well and it seems a large percentage of the heavy lifting to make the system function has been foisted off onto individual sts. Especially the way rage interacts with almost every subsystem in negative ways that can only be mitigated in specific circumstances........strikes me as unfun to play and kind of a nightmare to run.</div> </div> </div> </div>angst! Angst! Angst! Are you angsting yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:44:18-07:00","id":1519508,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Orphan81;n1519465]I hate the WoD 5th edition so very much I couldn't disagree with you more.[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Congrats on recognising your bioas! But to rephrease my point, the core mechanical system (ignoring the supernatural powers and traits directly associated with those) works better. As in how dice are rolled and interpreted (but it probably needs more iteration to get the numbers dowqn).<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]Blood dice and Rage Dice are so freaking clunky as mechanics compared to the pure simplicity of a spending system[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd probably scrap Hunger and go back to Blood Pool, but keep the concept of Rage Dice. They definitely need a reworking, I'd probably make it a case of players choosing to <i>add them to dice pools </i>at the risk of a brutal outcomed. But I'd probably also get rid of the Rage Check, bring back Gnosis, and do some more tweaking.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly more annoyed by the lack of Gnosis than how Rage works in W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Capping every single attribute and ability at 5 dots led to Underwhelming Vampire Elders that could get destroyed by a gang of mortals with some guns </div> </div> </div>That's a matter of opinion, and I honesty don't get all the cdomplaining about the lack of 'elder powers'. Oh look, it's a bunch of powers most players are nerver going to touch, what a wonderful usew of book space.... Honestly returning to the way Blood Pool used to work with V5's blood boost rules would solve a lot of those issues.<br /> <br /> The oWoD system also has issues with the fuzzy stat cap for mortals (it's not 5, but that seejms to be the intent, and some NPCs break that cap).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also why the Shifting system and alternate forms are so inelegant in 5th edition Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Not really part of the core rules, but they're not that much worse than those in W20 or Forsaken 2e. I also see nothing terribly wrong with the forms, barring Glabro not getting some version of Badass Motherfucker and Crinos being discount Gauru. Slightly simplified, but WoD5 wants to be mechnically simpler than WoD20 and everything about the forms will pretty much work as intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention all the shit they just stole from Chronicles of Darkness and shoe-horned in. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, rip out Blood Potency and that lot. Doesn't really change the core mechanics being sound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure we could clean up the Classic WoD system further... but the direction 5th edition took is a branch that needs to pruned and forgotten. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but why do that when WoD5 presents a more functional set of core mechanica? Hell if they really do kill off CofD they might just switch WoD6 to the Storytelling system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519472#post1519472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think the Rage mechanic will be better if the chance to enter in frenzy it's not ruled but how much Rage the character have, but the character's aupicious and the moon phase? Or a combination of both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combination of both with Willpower. Basing it on Rage loosely ties it with Auspice anyway pre-W5, and in W5 characters are going to be lashing out often anyway so is there really a need to occasionally force them into the combat forms to destroy stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T14:12:35-07:00","id":1519512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519443#post1519443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but getting rid of the changes to the core system are a pretty bad move, it's just better than the X20 system. Rolling back the Rage/Hunger rules, or at least making them them les spunishing, and tweaking default target numbers is almost a necessity (particularly if they want to do a Hunter #the Viliging '6e') but the core rules are fine. Moving to Storytelling or Storypath would be even better, but I don't see that happening (particularly the latter).</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree on the 5th Edition mechanics being better than X20 but I wouldn't mind a Storytelling version of the X20 lines (yeah, I know about the conversion guides)<br /> <br /> The setting changes are what irk me the most. I know we won't see a hard reset/retcon of that fluff barring a very drastic change in ownership of the IP but that probably won't happen either. Ah well, I'm just gonna vote with my wallet and not waste any money on W5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T14:49:23-07:00","id":1519513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519512#post1519512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I respectfully disagree on the 5th Edition mechanics being better than X20 but I wouldn't mind a Storytelling version of the X20 lines (yeah, I know about the conversion guides)</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of doesn't help that the Werewolf guide doesn't give advice for converting the Apocalypse Tribes into Forsaken Tribes and instead focuses on interpretting them as Lodges. Which is fine, but I kinf of wantred to have the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The setting changes are what irk me the most. I know we won't see a hard reset/retcon of that fluff barring a very drastic change in ownership of the IP but that probably won't happen either. Ah well, I'm just gonna vote with my wallet and not waste any money on W5. </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm very much not buying W% for similar reasons (it began with changing the Glass Walker patron from Cockroach and just got worse with every new fluff reveal). It annoys me even more that it means we probably won't get more Forsaken 2e material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:33:13-07:00","id":1519536,"title":"","content":"I got in the forum today after seeing the post on the World of Darkness site about the release.<br /> My irritation was rather high after reading the post on that site.<br /> It left a bad taste in my mouth.<br /> There was this idea in that article that getting rid of any cultural ties for the Tribes was objectively a good thing because this way &quot;You needn\u2019t worry about being locked into playing a particular \u201ctype\u201d based on your or your character\u2019s origin, or misrepresenting or appropriating another culture through your tribe choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I took as if normally I should worry if I wanted to play a Native American or any other culture or ethnicity character that wasn't my RL one.<br /> And also that I really really shouldn't to begin with, because that would be risk of misrepresenting or appropriating I should worry about...<br /> By this logic since I'm Italian I should only ever play Italians and say nay to any person that wants to play Italians at my table that aren't Italians because they wouldn't play them right.<br /> And here I was, thinking that RPGs were all about taking a role that isn't yourself in RL...<br /> <br /> But I digress.<br /> I just wanted to write that I'm sorry that Sambrano had to go through all that. Sambrano sounded like a reasonable person, one that aknowledged that even if the '90s version had objective flaws it still did good in a lot of ways because the message and the themes were there even if in a flawed way. Which was a good attitude and starting point, if you ask me.<br /> But while I'm sorry, I'm also glad that Sambrano took time to write down all that and put the events out in the open.<br /> And I'm happy for this.<br /> <br /> It lowered my personal irritation a bit. Because now that it's in the open, I hope it helps a few folks understand that avoiding any cultural ties is the shortsighted, boring, not-nuanced, uncool, easy and cowardly way to go<br /> It reminds me of an article about qipao becoming fashionable was wrong because it was cultural appropriation, then the same article reported that asian fashion designers were favourable about it but the article concluded that it was wrong and cultural appropriation anyway regardless of what asian designers said. Priceless. White Knighting intesifies, I'd say<br /> <br /> Once my sister said that cultures are meant to be shared and spread.<br /> This fear of cultural appropriation is taking a turn for the worse.<br /> I'm not from USA and one of the things that stimulated me in researching more proper knowledge on Native Americans in my life was WtA.<br /> But I guess I had the bare minimum of intelligence to not trust a game in educating me on real world stuff, and went for more serious sources.<br /> And don't get me started on how much new stuff about the real world and far away cultures and countries and religions I learned just thanks to a few throwaway names in MtAs used in an improper way...<br /> I guess for the time being we'll have less teenagers stimulated in researching about real life cultures by random and flawed notions about real cultures in their games, for fear that they could take those notions without a grain of salt<br /> <br /> I was almost convinced about buying the book, since WtA meant so much for me in the past.<br /> But this behind-the-scenes dispelled any uncertainity I had.<br /> This W5 edition can burn in hell for all I care.<br /> <br /> Edition Wars don't help the hobby and don't help selling books or having a stable community, so I must suppose Paradox didn't learn anything from the last 20 years of the hobby. Sambrano's team sounded like they learned that lesson at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:10:28-07:00","id":1519546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519536#post1519536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which I took as if normally I should worry if I wanted to play a Native American or any other culture or ethnicity character that wasn't my RL one.<br /> And also that I really really shouldn't to begin with, because that would be risk of misrepresenting or appropriating I should worry about...<br /> By this logic since I'm Italian I should only ever play Italians and say nay to any person that wants to play Italians at my table that aren't Italians because they wouldn't play them right.<br /> And here I was, thinking that RPGs were all about taking a role that isn't yourself in RL...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one case where it does matter, and not really comparable with other people playing Italians. Kind of the inverse of that litter commercial that you might have seen playing in the US with the crying American Indian... who was played by an Italian dude. Those roles take a great deal more information and time spent with the people in question, and if they're not okay with it, it's probably not a good idea. You might just end up playing and perpetuating a stereotype in spite of your best efforts, and there's already been too much of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:16:24-07:00","id":1519548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519536#post1519536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got in the forum today after seeing the post on the World of Darkness site about the release.<br /> My irritation was rather high after reading the post on that site.<br /> It left a bad taste in my mouth.<br /> There was this idea in that article that getting rid of any cultural ties for the Tribes was objectively a good thing because this way &quot;You needn\u2019t worry about being locked into playing a particular \u201ctype\u201d based on your or your character\u2019s origin, or misrepresenting or appropriating another culture through your tribe choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I took as if normally I should worry if I wanted to play a Native American or any other culture or ethnicity character that wasn't my RL one.<br /> And also that I really really shouldn't to begin with, because that would be risk of misrepresenting or appropriating I should worry about...<br /> By this logic since I'm Italian I should only ever play Italians and say nay to any person that wants to play Italians at my table that aren't Italians because they wouldn't play them right.<br /> And here I was, thinking that RPGs were all about taking a role that isn't yourself in RL...<br /> <br /> But I digress.<br /> I just wanted to write that I'm sorry that Sambrano had to go through all that. Sambrano sounded like a reasonable person, one that aknowledged that even if the '90s version had objective flaws it still did good in a lot of ways because the message and the themes were there even if in a flawed way. Which was a good attitude and starting point, if you ask me.<br /> But while I'm sorry, I'm also glad that Sambrano took time to write down all that and put the events out in the open.<br /> And I'm happy for this.<br /> <br /> It lowered my personal irritation a bit. Because now that it's in the open, I hope it helps a few folks understand that avoiding any cultural ties is the shortsighted, boring, not-nuanced, uncool, easy and cowardly way to go<br /> It reminds me of an article about qipao becoming fashionable was wrong because it was cultural appropriation, then the same article reported that asian fashion designers were favourable about it but the article concluded that it was wrong and cultural appropriation anyway regardless of what asian designers said. Priceless. White Knighting intesifies, I'd say<br /> <br /> Once my sister said that cultures are meant to be shared and spread.<br /> This fear of cultural appropriation is taking a turn for the worse.<br /> I'm not from USA and one of the things that stimulated me in researching more proper knowledge on Native Americans in my life was WtA.<br /> But I guess I had the bare minimum of intelligence to not trust a game in educating me on real world stuff, and went for more serious sources.<br /> And don't get me started on how much new stuff about the real world and far away cultures and countries and religions I learned just thanks to a few throwaway names in MtAs used in an improper way...<br /> I guess for the time being we'll have less teenagers stimulated in researching about real life cultures by random and flawed notions about real cultures in their games, for fear that they could take those notions without a grain of salt<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't like this comment enought. The whole fear about cultural appropriation may have started from a place of goodwill and compassion, but it has derailled into an hypocritical belief tainting any entertainement or fashion industries.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I can't help but believe that the lines you quote from the article (&quot;You needn\u2019t worry about being locked into playing a particular \u201ctype\u201d based on your or your character\u2019s origin, or misrepresenting or appropriating another culture through your tribe choice.&quot;<br /> Show a certain disconnect between writters and players. <br /> <br /> It may be due to the culture from which writers at these companies come from, but their idea that players would worry about &quot;appropriating&quot; another culture does not correlate with the many groups of ttrpg that I played with, discussed with or simply talked to IRL or online across the last two decades.<br /> <br /> Players typically don't care, and want to play what they find interesting as a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T23:51:32-07:00","id":1519565,"title":"","content":"It seems to reflect the mindset they had with v5 were they proudly rooted that you could play say.....a tzmisce noddist scholar is the carmarilla with the clans as more archeotypes and ultimately-character classes.<br /> The trouble is that this outlook relies on stripping so much lore and depth from the setting that this option is ultimately meaningless. If you can play a Sabbat style tzmisce noddist in either of the other two sects what does this say about the ivory tower or the anarchs or the clans? Same logic applies I can theoretically play a first nation ghost counci but it's ultimately a largely cosmetic choice since I could just as easily play a wasp whose racist and rich.<br /> <br /> If anybody can be a fianna no one really is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T00:56:20-07:00","id":1519573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519546#post1519546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one case where it does matter, and not really comparable with other people playing Italians. Kind of the inverse of that litter commercial that you might have seen playing in the US with the crying American Indian... who was played by an Italian dude. Those roles take a great deal more information and time spent with the people in question, and if they're not okay with it, it's probably not a good idea. You might just end up playing and perpetuating a stereotype in spite of your best efforts, and there's already been too much of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very american view. But considering that stereotyping X group matters when doing the same for group Y does not is a pretty alien concept across the western world outside of usa/canada.<br /> <br /> We're talking about ttrpg. Typically done by a group of friends around a table. Sterotyping a fictional character that will only be brought up in that context doesn't propagate some sort of disease-like mortal mind pathogen.<br /> <br /> People in ttrpg have always played everything and everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:25:25-07:00","id":1519587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519546#post1519546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one case where it does matter, and not really comparable with other people playing Italians. Kind of the inverse of that litter commercial that you might have seen playing in the US with the crying American Indian... who was played by an Italian dude. Those roles take a great deal more information and time spent with the people in question, and if they're not okay with it, it's probably not a good idea. You might just end up playing and perpetuating a stereotype in spite of your best efforts, and there's already been too much of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it different? I mean <i>I</i> shouldn't be playing a Native American, I know next to nothing about their cultures and have little motivation to learn*, but that also means I probably shouldn't be playing a Korean or Nigerian character (French I can probably work with, I feel culturally closer to them than the US).<br /> <br /> Yes there's an additional history of oppression and erasure to deal with, but every culture has their nuances and difficulties.<br /> <br /> * I also tend not to use the Pure Tribes, partially for that reason and partially because despite people's insistence I live in Yurp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:15:57-07:00","id":1519594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519546#post1519546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one case where it does matter, and not really comparable with other people playing Italians.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a friggin' example, not a comparation!<br /> I live in Italy, I didn't live through the stigma many italians lived through in USA but certaintly I didn't try to compare the two things.<br /> I don't mean to minimize or dismiss their personal struggles, but for sure they weren't genocided and kept alive in &quot;reservations&quot; like it was a big favour to them. On this we can agree upon. It's absolutely not the same thing.<br /> I was just using it as an example that I thought it would be good enough to be within the context, since there is silly stereotyping of italians in all entertainment industry. But I suppose it's not a good enough example for you\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it different? I mean <i>I</i> shouldn't be playing a Native American, I know next to nothing about their cultures and have little motivation to learn*, but that also means I probably shouldn't be playing a Korean or Nigerian character (French I can probably work with, I feel culturally closer to them than the US).<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div> Why? Who are you damaging exactly? Who are you wronging with playing &quot;let's pretend&quot; at your own gaming table?<br /> I must assume you'll never like to play in a game about samurai in feudal Japan because you're not Japanese?<br /> Maybe putting yourself in different shoes can be useful, even if it's made in a &quot;wrong&quot; way.<br /> Should I never play a female character because I'm male and I would probably perpetuate bad stereotypes even in an unintentional way?<br /> Or it might help me discover something about myself, just like sometimes it happens to professional actors?<br /> <br /> This conversation reminds me of the players in fantasy games that always play humans because it's the only species they are able to feel comfortable with.<br /> The world needs more imagination in order to think that a different world is possible, and it needs that we exercise the ability to put ourselves in the different shoes of our fellow human beings way way way way more than we normally do.<br /> Certainly the world doesn't need that we exercise more about wearing our usual clothes.<br /> <br /> And yeah sorry I'm talking BIG now and basically ranting and rumbling, but Werewolf was a game meant to be talking about something BIG and IMPORTANT in a puerile yet strong way. Something that given what's happening today in our real world it's not have been talked about enough. It wasn't meant ot be some vague crap of &quot;who knows really? take a guess, everyone guesses, nobody is sure, do what you want&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:01:54-07:00","id":1519609,"title":"","content":"As long as you do some basic groundwork and keep it respectful I don't have any issue playing other people's. I've played Muslims, Greeks, men and Americans so it'd be bit weird if first nation people where off limits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T07:12:42-07:00","id":1519628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519594#post1519594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Who are you damaging exactly? Who are you wronging with playing &quot;let's pretend&quot; at your own gaming table?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of home games? Lack of confidence with the material.<br /> <br /> But I've also played games in public spaces (it was actually easier at uni than having anybody host). In such cases it's best to be respectful to onlookers <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must assume you'll never like to play in a game about samurai in feudal Japan because you're not Japanese? </div> </div> </div>About reason number 38 on the list. Number 14 is 'seriously, fuck katana'.<br /> <br /> OTOH I do know slightly more about Japan than Native American cultures. And I'd really want to research it more before playing such a game (or China for a Wuxia game), otherwise we might just have picked up Big Eyes Small Mouth <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe putting yourself in different shoes can be useful, even if it's made in a &quot;wrong&quot; way.<br /> Should I never play a female character because I'm male and I would probably perpetuate bad stereotypes even in an unintentional way? </div> </div> </div>That one's <i>very</i> dependent on group, I've been in ones where crossplaying was standard and others with a policy of 'we'd rather not deal with potential embarrassment' (all mixed gender and adults, so that's not an issue).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or it might help me discover something about myself, just like sometimes it happens to professional actors? </div> </div> </div>Then that's cool! Personally it just helped me reinforce an eggshell <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This conversation reminds me of the players in fantasy games that always play humans because it's the only species they are able to feel comfortable with. </div> </div> </div>Hello!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world needs more imagination in order to think that a different world is possible, and it needs that we exercise the ability to put ourselves in the different shoes of our fellow human beings way way way way more than we normally do.<br /> Certainly the world doesn't need that we exercise more about wearing our usual clothes. </div> </div> </div>The world also needs people who'll go 'I'll only play a caricature, maybe I should research or change my concept'. It's not really putting myself in their shoes if I can barely manage the theme park version <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah sorry I'm talking BIG now and basically ranting and rumbling, but Werewolf was a game meant to be talking about something BIG and IMPORTANT in a puerile yet strong way. Something that given what's happening today in our real world it's not have been talked about enough. It wasn't meant ot be some vague crap of &quot;who knows really? take a guess, everyone guesses, nobody is sure, do what you want&quot; </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'd much rather have the ethnically aligned Tribes if you're going to be shouting about representation. Make them cool and dare me to do the fucking research.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm trying to remember what the original cultural ties of the BG, CoG, and GWs are supposed to be. I'm fairly certain that the GW were originally associated with the Fertile Cresent and the societies that rose there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T08:39:14-07:00","id":1519634,"title":"","content":"Regarding cultural appropriation and playing characters outside of your own ethnic group, I think there are a couple of points that need to be considered. And I definitely think that the conversation needs to be prefaced with the fact that this is a <i><b>complicated</b></i> subject, that I really think tends to work best when approached on a case-by-case basis rather than trying to come up with sweeping principles you can apply without regard to context.<br /> <br /> I think the first issue is to discuss what is meant by the term &quot;cultural appropriation.&quot; I've seen it used in two or three different ways, with distinctions that determine whether or not is an inherently negative phenomenon, versus a more neutral and context-dependent one. The first sense is one which uses &quot;appropriation&quot; rather aggressively, and is inherently negative. This is not about cultural sharing, but cultural theft and commodification. This is forcefully taking a piece of a culture you were never part of, twisting it and maiming it however you wish to make it into what you want, and then maybe throwing a price-tag onto it at the end. It's inherently disrespectful. And it becomes even worse when the things you start taking without permission are sacred (or profane) to the people you took it from.<br /> <br /> The second usage of the term I've encountered uses &quot;cultural appropriation&quot; simply to refer to the exchange of cultural ideas and values in any context, and thus whether or not it is positive or negative depends on that context. The sort of stuff discussed above is still wrong, obviously, but it leaves room for cultural exchange that can be regarded as more positive, or at least neutral. But even that gets messy sometimes; <a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bbcthree/article/10f9450a-ab94-4481-bffe-0d6568ae1bf0\" target=\"_blank\">pineapple on pizza has actually become a topic of international diplomacy.</a> So, to move this to the context of W5, whether or not it gets to be the good kind of cultural appropriation or not depends on whether or not that sharing is consensual and respectful. And thus far, that does not look to be the case.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that this is one of the many things where it's not good to become puritanical. Earlier comments in the thread have hit on how the earlier editions of WoD where a combination of positive visibility for certain aspects of Indigenous culture and identity, while also being quite disrespectful and ham-fisted in many other ways at the same time. And while those earlier editions absolutely could have been better, they have had a positive influence on many people as well. There are few things that are purely good or bad, so constructive conversation focuses on how to make things better. But part of making that better has to be actually letting the people whose ideas you're copying have their say, not talking over them and insisting on <b>your</b> interpretation of <b>their</b> lives.<br /> <br /> For the second point that I want to discuss, I'm going to borrow a convention used earlier in the thread when discussing mature vs. &quot;mature&quot; gaming.<br /> <br /> Are you going to play a Native American / Italian? Or are you going to play a &quot;Native American&quot; / &quot;Italian&quot;?<br /> <br /> Barring the exceptional cases of sacred/profane matters, I don't think that people from a given cultural group, or some other group-identity like sexuality or gender, is going to be opposed to a roleplayer making and playing a character who shares some aspect of their identity, as long as that character engages with that culture or identity in a way that is thoughtful and respectful. In fact, I think that many would probably appreciate someone who would take them time to learn their history, study their culture, and make a genuine effort to understand them so that they could play the role well. I think most people want to be understood, as long as you aren't forcing your way into things they consider personal or private.<br /> <br /> But if you're just going to play as a bundle of offensive stereotypes that you saw in a 40-year-old movie that you laugh at without really thinking about too deeply, I don't think it's at all surprising that people are going to call that out as dumb and trashy behaviour. It's intellectually lazy, and it contributes to the continuation of stereotypes that can destroy the lives of real people. And, once again leaning on the wisdom of previous posters whose names I can't be bothered to dig out from somewhere in 10 previous pages, this is a complicated issue with a lot of potential for real-world harm that the people making the game simply don't have a lot of control over; they can't force a gaming table to insist on not allowing racist stereotypes or not allowing in-game racism to serve as a cover for out-of-game racism. So they need to really focus on making sure that they get it right with the parts they can control.<br /> <br /> That was a lot of rambling, so I'm going to try and boil it down a bit:<br /> <br /> 1) The World of Darkness unintentionally took on a super-complicated bag that many other TTRPGs manage to avoid (somewhat) when it decided to exist in a reflection of our real world, with the real people in it. I don't necessarily think that was a mistake, but it is a big responsibility.<br /> <br /> 2) To all the folks getting outraged at the idea that you're not allowed to play X because you are Y: I don't think that any reasonable person is saying that. They are saying that you need to think about context, and you need to take it seriously, because you're not just playing with Tolkien-expies anymore. Do It Right, or Don't Do It. And some times, Do It Right means Don't Do It.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I couldn't find anywhere to fit it easily into my larger argument, but I do also want to mention that one of the things that can make cultural appropriation that could otherwise be neutral into a negative is when the group taking the culture is allowed to profit or enjoy that culture in a way the original group are not. For example, one of the reasons why cultural appropriation of Black hairstyles is such an issue in the US is because there is evidence that Black people with those hairstyles experience discrimination in the workplace while White people are more likely to get a pass, or even praised for it. Or when Elvis became a huge hit because he was a White performer who could perform a style of music that was popular but, until then, had been dominated (and originated) by Black performers in a still-very-openly-racist America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Extra comment about cultural appropriation that didn't fit the argument, but was too important to leave out 08-03-2023, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T10:11:54-07:00","id":1519638,"title":"","content":"I'm Black (with a bit of Scots-Irish and Romani in there from my Dad's side) and I've played lots and lots of characters who were White, Japanese, Korean, Brazilian, and Mexican.<br /> <br /> I also happen to be queer (but tbh, I dislike that term), poor, part of a religious minority, and disabled. And yet I've played straight characters, wealthy characters, Christian characters, and all of my characters were of able body and mind.<br /> <br /> I've also played as women despite being a man but tbh, I was assigned female at birth, so that's a bit more of a complicated topic. <br /> <br /> I honestly don't give a flying fuck if I'm playing a &quot;stereotype&quot; or indulging in so-called &quot;cultural appropriation&quot; and I don't care if anyone at my table does either, because I know it's fictional and so does everyone else at my game table. <br /> <br /> As long as it stays at the game table and within the realm of fiction, I'm of the view that it doesn't matter if something is &quot;problematic&quot; so long as the players and the Storyteller both know the difference between fiction and reality. <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is not real and it is not the real world. It may have some superficial similarities to the real world but it is a very stylized and over-the-top fictionalized dark fantasy version of the heavily world filtered through gothic romanticism and pop culture aesthetics, which for better or worse, have roots in so-called &quot;problematic&quot; tropes. Those &quot;problematic&quot; works of fiction and art also happen to be some of the most enjoyable works of media of all time and I find them far more preferable to the sanitized media of today, despite being a marginalized person myself.<br /> <br /> Who cares if something in a FICTIONAL game is racist, sexist, or whatever? So long as the person playing said character is not actively bigoted themselves and knows the difference between fiction and reality, I don't care.<br /> <br /> Even if the artist themselves had bigoted views or has done problematic things in real life, I still enjoy their works anyway as is. I love H.P Lovecraft's short stories, for example. Most of these people are long dead anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T10:51:51-07:00","id":1519640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519638#post1519638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Black (with a bit of Scots-Irish and Romani in there from my Dad's side) and I've played lots and lots of characters who were White, Japanese, Korean, Brazilian, and Mexican.<br /> <br /> I also happen to be queer (but tbh, I dislike that term), poor, part of a religious minority, and disabled. And yet I've played straight characters, wealthy characters, Christian characters, and all of my characters were of able body and mind.<br /> <br /> I've also played as women despite being a man but tbh, I was assigned female at birth, so that's a bit more of a complicated topic.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't give a flying fuck if I'm playing a &quot;stereotype&quot; or indulging in so-called &quot;cultural appropriation&quot; and I don't care if anyone at my table does either, because I know it's fictional and so does everyone else at my game table.<br /> <br /> As long as it stays at the game table and within the realm of fiction, I'm of the view that it doesn't matter if something is &quot;problematic&quot; so long as the players and the Storyteller both know the difference between fiction and reality.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is not real and it is not the real world. It may have some superficial similarities to the real world but it is a very stylized and over-the-top fictionalized dark fantasy version of the heavily world filtered through gothic romanticism and pop culture aesthetics, which for better or worse, have roots in so-called &quot;problematic&quot; tropes. Those &quot;problematic&quot; works of fiction and art also happen to be some of the most enjoyable works of media of all time and I find them far more preferable to the sanitized media of today, despite being a marginalized person myself.<br /> <br /> Who cares if something in a FICTIONAL game is racist, sexist, or whatever? So long as the person playing said character is not actively bigoted themselves and knows the difference between fiction and reality, I don't care.<br /> <br /> Even if the artist themselves had bigoted views or has done problematic things in real life, I still enjoy their works anyway as is. I love H.P Lovecraft's short stories, for example. Most of these people are long dead anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are fundamentally wrong to think that these sorts of things don't matter just because they are &quot;fiction.&quot; Our brains aren't actually that great at making the distinction. That's why arguments for diversity and inclusion in media exist; there is evidence to support the fact that being exposed to fictional characters of a given identity-group makes people less likely to discriminate against those kinds of people in real life. The stereotypes and cultural appropriation you indulge in at the table because you think it's harmless absolutely has the potential to bleed into your larger everyday life, often without you even realizing it.<br /> <br /> I mean, you do you. I'm not telling you that you're &quot;not allowed.&quot; I'm just saying that, allowed or not, it's probably the wrong decision if you care at all about the bigger picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T11:08:44-07:00","id":1519641,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I doubt any game writer, be them from any origin, would make their game (or their setting, or their werewolf tribe, or their dwarven clan) with the perspective &quot;I'm making this only so that people with the same origin as me will play this&quot;. Not a chance I say<br /> <br /> Not only I'm certain such representation is made to give presence, life, voice and expansion to that identity and culture to a wider view, but also so that other people can play and learn from it too. And I mean this in the context of a writer using their own environment and culture as basis or source for their content. Not representing a remote culture of them. <br /> They don't want to build walls. We don't want to build walls. We want bridges.<br /> <br /> I can only imagine the metaphor would go as &quot;let me have a door, and the key, just so that I can open it heartily of my own volition and show you around proudly&quot;<br /> Instead of you know. Having someone steal your home, or make a mockery of it on the other side of town, act like you are dead or alien, and try to (alien)explain everything about YOUR house and family; then act like they are doing you a favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T11:23:15-07:00","id":1519643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519640#post1519640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are fundamentally wrong to think that these sorts of things don't matter just because they are &quot;fiction.&quot; Our brains aren't actually that great at making the distinction. That's why arguments for diversity and inclusion in media exist; there is evidence to support the fact that being exposed to fictional characters of a given identity-group makes people less likely to discriminate against those kinds of people in real life. The stereotypes and cultural appropriation you indulge in at the table because you think it's harmless absolutely has the potential to bleed into your larger everyday life, often without you even realizing it.<br /> <br /> I mean, you do you. I'm not telling you that you're &quot;not allowed.&quot; I'm just saying that, allowed or not, it's probably the wrong decision if you care at all about the bigger picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I strongly yet respectfully disagree with you on that and I feel &quot;diversity and inclusion&quot; in fiction and media by way of shallow forced tokenism and bland sanitization doesn't actually help marginalized communities.<br /> <br /> Plus, I also find it to be very insulting and patronizing to me as someone from a marginalized identity group, even if it is well-intended\u200b.<br /> <br /> But that's just my own personal opinion and I'm gonna leave it at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-03-2023, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T12:10:24-07:00","id":1519646,"title":"","content":"It's pretty patronizing to say that your minority status gives you authority to permit the mistreatment of other minorities on their behalf Matt.<br /> <br /> Deflecting to bad representation is just that; a deflection. The whole point of this thread is that the fight for true diversity didn't end because a Native American finally got to play a Native American part, or that a Black person one a prestigious award. The work isn't over yet. The shallow stuff was a stepping stone to normalize minorities even being in our fiction. Claiming the cultural appropriation is a good thing is what keeps the representation shallow and demeaning, instead of letting it evolve into something better. In a previous thread specifically about cultural appropriation, I did a whole big post about how cultural appropriation has ruined Golems in pop-culture. Non-Jews taking the story of the Golem and using it just made it a boring ass word for, &quot;magical humanoid construct&quot; and completely lost the real cultural importance of the Golem in Jewish mythology and mysticism. Fighting cultural appropriation is how you make sure those stories actually teach the lessons they're meant to teach, instead of just becoming a mindless label for a stat block in an antagonist section of a book.<br /> <br /> Black people in American didn't become equal citizens because Lincoln said some words in a speech in the 1860s. It's taken a long time just to get where things are now, and it will take more time before there's real equality in America. All the push back against DEI, all the misuse of the concept of Death of the Author, and all of the whining about how things are &quot;PC gone too far,&quot; (or whatever buzzword people want to use now like cancel culture)? It's all the same logic used by people to fight against civil rights for minorities. It's used in media because as noted, media can create empathy and real equality through mutual exchange instead of power-imbalanced exchange, and if that happens, the people that wan unequal laws get less popular.<br /> <br /> You want to throw in with folks like Clarence Thomas? You do you. I couldn't live with myself if I was like that though. And that's what you're advocating for.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> Also, less to Matt specifically, as a Jew, on this forum, I've been accused of antisemitism, esp. by European posters, when I point out anti-Semitic myths they're perpetuating. They learned them somewhere. They felt those myths were normal enough to fine talking about in open forums. So it's my fault for bring people down when I point out they're doing bigotry, not their fault for falling for lies bigots told in the past.<br /> <br /> So the idea that we're &quot;done&quot; correcting racism and bigotry can go fuck itself, and anyone that really believes that we've gone &quot;too far&quot; can just post the truth that they're upset that WtA didn't become a game about how awesome Nazi-werewolves are to play. My ancestors didn't flee Europe because they had a real choice in the matter. If you don't feel like being part of the solution to all the problems that still exist, you can at least shut up and not make them worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T12:37:36-07:00","id":1519649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519646#post1519646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty patronizing to say that your minority status gives you authority to permit the mistreatment of other minorities on their behalf Matt.<br /> <br /> Deflecting to bad representation is just that; a deflection. The whole point of this thread is that the fight for true diversity didn't end because a Native American finally got to play a Native American part, or that a Black person one a prestigious award. The work isn't over yet. The shallow stuff was a stepping stone to normalize minorities even being in our fiction. Claiming the cultural appropriation is a good thing is what keeps the representation shallow and demeaning, instead of letting it evolve into something better. In a previous thread specifically about cultural appropriation, I did a whole big post about how cultural appropriation has ruined Golems in pop-culture. Non-Jews taking the story of the Golem and using it just made it a boring ass word for, &quot;magical humanoid construct&quot; and completely lost the real cultural importance of the Golem in Jewish mythology and mysticism. Fighting cultural appropriation is how you make sure those stories actually teach the lessons they're meant to teach, instead of just becoming a mindless label for a stat block in an antagonist section of a book.<br /> <br /> Black people in American didn't become equal citizens because Lincoln said some words in a speech in the 1860s. It's taken a long time just to get where things are now, and it will take more time before there's real equality in America. All the push back against DEI, all the misuse of the concept of Death of the Author, and all of the whining about how things are &quot;PC gone too far,&quot; (or whatever buzzword people want to use now like cancel culture)? It's all the same logic used by people to fight against civil rights for minorities. It's used in media because as noted, media can create empathy and real equality through mutual exchange instead of power-imbalanced exchange, and if that happens, the people that wan unequal laws get less popular.<br /> <br /> You want to throw in with folks like Clarence Thomas? You do you. I couldn't live with myself if I was like that though. And that's what you're advocating for.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> Also, less to Matt specifically, as a Jew, on this forum, I've been accused of antisemitism, esp. by European posters, when I point out anti-Semitic myths they're perpetuating. They learned them somewhere. They felt those myths were normal enough to fine talking about in open forums. So it's my fault for bring people down when I point out they're doing bigotry, not their fault for falling for lies bigots told in the past.<br /> <br /> So the idea that we're &quot;done&quot; correcting racism and bigotry can go fuck itself, and anyone that really believes that we've gone &quot;too far&quot; can just post the truth that they're upset that WtA didn't become a game about how awesome Nazi-werewolves are to play. My ancestors didn't flee Europe because they had a real choice in the matter. If you don't feel like being part of the solution to all the problems that still exist, you can at least shut up and not make them worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I get why you feel the way you do. Your intentions are noble and just a couple of years ago, I would've been fully backing you on all the points you've made. But after some rather unfortunate events in my personal life that I'd rather not want to relive, I just finally stopped caring.<br /> <br /> I used to be all about fighting bigotry and oppression at every turn and making it the entire focus of my life, but it took a toll on my mental health. It ruined me emotionally and I nearly died as a result of the depression, misery, and burnout I felt. There's a reason why I feel the way I feel and why I believe what I believe nowadays.<br /> <br /> I've spoken my peace and all I can do is just agree to disagree with you. I'm not going to fight you on this and I'm not going to tell you how to live your life. Don't tell me how to live mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-03-2023, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:11:54-07:00","id":1519656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519649#post1519649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I just finally stopped caring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The energy you're putting into this doesn't really say &quot;I stopped caring.&quot; And yeah, I saw your post pre-edit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I used to be all about fighting bigotry and oppression at every turn and making it the entire focus of my life, but it took a toll on my mental health. </div> </div> </div>Yep, balance is important. I don't define my entire life around fighting injustice, because... I'm human and I need to take care of myself too.<br /> <br /> It sucks that you got burnt out and whatever bad shit happened happened, but it seems like you don't really disagree with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to fight you on this and I'm not going to tell you how to live your life. Don't tell me how to live mine. </div> </div> </div>But therein lies the rub. We're at an impasse where we can't actually have both sides move apart and go their separate ways. Either I need to keep calling out injustice when I see it despite it telling people how to live their lives, or I'm letting you tell me how to live my life; because yeah, you are telling me how to live my life when you say that I'm not allowed to advocate for people to live differently than how they are.<br /> <br /> I'll be fine if you want your cop-out &quot;agree to disagree&quot; and not respond to this post. I don't need the last word, but I do like having more examples of my posts do not actually forcefully compel people to respond to me beyond their ability to control themselves (yeah, people on this forum spent years trying to gaslight me with that BS).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 08-03-2023, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:37:59-07:00","id":1519659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519656#post1519656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The energy you're putting into this doesn't really say &quot;I stopped caring.&quot; And yeah, I saw your post pre-edit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yep, balance is important. I don't define my entire life around fighting injustice, because... I'm human and I need to take care of myself too.<br /> <br /> It sucks that you got burnt out and whatever bad shit happened happened, but it seems like you don't really disagree with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But therein lies the rub. We're at an impasse where we can't actually have both sides move apart and go their separate ways. Either I need to keep calling out injustice when I see it despite it telling people how to live their lives, or I'm letting you tell me how to live my life; because yeah, you are telling me how to live my life when you say that I'm not allowed to advocate for people to live differently than how they are.<br /> <br /> I'll be fine if you want your cop-out &quot;agree to disagree&quot; and not respond to this post. I don't need the last word, but I do like having more examples of my posts do not actually forcefully compel people to respond to me beyond their ability to control themselves (yeah, people on this forum spent years trying to gaslight me with that BS).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to lie, I'm very angry and upset right now but I edited my post to be less inflammatory and outwardly angry and I'm trying to be civil here.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just &quot;cop-out&quot; and not reply any further but I'm gonna try and level with you. There's a reason why I got so upset at your post earlier and why I also eventually just got burnt out and turned to apathy and hedonism when it came to the subject of entertainment and pop culture.<br /> <br /> If you want to call out injustice then go on and so do, but from my own lived experience. it's not going to necessarily compel anyone to your cause and do things the way you want them to be done.<br /> <br /> If anything, I've seen that it often has the opposite effect in regards to trivial pursuits such as entertainment, especially online. Calling out injustice and fighting for a cause when you're out in real life and actually doing shit is a great thing that actually helps combat genuine oppression.<br /> <br /> But calling out problematic or bigoted content in trivial entertainment online rarely ever works. It will usually either come off as preachy and piss people off to the point it makes them side against you out of petty spite (I can't tell you how many friends and loved ones I've alienated with my activism) or it can make people become so worked up to try and defend your cause and &quot;do better&quot; that they eventually wear themselves out, crash and burn, and just drop out completely like I did.<br /> <br /> Maybe I just went about it the wrong way but all I do know is that my attempts to call everything out was either met with apathy or wound up turning people against me and my points. And if you can do this without burning yourself out and actually getting people to your side, then good for you. But for me, it just led to ruin. I ended up creating more bigots with my activism than convincing them otherwise.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just being overly sensitive because your posts remind me of how I used to behave both online and IRL until it led me to a prolonged mental health crisis throughout 2020 and 2021. I've since recovered, but I don't want to be compared to Clarence Thomas or the Nazis just because I'd rather just have fun and enjoy older entertainment, problematic content be damned, then go back to destroying myself emotionally and mentally by obsessively fixating on every aspect of my life from a critical standpoint.<br /> <br /> Sorry for snapping at you earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":".  Added clearer context and detail 08-03-2023, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:20:24-07:00","id":1519663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519536#post1519536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was this idea in that article that getting rid of any cultural ties for the Tribes was objectively a good thing because this way &quot;You needn\u2019t worry about being locked into playing a particular \u201ctype\u201d based on your or <b>your character\u2019s origin</b>, or misrepresenting or appropriating another culture through your tribe choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I took as if normally I should worry if I wanted to play a Native American or any other culture or ethnicity character that wasn't my RL one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another side to that alleged issue: the presumption of tribal characters belonging a certain ethnicity and vice versa.<br /> You may want to play an Utkena, because you're interested southwestern Native American culture. Whether that's your culture or not. But you might want to play one because you're into vaguely spooky magic. What will such a player, or writer for that matter, do with the real, indigenous heritage of tribe?<br /> <br /> Also, Fianna piss me off as a Celt, in a way that they probably wouldn't if they were of no particular culture, although I can't put my finger on what it is about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T15:24:35-07:00","id":1519671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519659#post1519659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason why I got so upset at your post earlier...</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone that wouldn't be upset at my post isn't someone I could respect. I wasn't trying to be even, mollifying, or neutral. We haven't Internet-known each other long, but you seem like a cool dude. But if you say something that seems pretty bad... I'm going to say so. I don't waste my time on people I know I have no chance of reaching. I've been an activist for over 30 years (which meant I've been at this longer than the Internet has allowed us to take easy pot shots on social media). Someone already broke out the studies and research aspect, and as usual that didn't really change much. So I ripped off the band-aid. Which stings, but gets to the problem faster.<br /> <br /> Also, I would point out that the only thing I've &quot;asked&quot; for in this regard is for people that don't care about cultural appropriation and so on to stop deriding it. I didn't ask for people to join in arms against it. I told people to shut up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, I've seen that it often has the opposite effect in regards to trivial pursuits such as entertainment, especially online. </div> </div> </div>But that's the thing. Entertainment isn't trivial. It's a definitional aspect of civilization (or at least when it moves from Calvin-ball style play to organized play and art). Entertainment is so important that if all USA own entertainment properties (both real and intellectual) were evenly divided so each citizen got the same amount of ownership value... we'd all be actual billionaires.<br /> <br /> You complained about how sanitized mainstream entertainment media is &quot;these days&quot; (though I've heard boomers, gen-xers, and millenials all say that of their own pop-culture zeitgeists enough to think it's more perspective than not), but it's that way because a tiny group of not very diverse people make the decisions to retread the same stuff over and over. That's the great thing about more diversity in the whole process rather than letting the same few hundred most white mostly Christian mostly AMAB super rich folks make all the decisions about what gets mass releases and what's tossed on a streaming service for a month before it disappears to save corporate money. Diversity gets us new voices, new stories, and a lot of people that want to take risks with stuff. It's the cultural stagnation at the top that stagnates the whole industry. If we want movies to get better, with need to find the next Spike Lee (very mixed feelings on his work, but that's my point, he takes risks and some work out and some don't), not the next Bob Iger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but I don't want to be compared to Clarence Thomas or the Nazis just because I'd rather just have fun and enjoy older entertainment, problematic content be damned, then go back to destroying myself emotionally and mentally by obsessively fixating on every aspect of my life from a critical standpoint. </div> </div> </div>There's a false dichotomy here of either having to ignore the problematic stuff in older media, or be a Too Online Activist that burns out. You can do stuff that doesn't have me comparing you to assholes and bigots, without having to join my cause. I don't recruit online (no matter how much our social media manager keeps saying we need to do that more, I still get more people that she does). <br /> <br /> You can just... not say, &quot;HP Lovecraft's bigotry be damned, I'm going to love his work unconditionally!&quot; Enjoying problematic media (aka all media worth enjoying ever created and likely to ever be created) is simple: acknowledge and don't diminish the problems. &quot;HPL was really bigoted even for his time, it leaks into his works, some people might want to nope out because of the yikes in the stories, but if you can stomach that, it's wonderfully written cosmic horror.&quot; Lovecraft is a bit of a low bar to me because despite his casual bigotry in his works, he generally avoided making any of it so central to the story the story couldn't work with a few edits to get rid of it. Something like... WtA or the WoD at large are much bigger lifts because not only are they contemporary for us, they're a lot really shitty stuff baked into the core of the games that's still there decades later despite a lot of attempts to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> Just... don't defend the problems. Don't deride the solution. I assure that helps the bigots way more than any Internet tribalism you went through in the past. That's why I went straight for Thomas as a specific individual to cite, because that's his whole damned career after he felt bad because people might think less of him because Black people needed help from society to get equality, he defends inequality, and attacks solutions. He puts imagined harms over real harms. Internet debates are way more imagined harms than real harms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for snapping at you earlier. </div> </div> </div>I was ready for way worse (than your pre-edit version too), and I wouldn't have held it against you. Thank you for opting for this path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T23:20:53-07:00","id":1519710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519634#post1519634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/@<br /> But if you're just going to play as a bundle of offensive stereotypes that you saw in a 40-year-old movie that you laugh at without really thinking about too deeply, I don't think it's at all surprising that people are going to call that out as dumb and trashy behaviour. It's intellectually lazy, and it contributes to the continuation of stereotypes that can destroy the lives of real people. And, once again leaning on the wisdom of previous posters whose names I can't be bothered to dig out from somewhere in 10 previous pages, this is a complicated issue with a lot of potential for real-world harm that the people making the game simply don't have a lot of control over; they can't force a gaming table to insist on not allowing racist stereotypes or not allowing in-game racism to serve as a cover for out-of-game racism. So they need to really focus on making sure that they get it right with the parts they can control.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, but I have to call bullshit. 5 rolists having fun at a table even using stereotypes does not destroy people lives.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes, especially those used for genuine fun (aka not targetted at someone concerned) are rarely correlated with any ill actions toward those concerned.<br /> <br /> A rolist playing a stereotype of a catholic priest will not then go out to insult the priest of his village. Nor does someone &quot;badly&quot; playing a native american will go out of their way to make real life natives miserable.<br /> <br /> <br /> This idea that there's a cause and effect relation between those is an axiom some people believes, not a demonstrated fact.<br /> <br /> The only criteria that need to exist on what is permissible at a ttrpg table is if everyone around said table is okay with it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519634#post1519634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) To all the folks getting outraged at the idea that you're not allowed to play X because you are Y: I don't think that any reasonable person is saying that. They are saying that you need to think about context, and you need to take it seriously, because you're not just playing with Tolkien-expies anymore. Do It Right, or Don't Do It. And some times, Do It Right means Don't Do It.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They do perpetually moralize on the topic and demand that we do it The Right Way(tm).<br /> <br /> And that's what people talk about when thry say the author don't allow it. They don't allow it &quot;morally&quot;. &quot;It's do it this way or you're a bad person&quot;.<br /> <br /> And you're doing it here by saying that &quot;some times, Do It Right means Don't Do It&quot;. You're making a moral command.<br /> <br /> And again, this is ttrpg, the only criteria for &quot;do it right&quot; should only be &quot;does that annoy my table mates or not?&quot;.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519634#post1519634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> P.S. I couldn't find anywhere to fit it easily into my larger argument, but I do also want to mention that one of the things that can make cultural appropriation that could otherwise be neutral into a negative is when the group taking the culture is allowed to profit or enjoy that culture in a way the original group are not. For example, one of the reasons why cultural appropriation of Black hairstyles is such an issue in the US is because there is evidence that Black people with those hairstyles experience discrimination in the workplace while White people are more likely to get a pass, or even praised for it. Or when Elvis became a huge hit because he was a White performer who could perform a style of music that was popular but, until then, had been dominated (and originated) by Black performers in a still-very-openly-racist America.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, this is also why many people don't take claims of cultural appropriation serisously.<br /> You may not have realized it, but you shifted the criterias of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> In the beginning of you comment you described it as &quot;forcefully taking a piece of a culture you were never part of, twisting it and maiming it however you wish to make it into what you want, and then maybe throwing a price-tag onto it at the end.&quot;<br /> <br /> Howether, copying a hairstyle does not match that criteria. Since there's no maiming or twisting it.<br /> <br /> Now you made the new criteria being the status of the group in question, which completly shift the idea from &quot;taking without respect from another culture is bad&quot; to &quot;it his bad due to the state of that community&quot;.<br /> <br /> And to be straightforward, I'm not trying to attack you for that confusion of criterias. But I simply want to pinpoint that this concept is perpetually drowing in double standards. <br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, by the way you describe the issue, it seems the problem is not that white people had these hairstyle done to them, but how certain people reacted. Hence it was not the &quot;appropriation&quot; in itself that is the problem. This is a case of missed target.<br /> <br /> And while I think of it, this exemple you gave also show a glaring danger of this idea of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> There have been cases of white girls, typically red headed, who have been harassed by people because they were accused of appropriating the afro hairstyle. Even though these girls, like a certain number of red headed people, are born with hair that have a natural tendency to go with way.<br /> Or when people at a celtic festival in europe were berated for &quot;appropriating the dreadlock hairstyle&quot;. Even though dreadlocks are a traditional hairstyle from ancient nordic and some celtic culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is a toxic concept, which stop people from sharing and appreciating cultures, and by doing so, spread it's influence (look at how well this has worked for Japan post WW2).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T23:28:12-07:00","id":1519711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519640#post1519640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why arguments for diversity and inclusion in media exist; there is evidence to support the fact that being exposed to fictional characters of a given identity-group makes people less likely to discriminate against those kinds of people in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I would say that the current backlash against diversity in media even in the USA and the fact that despite such diversity being nearly obligatory in american entertainment, the rate of acceptation of lgbt has gone down for the first time since the rate is measured speaks otherwise.<br /> <br /> People dislike being lectured at. And it's a common feeling that the whole D.I.E. initiatives is a direct way to try to influence the public. Which is not appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519640#post1519640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stereotypes and cultural appropriation you indulge in at the table because you think it's harmless absolutely has the potential to bleed into your larger everyday life, often without you even realizing it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but that doesn't sounds like a fact based belief. I'm pretty curious on the social science litterature, and I clearly don't remember any demonstration of even a weak correlation between those.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T05:36:59-07:00","id":1519735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519710#post1519710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I have to call bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>For someone complaining about a lack fo demonstrated fact, you're not offering any of your own in your call of bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5 rolists having fun at a table even using stereotypes does not destroy people lives. </div> </div> </div>I know four people that have attempted suicide due to bigoted based bullying, gaslighting, and harassment that happen when they joined gaming groups that seemed to be chill and cool people, and then slowly pushed more and more boundaries until those people I know now were traumatically scarred for life. There are concepts that aren't even thing that sound bad that are off-limits in some of my games because they're trauma triggers for some of our gaming circles.<br /> <br /> Because very few people only have a single tiny group of other gamers that they socialize with. People game with other group to try other games, or to fit a different schedule, or whatever. Gamers love to talk about what they feel was cool stuff in their games with other people, which spreads what happen at one table beyond it.<br /> <br /> You've never seen it? Awesome for you and your folks for being nice people. It doesn't happen? That's bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...rarely correlated... </div> </div> </div>Demonstration of fact for this? Though at least you're admitting it does actually happen, which means it should matter. One person having to suffer this is too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A rolist playing a stereotype of a catholic priest will not then go out to insult the priest of his village. </div> </div> </div>That was my first gaming group's Christian raised players' favorite pastime. Though causation was definitely dislike of the Church first, playing evil priests second, shouting at a certain priest while driving by third.<br /> <br /> It didn't inspire me to do it to my Rabbi... but my Rabbi didn't inspire that in me. It certainly left an impression, and when I was younger I said a lot of inappropriate things about child molesting priests in front of Catholics that was very rude (even if not completely uncalled for as the truth about that has come out).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor does someone &quot;badly&quot; playing a native american will go out of their way to make real life natives miserable. </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do. They just don't realize it. As is very predictable, you're framing this all as if the results only matter if someone puts on a Nazi uniform and starts harassing people in the streets, and not all of the smaller harder to see things that happen.<br /> <br /> What you seem staunchly opposed to understanding, so apparently role-playing as all these different kinds of people hasn't actually taught you by itself, is that being a persecuted minority already comes with a base-line level of misery above everything else in the majority also has to deal with. One of the worst part of it is that there's lots and lots of people that say the right things, but don't actually do them when the situation comes around. Most people don't actually want to make the world better, they just don't want their world to be upset. So when you're in a room, and someone says a nasty joke about your people, and you call them out on it? There is very little like the misery of seeing a room full of people bending over backwards to defend a bigoted joke, instead of joining up in telling the person that made the joke they're in the wrong to have done so. They're rather the minority suffer in silent misery, that have to distract from their content status quo to &quot;make a scene&quot; out of it.<br /> <br /> So when we're in place... just like this forum.... when people talk about their badly done minority characters, or defending badly done minority characters in media as being not bad somehow, that's making people miserable. And if someone calls them out on it, they're going to act all offended by the idea because they don't see themselves as bad people, so they can't be bigots, and bigotry is only done by bad people, so they can't have done some bigotry accidentally because that doesn't work. And then a lot of people come to their defense (or at least spam those like buttons), which increases the misery because the people trying to have less casual bigotry in their community get tuned into the bad guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only criteria that need to exist on what is permissible at a ttrpg table is if everyone around said table is okay with it. </div> </div> </div>Meaninglessly true. If a group decides it's fun to play Nordic Christian warriors killing Jews and Muslims thinly disguised as goblins and orcs? They have every right to do that. There's even an RPG out there just for them. There's nothing anyone else can do to stop it in a functional liberal democracy.<br /> <br /> We can however, make sure that they know exactly how unacceptable and shameful it is to the rest of us so they at least keep it to themselves instead of bragging about how their crit to genocide people was role-played in public.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They do perpetually moralize on the topic and demand that we do it The Right Way(tm). </div> </div> </div>You're insistence that the only thing that matters is what the individuals at the table to agree to is no different in approach, but much harder to defend morally... because things don't actually stay at the table.<br /> <br /> You're making a moral command as well. Just one that happens to be great for people that don't face discrimination, and sucky for ones that do, because it empowers bad people, and does nothing to make good people's lives better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, this is also why many people don't take claims of cultural appropriation serisously. </div> </div> </div>Many people don't take it seriously because of the truth isn't something they want to deal with is a predictable by telling statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may not have realized it, but you shifted the criterias of cultural appropriation. </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't. That's why it was an addendum with a caveat of it not fitting in worth the core post's argument. The text you quote includes this specific line: &quot;...one of the things that can make cultural appropriation that could otherwise be neutral into a negative...&quot; that is not shifting the criteria in that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Howether, copying a hairstyle does not match that criteria. Since there's no maiming or twisting it. </div> </div> </div>There most certainly are both here in the US when it comes to Black natural hair; and not just here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you made the new criteria being the status of the group in question, which completly shift the idea from &quot;taking without respect from another culture is bad&quot; to &quot;it his bad due to the state of that community&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;status&quot; of the group in question has always been part of the equation. Cultural appropriation happens when there is a disparity in status between two cultures. That's what allows one to take from the other without respect or permission in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I simply want to pinpoint that this concept is perpetually drowing in double standards. </div> </div> </div>You've yet to demonstrate a single one despite this supposed ocean of them to drown in. But if you want to keep repeating the lies of Nazis, fascists, white supremacists, and so on, you're doing a great job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, by the way you describe the issue, it seems the problem is not that white people had these hairstyle done to them, but how certain people reacted. Hence it was not the &quot;appropriation&quot; in itself that is the problem. This is a case of missed target. </div> </div> </div>Are you even reading the posts?<br /> <br /> The problem is that white women in the US can get hairstyles and face no negative consequences or even positive ones, while Black people (not actually just women), who naturally have hair that requires those styles, are actively punished for it. Black kids in the US get suspended from schools for hair styles white kids don't. Black people face job and house discrimination for keeping their natural hair styles instead of spending lots of time and money on making their hair &quot;normal,&quot; while white people can &quot;experiment&quot; with Black hair and not suffer those consequences.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think this isn't appropriation and is a &quot;missed target.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while I think of it, this exemple you gave also show a glaring danger of this idea of cultural appropriation. </div> </div> </div>Are you seriously comparing a century of active socioeconomic discrimination to an unsourced thing about one festival in Europe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There have been cases of white girls, typically red headed, who have been harassed by people because they were accused of appropriating the afro hairstyle. </div> </div> </div>Source?<br /> <br /> Because around here Afro, Redfro, and Jewfro (that's also the thing, my dad's got the hair for it, mine isn't thick enough even if it's curly as hell) is actually a bonding point between communities that face discrimination (gingers get a lot more shit from other white people than Black people, I assure you), because it's a common experience to have our hair used against us. Plus being able to suggest good barbers/hair salons that know how to work with high curl hair in parts of town that you're not used to,and other tips. That's good cultural exchange even if somewhat forced by not great circumstances. I have sat in a room with all three of those groups, where we all got to share the insipid experiences of old white ladies (and for some reason it's always old white ladies) that just walk up and grab our hair without even asking.<br /> <br /> Even if there's some initial mistrust, people get authentic experiences, and cultural appropriation is not the cause of anti-ginger discrimination in Western society. There might have been some stupid Internet drama where people spouted off on things without context, but Black folks recognize real fast when someone else has been through things because of physical features they can't help.<br /> <br /> This is not &quot;toxic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a toxic concept, which stop people from sharing and appreciating cultures, and by doing so, spread it's influence (look at how well this has worked for Japan post WW2). </div> </div> </div>Who said we wanted out culture shared without our permission? Who says we want others to appreciate it without context they can't have because they didn't live it? Who says we want &quot;influence&quot; like that?<br /> <br /> It doesn't stop people from sharing for themselves, it stops other people from sharing without our ability to have a say in the matter.<br /> <br /> Also Japan, really? Sure, exporting manga and anime has made some companies a lot of money, but post-WWII culture in Japan is not doing well for it. The country is run by ultranationalists that enforce xenophobia and racism in government policies (esp, immigration), post-WWII has seen a massive push to modernize the culture leaving traditional Japanese culture hanging on by a thread mostly funded by need to make sure all the unique exotic things are there for tourists to gawk at, it's created generations that don't want to get married or have kids (only 800K babies were born in Japan in 2020, a country of 125 million people, those are bad numbers for keeping their culture going), and the previously mentioned government refuses to make the country more welcoming to immigrants to make up for their low birth rates like most wealthy nations facing that issue do, despite a decade of throwing huge amounts of money to try to figure out how to get Japanese kids to grow up and marry Japanese people and have Japanese babies not working.<br /> <br /> So, sure, Japan, great example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519711#post1519711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that the current backlash against diversity in media even in the USA and the fact that despite such diversity being nearly obligatory in american entertainment, the rate of acceptation of lgbt has gone down for the first time since the rate is measured speaks otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't.<br /> <br /> The backlash is a small minority of bigots, and the decline of acceptance of LGBTQ+ folks going down is fueled by the far right attacks on trans people (who have not had the level of cultural acceptance as gay and lesbians have), and continued American racism as white gay representation was doing great, but minority gay representation is still well below that.<br /> <br /> It's a purposeful effort in the US to try to drive a wedge between LG and BTQ+ (like has been very successful in the UK), because the public has largely accepted the first two (and that hasn't declined, but it has plateaued even if at a strong support), which matches with cultural representation, and is still minimally exposed to the rest, making them easy targets as they try to climb up the ladder next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People dislike being lectured at. </div> </div> </div>And yet, that only matter in one direction.<br /> <br /> People hate to be lectured at, but they certainly lecture at other people just fine. You're lecturing plenty here yourself.<br /> <br /> Besides, we're only calling it &quot;lecturing&quot; because we don't agree with it. If you're posting long in-depth essays people agree with it's not lecturing then.<br /> <br /> What people really don't like, as I said before, is being made to feel uncomfortable. They don't like &quot;lectures&quot; because they're hearing uncomfortable things that might make them have to change, which is also discomforting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is not appreciated. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's so horrible that people are honestly trying to influence the public to be... more empathetic to minorities. The fact that people don't appreciate that tells on those people, not the people doing DEI. <br /> <br /> Also, DEI training is such a non-issue. It's like doing your standard workplace harassment training that's been normal for decades. It's not some onerous burden. It's a set of guidelines to learn to avoid getting in trouble with HR, which is part of every job for other issues anyway. Just like CRT before it, bad faith people blew it up into this giant Thing, so people like you think there's some real deep seated issue to debate. DEI in the actual world isn't controversial, just like training people how to not sexually harass their coworkers isn't controversial. The controversy is made up bullshit labeled DEI so there's something for people to fight over. It's kinda sad that we have to have training programs in how not to be rude to people different than you as a society, but it's worse that people try to turn those programs into some giant conspiracy theory because that's the best they can do to create culture wars for politicians to fight over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, but that doesn't sounds like a fact based belief. I'm pretty curious on the social science litterature, and I clearly don't remember any demonstration of even a weak correlation between those. </div> </div> </div>This just sounds like you have your head buried in the sand.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T07:25:43-07:00","id":1519743,"title":"","content":"&quot;Here's this tabletop roleplaying game where you can play anybody on Earth... Oh except Native Americans. You're not allowed to play them, unless you're a Native American. By the way, we have two tribes who are Native American in origin. But you're not allowed to play them. Oh if your Storyteller isn't Native American, they shouldn't use them as NPCs either.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bruh, this is how we end up with erasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T07:35:21-07:00","id":1519744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519743#post1519743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Here's this tabletop roleplaying game where you can play anybody on Earth... Oh except Native Americans. You're not allowed to play them, unless you're a Native American. By the way, we have two tribes who are Native American in origin. But you're not allowed to play them. Oh if your Storyteller isn't Native American, they shouldn't use them as NPCs either.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bruh, this is how we end up with erasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if we're assessing by representation when push comes to shove the ultimate result of w5 is the erasure of one of the few representions of Native Canadians in pop culture media.<br /> <br /> edit-as a brit i honestly cannot think of any others<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-04-2023, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T08:17:54-07:00","id":1519745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519743#post1519743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Here's this tabletop roleplaying game where you can play anybody on Earth... Oh except Native Americans. You're not allowed to play them, unless you're a Native American. By the way, we have two tribes who are Native American in origin. But you're not allowed to play them. Oh if your Storyteller isn't Native American, they shouldn't use them as NPCs either.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bruh, this is how we end up with erasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a vast amount of space between those two poles. You can play and use cultures you are not part of, but do it with respect, do some research and don't play up negative stereotypes. If someone tells you something hurts them and they are not comfortable with it, listen to them and adapt. There's a lot of things we take for granted that are parts of negative cultural stereotypes, and we should be aware which of them are negative and hostile to others.<br /> <br /> Being willing to take a step back, listen and learn is how this works out beneficial to everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T08:57:46-07:00","id":1519748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519745#post1519745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a vast amount of space between those two poles. You can play and use cultures you are not part of, but do it with respect, do some research and don't play up negative stereotypes. If someone tells you something hurts them and they are not comfortable with it, listen to them and adapt. There's a lot of things we take for granted that are parts of negative cultural stereotypes, and we should be aware which of them are negative and hostile to others.<br /> <br /> Being willing to take a step back, listen and learn is how this works out beneficial to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking for the negative in my post. This was kind of the whole point with what J.F. Sambrano was saying. He liked the entire fact there were two Native American tribes in Werewolf, even if they had a bunch of flaws. The idea they were at least trying was awesome... and he wanted to do better less flawed versions of them, for people to play.<br /> <br /> Not to sit on the metaphorical shelf like fragile figures that will break if we handle them the wrong way.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need to sit through a college thesis class to play a pretend game. The entire point of presenting them the 'right way' in the core book, should be everything you need in order to play them.<br /> <br /> I like to give the benefit of the doubt and think nobody here wants to play a lazy stereotype, but at the end of the day, any research you do to play a &quot;Game&quot; should be light enough to not be daunting or entirely off putting in the first place.<br /> <br /> Because when you throw up too many barriers to even get a chance to play the character, that's just another form of erasure.<br /> <br /> From what I've read when it comes to the Indigenous game designers out there, no, they don't want people playing harmful stereotypes... But they DO want people to play Indigenous characters. They want that because it brings visibility to them. It shows they exist and are part of the world, and not something you're going to just sweep away because it's too much of a quagmire to get involved with.<br /> <br /> Hell, this is one of the reasons Coyote and Crow exists... It's an entire game where you can ONLY play Indigenous characters, made by an Indigenous writer. They want these characters played, not hid under a glass case to be admired in some museum but ever touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:06:08-07:00","id":1519749,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone!<br /> <br /> So a little bit of context: I'm in the middle of a move, and yesterday I accidentally canceled my internet early, because I'm a fool. So I'm mostly limited to phone replies for the next week or so, which sucks.<br /> <br /> So I really want to thank <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> for saying what I'd probably want to say better and with greater depth than I could have managed, even if I had my computer available <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:30:23-07:00","id":1519760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For someone complaining about a lack fo demonstrated fact, you're not offering any of your own in your call of bullshit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because it\u2019s your job. You make a positive claim about the existence of a phenomena, aka that stereotypes in a ttrpg tables cause real life harm.<br /> Hence YOU have to prove it. It\u2019s not to others to disprove you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know four people that have attempted suicide due to bigoted based bullying, gaslighting, and harassment that happen when they joined gaming groups that seemed to be chill and cool people, and then slowly pushed more and more boundaries until those people I know now were traumatically scarred for life. There are concepts that aren't even thing that sound bad that are off-limits in some of my games because they're trauma triggers for some of our gaming circles.<br /> <br /> Because very few people only have a single tiny group of other gamers that they socialize with. People game with other group to try other games, or to fit a different schedule, or whatever. Gamers love to talk about what they feel was cool stuff in their games with other people, which spreads what happen at one table beyond it.<br /> <br /> You've never seen it? Awesome for you and your folks for being nice people. It doesn't happen? That's bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That anecdote is yout of touch with what is said.<br /> We\u2019re talking baout your belief that steretypes in game, even with the agreement of everyone around, causes real lige harm.<br /> People being directly harassed by other players is litterally not adressing the point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demonstration of fact for this? Though at least you're admitting it does actually happen, which means it should matter. One person having to suffer this is too much.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And one person is not enough to placate the entire ttrpg constantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my first gaming group's Christian raised players' favorite pastime. Though causation was definitely dislike of the Church first, playing evil priests second, shouting at a certain priest while driving by third.<br /> <br /> It didn't inspire me to do it to my Rabbi... but my Rabbi didn't inspire that in me. It certainly left an impression, and when I was younger I said a lot of inappropriate things about child molesting priests in front of Catholics that was very rude (even if not completely uncalled for as the truth about that has come out).</div> </div> </div> </div>So you litterally contradicted your point by having a whole group playing stereotypes and never causing real life harm based on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they do. They just don't realize it. As is very predictable, you're framing this all as if the results only matter if someone puts on a Nazi uniform and starts harassing people in the streets, and not all of the smaller harder to see things that happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, the \u00ab results \u00bb matters when they can be demonstrated. You ASSUME a link of causality. It\u2019s not demonstrated<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What you seem staunchly opposed to understanding, so apparently role-playing as all these different kinds of people hasn't actually taught you by itself, is that being a persecuted minority already comes with a base-line level of misery above everything else in the majority also has to deal with. One of the worst part of it is that there's lots and lots of people that say the right things, but don't actually do them when the situation comes around. Most people don't actually want to make the world better, they just don't want their world to be upset. So when you're in a room, and someone says a nasty joke about your people, and you call them out on it? There is very little like the misery of seeing a room full of people bending over backwards to defend a bigoted joke, instead of joining up in telling the person that made the joke they're in the wrong to have done so. They're rather the minority suffer in silent misery, that have to distract from their content status quo to &quot;make a scene&quot; out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that this is only your pretty biased view of people, not a reality ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when we're in place... just like this forum.... when people talk about their badly done minority characters, or defending badly done minority characters in media as being not bad somehow, that's making people miserable.<br /> <br /> And if someone calls them out on it, they're going to act all offended by the idea because they don't see themselves as bad people, so they can't be bigots, and bigotry is only done by bad people, so they can't have done some bigotry accidentally because that doesn't work. And then a lot of people come to their defense (or at least spam those like buttons), which increases the misery because the people trying to have less casual bigotry in their community get tuned into the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actually more that no one like pseudo white knights that gets offended at every Thing contradicting their narrow moral view.<br /> And again, this misery you talk about is undemonstrated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaninglessly true. If a group decides it's fun to play Nordic Christian warriors killing Jews and Muslims thinly disguised as goblins and orcs? They have every right to do that. There's even an RPG out there just for them. There's nothing anyone else can do to stop it in a functional liberal democracy.<br /> <br /> We can however, make sure that they know exactly how unacceptable and shameful it is to the rest of us so they at least keep it to themselves instead of bragging about how their crit to genocide people was role-played in public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you read yourself before posting ? \u00ab Meaninglessly true \u00bb is a self defeating statement, sive whenether the statement your responding to about what should happen at a table IS the meanig of the conversation.<br /> And don\u2019t confuse yourself as a majority with a \u00ab the rest of us \u00bb. You have hardly any to tell that you\u2019re not part of a very vocal minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're insistence that the only thing that matters is what the individuals at the table to agree to is no different in approach, but much harder to defend morally... because things don't actually stay at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actually very easy to defend morzlly : you give no evidence that things in the make belieieve game accepted by the whole table does harm in real life<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're making a moral command as well. Just one that happens to be great for people that don't face discrimination, and sucky for ones that do, because it empowers bad people, and does nothing to make good people's lives better.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m making the opposite of a moral command. I\u2019m saying \u00ab lets each table do as they want \u00bb.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many people don't take it seriously because of the truth isn't something they want to deal with is a predictable by telling statement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a baseless claim. For all you know, many people don\u2019t tke it seriously because it is a ridiculous idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they didn't. That's why it was an addendum with a caveat of it not fitting in worth the core post's argument. The text you quote includes this specific line: &quot;...one of the things that can make cultural appropriation that could otherwise be neutral into a negative...&quot; that is not shifting the criteria in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Since the original criteria is only about the intention of the one taking a cultural element, and it is then shifted to a criteria about the state of said culture.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There most certainly are both here in the US when it comes to Black natural hair; and not just here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You confuse the intention of those who take the element, here the hairstyle, with the vision ofnpeople around them of that element<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;status&quot; of the group in question has always been part of the equation. Cultural appropriation happens when there is a disparity in status between two cultures. That's what allows one to take from the Other without respect or permission in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, the original criteria was always about intention, not the state of the culture.<br /> Nor does disparity stop a weaker culture from taking from a stronger one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've yet to demonstrate a single one despite this supposed ocean of them to drown in. But if you want to keep repeating the lies of Nazis, fascists, white supremacists, and so on, you're doing a great job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I demonstrated it in the very comment you\u2019re answering to. But as we\u2019ve seen in this exchange already, you clearly don\u2019t read or understand what I say.<br /> And as expected, you\u2019re one of those people who see facists and whitb supreamacists everywhere. You sbould have started with that, I would have known you couldn\u2019t argue your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you even reading the posts?<br /> <br /> The problem is that white women in the US can get hairstyles and face no negative consequences or even positive ones, while Black people (not actually just women), who naturally have hair that requires those styles, are actively punished for it. Black kids in the US get suspended from schools for hair styles white kids don't. Black people face job and house discrimination for keeping their natural hair styles instead of spending lots of time and money on making their hair &quot;normal,&quot; while white people can &quot;experiment&quot; with Black hair and not suffer those consequences.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think this isn't appropriation and is a &quot;missed target.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you\u2019re not thinking.<br /> I\u2019ll use some dialectics to dumb it down.<br /> <br /> Cultural appropriation is taking cultural elements without respect<br /> So if a culture is A, the hairstyle is B, the white woman is C and the people reacting to it is D<br /> Cultural appropriation is when C takes B from A.<br /> <br /> What you\u2019re describing is D reacting to B differently when it\u2019s on A or C<br /> Which has nothing to do with cultural appropriation, as it\u2019s not the same logicao following.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you seriously comparing a century of active socioeconomic discrimination to an unsourced thing about one festival in Europe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the hell did you get that ? We\u2019re talking about cureent people suffering because of the pseudo moral outrage of others.<br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1519735]<br /> Source?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here\u2019s a few<br /> <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/student/news/black-san-francisco-student-filmed-harassing-white-student-because-of-his-dreadlocks-in-cultural-appropriation-row-a6959181.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.independent.co.uk/studen...-a6959181.html</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://boundingintocomics.com/2020/11/21/animal-crossing-new-horizons-player-faces-wave-of-harassment-and-accusations-of-racism-over-in-game-bun-hairstyle/amp/\" target=\"_blank\">https://boundingintocomics.com/2020/...hairstyle/amp/</a> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1519735]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said we wanted out culture shared without our permission? Who says we want others to appreciate it without context they can't have because they didn't live it? Who says we want &quot;influence&quot; like that ?<br /> <br /> It doesn't stop people from sharing for themselves, it stops other people from sharing without our ability to have a say in the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said you or anyone else had a choice ?<br /> Culture will be copied. Because like everyone else, you qhow your culture on yourself and when you speak, and people will hear it, see it. And inevitably if there\u2019s interest, imitate it.<br /> You can\u2019t stop that, no culture ever succeeded in stopping others to do so. I can\u2019t stop anyone from taking elements of my french culture, and you can\u2019t stop others from doing so with yours.<br /> <br /> Because culture is not an object that can be kept. It\u2019s an idea, and idea, once expressed, travels.<br /> <br /> The only way to keep your culture only for yourself would be to practice it in secret.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Japan, really? Sure, exporting manga and anime has made some companies a lot of money, but post-WWII culture in Japan is not doing well for it. The country is run by ultranationalists that enforce xenophobia and racism in government policies (esp, immigration), post-WWII has seen a massive push to modernize the culture leaving traditional Japanese culture hanging on by a thread mostly funded by need to make sure all the unique exotic things are there for tourists to gawk at, it's created generations that don't want to get married or have kids (only 800K babies were born in Japan in 2020, a country of 125 million people, those are bad numbers for keeping their culture going), and the previously mentioned government refuses to make the country more welcoming to immigrants to make up for their low birth rates like most wealthy nations facing that issue do, despite a decade of throwing huge amounts of money to try to figure out how to get Japanese kids to grow up and marry Japanese people and have Japanese babies not working.<br /> <br /> So, sure, Japan, great example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of the lack of kids, none of these are issues to japanese people. For them, favorih their people over strangers is normal. Nor is imigration a solution for them, since they are replacing menial jobs with robotics.<br /> And frankly, seeig how well it worked in europe, I can\u2019t blame them for that last position.<br /> As for their traditional culture, you confuse modernisation of day to day life with abnadonment of culture.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't.<br /> <br /> The backlash is a small minority of bigots, and the decline of acceptance of LGBTQ+ folks going down is fueled by the far right attacks on trans people (who have not had the level of cultural acceptance as gay and lesbians have), and continued American racism as white gay representation was doing great, but minority gay representation is still well below that.<br /> <br /> It's a purposeful effort in the US to try to drive a wedge between LG and BTQ+ (like has been very successful in the UK), because the public has largely accepted the first two (and that hasn't declined, but it has plateaued even if at a strong support), which matches with cultural representation, and is still minimally exposed to the rest, making them easy targets as they try to climb up the ladder next.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All that is bullshit.<br /> If it was a minority of protesters, entertainment companies would be for the first time losing money over it and abandoning DEI.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/nypost.com/2023/07/12/equity-activists-outraged-at-disney-netflix-for-forcing-dei-chiefs-out-corporate-blackface/amp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/nypost.com/2023/07/12/equity-activists-outraged-at-disney-netflix-for-forcing-dei-chiefs-out-corporate-blackface/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/nypost.com/2023/07/12/equity-activists-outraged-at-disney-netflix-for-forcing-dei-chiefs-out-corporate-blackface/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/amp/s/nypost.com/2023/07/12/equity-activists-outraged-at-disney-netflix-for-forcing-dei-chiefs-out-corporate-blackface/amp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Plus, these people are not bigots, critics of such agenda are simply fed up with empty virtue signaling and attempt at social engineering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, that only matter in one direction.<br /> <br /> People hate to be lectured at, but they certainly lecture at other people just fine. You're lecturing plenty here yourself.<br /> <br /> Besides, we're only calling it &quot;lecturing&quot; because we don't agree with it. If you're posting long in-depth essays people agree with it's not lecturing then.<br /> <br /> What people really don't like, as I said before, is being made to feel uncomfortable. They don't like &quot;lectures&quot; because they're hearing uncomfortable things that might make them have to change, which is also discomforting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what happen when people lecture at others ? They get debated, mocked or ignored.<br /> And no, it\u2019s not called lecturing because we don\u2019t agree with it, but because it\u2019s litterally preaching.<br /> People don\u2019t hear inconfortable things in these messages, they hear annoying things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's so horrible that people are honestly trying to influence the public to be... more empathetic to minorities. The fact that people don't appreciate that tells on those people, not the people doing DEI.<br /> <br /> Also, DEI training is such a non-issue. It's like doing your standard workplace harassment training that's been normal for decades. It's not some onerous burden. It's a set of guidelines to learn to avoid getting in trouble with HR, which is part of every job for other issues anyway. Just like CRT before it, bad faith people blew it up into this giant Thing, so people like you think there's some real deep seated issue to debate. DEI in the actual world isn't controversial, just like training people how to not sexually harass their coworkers isn't controversial. The controversy is made up bullshit labeled DEI so there's something for people to fight over. It's kinda sad that we have to have training programs in how not to be rude to people different than you as a society, but it's worse that people try to turn those programs into some giant conspiracy theory because that's the best they can do to create culture wars for politicians to fight over.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And stabdard workplace harassment training is typically despised as well. It\u2019s useless moral pandering.<br /> DEI is so controversial that it\u2019s very value is debated in both politics and by companies like disney who abandon it now.<br /> <br /> These programs aren\u2019t for teaching people to not be rude, but to swallow a set of beliefs that are not justified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519735#post1519735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This just sounds like you have your head buried in the sand.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite. I\u2019m open to facts, which you can\u2019t produce, not to emotional outburst and ideologically driven rants.<br /> <br /> Were you to listen to people outside your bubble, you\u2019d realise that what you believe are facts are far less absolute as you imagine it to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T13:50:27-07:00","id":1519784,"title":"","content":"Since we're accepting anecdotes as sufficient to qualify as facts for the purposes of this argument, I can pull out two supporting the specific argument that there is a racism problem in tabletop roleplaying:<br /> <br /> First of all, <b>the subject of this thread.</b><br /> <br /> But you could argue that's about the <i>industry</i>, not the <i>players</i>. So I'll instead refer to an anecdote I've seen shared a few times now by CTPhipps, so I'm assuming it's at least somewhat well-known on here, regarding Vampire LARP players in his community that used <i>Kindred of the East</i> to justify racism directed against Asian players. I don't agree with all of his opinions based on that anecdote, but it's a Fact by the standards of this discussion.<br /> <br /> (you can tag him if you want, but I don't feel like dragging his attention here is necessary atm)<br /> <br /> But hey, I can do you one better. I can bring in a whole pile of professional research that supports the broader argument that lack of diversity in media is harmful to those not being represented, and conversely that representation in media comes with positive effects:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://scholars.org/contribution/how-racial-stereotypes-popular-media-affect-people-and-what-hollywood-can-do-become#\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://scholars.org/sites/scholars/files/brief/2019/Pink%20Brief%20Background_21.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://scholars.org/contribution/how-racial-stereotypes-popular-media-affect-people-and-what-hollywood-can-do-become#\" target=\"_blank\"> How Racial Stereotypes in Popular Media Affect People &mdash; and What Hollywood Can Do to Become More Inclusive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://scholars.org/contribution/how-racial-stereotypes-popular-media-affect-people-and-what-hollywood-can-do-become#\" target=\"_blank\"> https://scholars.org/contribution/how-racial-stereotypes-popular-media-affect-people-and-what-hollywood-can-do-become# </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In 2015, the average U.S. resident consumed traditional and digital media for about 15.5 hours each day. In the same year, eight- to twelve-year-old children consumed an average of six hours of media a day and teens consumed nine hours. This mind-boggling amount of media consumption shapes how U.S. residents see the world, and racial imagery in the media has cumulative effects on society. Often biased media portrayals of racial groups cannot be dismissed as mere entertainment, especially not if their impact on youth are taken seriously. </div> </div> </div><br /> (also note that this one also has criticisms of current corporate diversity policies, so it's a strawman argument to act like people who support diversity in general support every approach that other people choose to take in that area)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://digitalcommons.chapman.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?referer=&amp;httpsredir=1&amp;article=1018&amp;context=comm_articles\" target=\"_blank\">https://digitalcommons.chapman.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?referer=&amp;httpsredir=1&amp;article=1018 &amp;context=comm_articles</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://cupola.gettysburg.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1757&amp;context=student_scholarship\" target=\"_blank\">https://cupola.gettysburg.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1757&amp;context=student_schol arship</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mediasmarts.ca/digital-media-literacy/media-issues/diversity-media/visible-minorities/racial-cultural-diversity-entertainment-media\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://mediasmarts.ca/sites/default/files/MediaSmarts_Eng_Logo_w_tag_30th%20%281%29_0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mediasmarts.ca/digital-media-literacy/media-issues/diversity-media/visible-minorities/racial-cultural-diversity-entertainment-media\" target=\"_blank\"> Racial and Cultural Diversity in Entertainment Media </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mediasmarts.ca/digital-media-literacy/media-issues/diversity-media/visible-minorities/racial-cultural-diversity-entertainment-media\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mediasmarts.ca/digital-media-literacy/media-issues/diversity-media/visible-minorities/racial-cultural-diversity-entertainment-media </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In much the same way that racialized groups are under- or misrepresented in news media, they are also not accurately portrayed in entertainment media, which tends to reinforce themes that are conveyed in the news. Although positive change is occurring, it is important that media content more accurately and fairly reflect the reality of Canadian multiculturalism. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yes, there ARE Facts on this side of the argument. I'd argue the facts are much better than a couple of cherry-picked examples of extreme and sensational headlines. If you can pull out someone trying to attack someone over their haircut and try and pin it on &quot;our&quot; side as an example of what's wrong, then I can pull up a video of Stefan Molyneux and argue that's &quot;your&quot; side, if we're allowed to just lump the people we disagree with in with the worst excesses of their ideological position without drawing any explicit connection between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Slight recant, I went half a step too far 08-04-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T14:40:03-07:00","id":1519787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519710#post1519710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, but I have to call bullshit. 5 rolists having fun at a table even using stereotypes does not destroy people lives.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes, especially those used for genuine fun (aka not targetted at someone concerned) are rarely correlated with any ill actions toward those concerned.<br /> <br /> A rolist playing a stereotype of a catholic priest will not then go out to insult the priest of his village. Nor does someone &quot;badly&quot; playing a native american will go out of their way to make real life natives miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read through AD&amp;D 1e's Deities and Demigods? By all accounts, hindsight has shown it to be a rather poor quality book that presents a lot of figures of real world cultures as what amounts to an epic level monster manual, but the more relevant reason is that it's horribly researched for every culture, so the Celt fans actually have some vehicle to find out why it's bad to lump all of the native peoples of the Americas* into one section and make what we can reasonably sure are very bad assumptions about figures of their beliefs. While not quite as horrible a lump as that, the Celtic myth section is replete with jumbled up bits of legendry, with the most notably being that they present the Welsh deity of the dead, Arawn, as the main deity of all Celts, from Ireland to their continental reaches. It pretty much just keeps getting worse from there; by the end of the section, someone who doesn't know better but read this book will be worse off than not having read anything at all. Those people then grow up, continue on in the hobby, and write Scion 1e's Celtic deities section, or other, similar passages.<br /> <br /> Oh, and also Werewolf. You know why there's a mangled spelling of Zhong Kui/Chung K'uei in the Nuwisha breed book? Because the WW's people were big D&amp;D players before they made their own games, and they didn't have access to anything telling them to stop and reconsider before choosing a grab bag of figures literally ripped from Deities and Demigods and plunking them down in the Nuwisha personal totems section, poor rendering of Chung K'uei (as &quot;Chung Kuel&quot;) included. The same applies to KotE with its demon archer and presentation of Tou Mu, and in a linguistic sense, that terrible, terrible text box from Blood and Silk that, much as with the Dei&amp;Dem Celtic myth chapter, is probably worse than not having read anything on the subject of transliteration at all, because at least then they're open to learning what Yale and Pinyin are, and why the former is neither one of the main systems for Chinese Romanization in the world, nor the agency responsible for spelling Beijing as Peking (as Yale Romanization was nowhere near even a twinkle in anyone's eye when pre-1850s Mandarin was around). With someone who's read that text box? They'll have confidence that they're right even though a quick wikipedia search shows them to be woefully in error, and the general response of humans to being told that they are wrong can include such tendencies as digging in and doubling down.<br /> <br /> Because of an rpg. Not an old book on Romanization of languages, not a professional document that's just old, but an rpg book, with basically no research behind it but a lot of mood and atmosphere than take hold of someone's head and get them to reject what actually is based on what they like.<br /> <br /> As a non-cultural example, consider that there's a bizarre number of people who think that dinosaurs being feathered makes them &quot;gay&quot;, or how difficult it is to convince people that dire wolves were not, in fact, giant wolves. The former isn't from rpgs, but the latter? That definitely is. And I've more or less traced it back to a typographical error from 1e to 2e AD&amp;D, when some agency or person transposed the size of dire wolves and wargs.<br /> <br /> Now stop and consider what W5 calls Hispo. What animal it uses to do that.<br /> <br /> Yeah. This terrible new edition has everything to do about this. It is, as other posters have noted, how we got here. A series of dumb accidents resulting from people not purging their hobby-related quick memory and doing some quick reality checks. Then the errors start to copy themselves, until few people realize why they ascribe something to anything, they just do it, and getting them to stop becomes like reminding people that dire wolves weren't what they've been presented as in post-1e AD&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* But for whatever reason the Aztecs got their own section. Could be the architecture, could be the lurid tales of Mexica spread by the Spaniards over the course of about 5 centuries.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T14:49:14-07:00","id":1519788,"title":"","content":"Well, I have another story for my online French friends to hear and then hang their heads as Americans continued to be justified in perpetuating the US stereotype of French people being