thing, they just do it, and getting them to stop becomes like reminding people that dire wolves weren't what they've been presented as in post-1e AD&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* But for whatever reason the Aztecs got their own section. Could be the architecture, could be the lurid tales of Mexica spread by the Spaniards over the course of about 5 centuries.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> sorry but it is also out of topic. You're talking about what people thought of published lore. Not of consenting adults playing stereotyped characters causing litteral harm outside the table","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T23:50:15-07:00","id":1519827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519788#post1519788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I have another story for my online French friends to hear and then hang their heads as Americans continued to be justified in perpetuating the US stereotype of French people being snobbish faux-intellectuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not believing your evidence less emotional outburst is being a snobbish faux intellectual?<br /> <br /> I'm afraid you're justifying the stereotype that americans are uneducated and uses concepts outside of their understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also saving a big ass post to get to one really important thing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519788#post1519788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you seriously claiming that thinking that people who openly play MYFAROG and discuss it in public should be met with social consequences for doing so is a minority position?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is, just look at those who scream about it. You'll always find the same people over and over again. It is a screaming minority<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T00:15:59-07:00","id":1519828,"title":"","content":"Nah, I'm not bothering with a big post, or correcting all your misuses of words you think make you sound smart. You think the majority of people are cool with a RPG written be a convicted arsonist and murderer, who wants to promote violent white supremacy via his game, being promoted by people that play for for the violent white supremacy is wants people to adopt as an ideology. There's not point in speaking to someone that thinks the majority opinion is that there should be no social consequences for openly espousing neo-Nazism, revisionist pagan racism, and other bigotry.<br /> <br /> Publicly denouncing MYFAROG is like, the lowest of the low bars in &quot;I want to express I'm not sympathetic to Nazism&quot; possible in RPGs. It's as easy as saying Hitler was evil.<br /> <br /> Go shove your eristics up somewhere uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T02:23:02-07:00","id":1519833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519828#post1519828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I'm not bothering with a big post, or correcting all your misuses of words you think make you sound smart. You think the majority of people are cool with a RPG written be a convicted arsonist and murderer, who wants to promote violent white supremacy via his game, being promoted by people that play for for the violent white supremacy is wants people to adopt as an ideology. There's not point in speaking to someone that thinks the majority opinion is that there should be no social consequences for openly espousing neo-Nazism, revisionist pagan racism, and other bigotry.<br /> <br /> Publicly denouncing MYFAROG is like, the lowest of the low bars in &quot;I want to express I'm not sympathetic to Nazism&quot; possible in RPGs. It's as easy as saying Hitler was evil.<br /> <br /> Go shove your eristics up somewhere uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you're not bothering to &quot;correct me&quot; because you can't. Your position isn't based on reason or fact.<br /> <br /> and again, you fail to adress what I actually say.<br /> <br /> At no point did I say that it's good to write a game about propagating nazism and publishing it.<br /> in fact I stated multiple time that writers should not push their ideology on players.<br /> <br /> I'm still only talking about your baseless belief that consenting rolists playing stereotyical characters harm people outside of the table.<br /> <br /> IT's only the fift comment with which you answer entirely out of topic.<br /> <br /> You shouod use chagpt to explain to you what I write, it will clearly do a better job than your analysis skills.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bYou confuse playing a character and espousing an ideology.<br /> <br /> Which show you don't understand the very concept of rolism.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T18:52:22-07:00","id":1519914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519826#post1519826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> sorry but it is also out of topic. You're talking about what people thought of published lore. Not of consenting adults playing stereotyped characters causing litteral harm outside the table</div> </div> </div> </div>The only people who considered that D&amp;D lore were the ones who didn't know better. Who went on to write games, like at WWGS. Some of them went on to also realize that they weren't really good takes and that it probably wasn't good to propagate them. And that is quite definitely and example of harm outside the table because a consenting adult agreed to go along with a shit take for far too long. I mean, the shit takes don't just pop up from nothing; they're long-established shit takes that no one tends to question. And all too frequently, someone who does question them gets shuffled into the part of being &quot;no fun&quot;. Kind of like this thread, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:19:10-07:00","id":1519924,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hey everyone, I decided to try and lay out my broader position on all of this, building up from the foundations to more specific issues.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Ethics of Giving A Fuck vs. Not My Problem</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I\u2019m going to start by saying that I think most people are supportive of multiculturalism and diversity in a broad sense, or at the very least they don\u2019t see it as some blasphemous social engineering being imposed by out-of-touch elites. I\u2019d say the majority is probably just largely indifferent; they get their Vampire/Werewolf/Dragon game, read the books without thinking about them too much, roll the dice and enjoy themselves without caring much about whether a given identity-group is being represented accurately or fairly. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> hit on above, this is precisely how wrong portrayals that started in Dungeons and Dragons found their way into World of Darkness, via authors who absorbed those ideas uncritically and regurgitated them without thinking about them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now here\u2019s the thing: I don\u2019t really care that much about what the majority position is. Anyone who has studied history and isn\u2019t an arch-conservative or religious fundamentalist needs to accept that majorities have often been happy to accept things that we nowadays, rightly in my opinion, regard as unacceptable and immoral behaviour. So I don\u2019t care about whether or not the majority agrees, and I don\u2019t care whether or not it is the law: I care about whether or not it is <b>right</b>.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Which is opening the can of cans of worms that is moral philosophy, how do we decide what\u2019s right? Lots of opinions out there on that, and I\u2019m not going to claim that the ideas I\u2019m sharing are original. But one way of looking at this issue is \u201cgiving a shit\u201d versus \u201cnot my problem.\u201d In the \u201cnot my problem\u201d framework, there are lines drawn around your moral obligations, and anything that doesn\u2019t fall inside that bubble of responsibility does not need to be acted upon. So, for example, if someone cannot draw a direct line between stereotypes in a roleplaying gamebook and hate crimes, then there is no moral obligation to remove or critically engage with those stereotypes, because it\u2019s \u201cnot my problem\u201d until I personally decide that the level of harm involved merits my concern.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In contrast, what I\u2019m calling \u201cgiving a shit\u201d is about actively caring about what is happening in the wider world. It\u2019s not just about drawing a line around the things you care about and the things that you don\u2019t, but caring about everyone and everything, and constantly striving to make things better for everyone. And to be clear, that\u2019s not something you can do perfectly, and the fact that you will make mistakes or not be able to do as much as you would like is something you grit your teeth and accept regardless of how much it sucks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So to be very clear, I\u2019m approaching this matter from the perspective of Giving A Shit. I\u2019m not interested in policing what individuals do at their private gaming table, but I am genuinely boggled by the argument that official materials <b>should</b> be filled with ignorant and incorrect stereotypes that will make a significant portion of the customer base uncomfortable or upset. Who wants to fight over the right to be aggressively and proudly incorrect? I actively invite people to engage with efforts promoting multiculturalism and diversity critically, to try and improve them by making reasonable arguments against the flaws and offering constructive advice on how to do better. But arguing that the entire premise is flawed and unwelcome not only seems inaccurate to me, but it is morally wrong regardless of whether or not it reflects the majority position, because I Give A Shit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And before you even try, it\u2019s not your job to decide how much misery another person needs to experience \u201ccharacter growth.\u201d The universe shits on all of us more than enough, thank you very much, so don\u2019t try to make excuses for cruelty by arguing that it\u2019s \u201cfor their own good.\u201d Nor will I accept the idea that some minority of ignorant bigots are <b>actually</b> the victims because everyone else rightly treats their ideas as toxic.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Diversity Matters</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I provided links above to the work of professionals who have studied the impacts of diversity in media, and how it contributes to the mental and emotional health of the groups being represented. If you combine Giving A Shit as a motive with said evidence supporting the idea that good representation helps people, then wanting good representation reasonably follows from there. Again, you can have criticisms about how the particular details of how representation is achieved; complaints about tokenism come just as often from people who otherwise support diversity and representation in media as they do from angry right-wingers freaking out about the Cultural Marxists brainwashing their children.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This is also a good chance to touch on the contrast between corporate diversity efforts versus Giving A Shit. To the extent that Paradox is trying to avoid nasty stereotypes and invasive cultural appropriation, it\u2019s not because they care about the feelings of their customer base. Individual workers at Paradox might, but the institution is involved in this to make <b>money</b>. To the extent that they have chosen a side in the \u201cculture war,\u201d it is because that is the side where they see the most profit to be made. To the extent that many of their efforts are either ineffectual or actively detrimental, a good part of that comes from the fact that the actual motive of Making Money interferes with the pretend motive of Giving A Shit; if diversity is too expensive, or creates some uncomfortable publicity, can it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Obviously, not every decision Paradox has made with the WoD has been the most profitable one, but I am pretty confident that they\u2019ve run the numbers and figured out that the people who actively want them to pander to trashy outdated stereotypes are a minority compared to the customers who would be insulted by said content and would rightly take their money elsewhere. So I\u2019m not very persuaded by any attempts to declare, without evidence, that our position is actually the minority one.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Microaggressions</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In my earlier posts, I took the position that uncritically playing with game material that employs bigoted stereotypes runs the risk of those stereotypes bleeding over into your activity outside of the game, and that it even has the potential to ruin lives in extreme cases. The next couple of sections will be defending that position.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">First of all, I\u2019m not at all trying to make the claim that you can consistently draw a direct causal link from \u201cI read a bunch of racist stereotypes\u201d to \u201cI went out and committed a hate crime.\u201d The problem is a systemic one, where no individual factor can be pointed out as singularly responsible, but all of them collectively contribute to the result. In the case of a bunch of gamers interacting with trashy stereotypes without critically engaging and educating themselves on the subject, the most common result is not going to be a spree-shooter, but a walking micro-aggression factory. They\u2019re going to spew out ignorant comments that hurt people without thinking, often without even realizing. And unless they weirdly happen to live the life of an ethno-nationalist already without happening to be one, surrounded by people just like them who aren\u2019t reduced to a bunch of denigrating caricatures in the fiction they consume, then they\u2019re going to open their mouth at some point out in public and ram their foot inside at mach speed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There are two problems with this. The first being that they are going around hurting people. Whether or not it\u2019s intentional both matters and doesn\u2019t matter; it matters in the sense that they might genuinely be open to correction if they aren\u2019t being harmful intentionally; it does not matter inasmuch as <b>you don\u2019t get to go around hurting people over and over just because you didn\u2019t think about it.</b> They aren\u2019t evil, they don\u2019t need to be punished, but they don\u2019t get to cry foul when people tell them that what they are saying is wrong and that it is hurting people. If you don\u2019t care about hurting people, fine, but you\u2019re telling on yourself when you adamantly argue for your right to inflict your ignorance on the people around you.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Toilet Bowl</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But hey, I didn\u2019t just talk about microaggressions, I talked about \u201cruined lives.\u201d So let\u2019s talk about how \u201cinnocent\u201d bigotry can lead down a spiral that ruins lives. And boy, do I have a twist for you!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">We\u2019re going to go back a bit and talk about what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> had to say earlier about how people get their back up when they get corrected on this stuff because they want to just keep doing what they\u2019re doing, without having to take responsibility or make an effort to change. Now let\u2019s take that and apply it to our \u201cinnocent\u201d little microaggression-eer from above, we\u2019ll call him Bob. Bob is hanging out with Sally, and Bob spouts off some ignorant thing he picked up in an RPG book that aggressively argues against the need to accurately represent minorities and treat them with respect. I\u2019m not going to bother with a specific example, because you can get the idea without me having to say anything stupid like that out loud. Sally is part of the identity-group that Bob just slandered, and she is understandably upset that her friend/acquaintance/etc. has expressed something so ignorant and hurtful.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Let\u2019s talk about intellectual and emotional labour. When you demand that a member of a minority group that experiences oppression take the time to explain that oppression to you, or even worse demand that they prove it, when you could easily educate yourself on the subject if you actually cared enough to bother, you are attempting to force intellectual labour onto them. And when you say something ignorant that hurts someone, and then demand that they remain calm and civil while you continue to say the hurtful thing because you \u201cjust don\u2019t understand what the big deal is,\u201d then you are demanding emotional labour from them. This is why people who regularly experience bigotry tend to get irritated when they are asked to prove something that they\u2019ve already proved nine times this week to ignorant little shits who would rather treat the matter like a \u201cgotcha question\u201d then just take the time to learn about it themselves.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All of this is meant to lead up to the fact that Sally is probably not going to be especially gentle with Bob when she responds to his microaggression. She may not try to be mean, but she\u2019s probably going to say something that will make him feel uncomfortable in some way, because she is going to tell him that something he did or believes is wrong. Going back to the tendency for people to get their back up when being called out on their nonsense, Bob is pretty likely in turn to get defensive, deflect, make excuses, and Sally may escalate her challenge in response, leading to a cycle of Bob getting increasingly bitter as he keeps getting trouble over, in his mind, \u201cnothing.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Eventually, though, Bob will find his people. Or they will find him. The people who don\u2019t make him feel bad over his \u201cjokes,\u201d who don\u2019t tell him he\u2019s wrong not to care about this stuff. Eventually, they might start \u201cshowing\u201d him how \u201cthose people\u201d are actually responsible for everything that he thinks is wrong in his life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You know, the fascists.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once again, I have to be clear that I am not describing this as a slippery slope that everyone goes down under these circumstances. But it is enough of a trend that it\u2019s pretty well documented on platforms like YouTube, a spiral of radicalization that people fall down to varying degrees. And you don\u2019t need to go too far down in order to become the kind of person who\u2019ll contribute to making another person\u2019s life a living hell. Online death threats, doxing, SWATing. Your individual contributions don\u2019t even need to be the worst to add to an experience that can be downright soul-crushing in its entirety. And at the most extreme end of the spectrum, you have the ones that end up killing people.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The real twist? The ones who end up going down this spiral don\u2019t just end up ruining the lives of other people. They often end up ruining their own lives as well, damaging or destroying healthy relationships and building up connections with a toxic and abusive community that could turn it\u2019s wrath back on them if they are ever regarded as a \u201ctraitor.\u201d And to be clear, this is not the worst aspect; I'm not going to be gleeful over people finding out the hard way that bigotry is almost as toxic to the bigot as the target of their hate, but the people they have been helping to hurt didn't bring it on themselves.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Most of the evidence that I have on this stuff is not tied to tabletop roleplaying games specifically. A lot of what I just wrote is based on \u201cThe Alt-Right Playbook: How to Radicalize a Normie\u201d by Innuendo Studios, can\u2019t recommend it enough. While it doesn\u2019t talk about tabletop players in particular, it does discuss a broader trend of alt-right efforts to spread into geek fandoms, because they\u2019re finding a lot of fertile soil in the form of young aggrieved white men. I think that makes a pretty strong inductive case for the idea that casual bigotry within gaming communities is a problem that can spiral out of control if it\u2019s overlooked or ignored.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So can I Play a Nazi or Not?</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I feel like I need to introduce this section by making something very clear: I am not demanding that roleplayers only play \u201cgood\u201d characters, or that certain kinds of \u201cevil\u201d characters should be off limits. I play monsters. I enjoy playing monsters, characters doing horrible things and treating the suffering of others as irrelevant or entertaining. I must admit, I\u2019m not generally interested in playing as a bigot for the most part, because bigotry has always struck me as a boring and stupid kind of evil. But I\u2019m not at all opposed to people roleplaying as bigots, in principle. Nor do I think that oppressed minority groups must always be depicted as flawless saints.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And I\u2019m also going to invoke the \u201cI\u2019m not your dad\u201d principle once more, and make sure that you understand that I don\u2019t think the Roleplay Police should be breaking into your kitchen-table game to make sure that you\u2019re not tossing around slurs. You can do <b>whatever you want</b>. And so can we, by telling you that we think you\u2019re wrong as long as you keep trying to carry on a public conversation about how insulted you are that the people writing books for a massive audience don\u2019t want to shit on a portion of said audience.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So, of course you can play a Nazi. No one is going to stop you.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But <b>how</b> and <b>why</b> you play a Nazi matters. You could create a game set in WW2 Germany that seeks to explore the history and psychology of life in the Third Reich. It could be interesting and informative. And if one of the players in your group had his great-grandparents die during the Holocaust, it\u2019s something you should <b>PROBABLY</b> discuss with them first!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you decided that you just wanted to play as a Nazi because it\u2019s edgy and controversial and gives you an easy excuse to play a card-carrying, moustache-twirling villain, I\u2019m probably going to find it uninteresting and superficial, but I wouldn\u2019t think you were doing anything wrong (again, as long as everyone at the table is cool with it).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you decide to play as a Nazi because it gives you a cover to say things In Character that you wish you could say Out Of Character, then that is pretty obviously shitty and wrong, unless you\u2019re <b>actually</b> a bloody Nazi.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So yes, you can absolutely play as a Nazi. You can even play as a Nazi and be a perfectly fine and upstanding person. But if you\u2019re choosing to play as a Nazi even when it makes the other people at your table uncomfortable, or if you\u2019re going to start thoughtlessly repeating Nazi propaganda you stumbled on in a game book because you didn\u2019t bother to educate yourself and learn the extent to which so much of how we commonly view the Nazis is <b>based on Nazi propaganda</b>, then people are probably going to call you on your shit.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Conclusion</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you are going to go to the mat fighting for your right to indulge in bigoted falsehoods, you\u2019re telling on yourself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Or you need to make a <b>much</b> better case for the idea that the Roleplay Police are waiting outside your door, ready to swoop down and destroy your life for thought-crime. Other people giving a shit about being nice to other human beings is not Orwell\u2019s nightmare come to life.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T00:40:55-07:00","id":1520504,"title":"","content":"J.F. Sambrano shared the post below: <hr /><br /> I wrote my last major take on the controversy surrounding <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hashtag/WerewolftheApocalypse5th?src=hashtag_click\" target=\"_blank\">#WerewolftheApocalypse5th</a> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hashtag/W5?src=hashtag_click\" target=\"_blank\">#W5</a> and how I was treated by Brand Editor Karim Muammar on the rpgnet forums. This one includes some receipts of the uncredited work if you wanted to see that.\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition-and-the-anti-indigeneity-in-the-gaming-industry.912221/post-24904125\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre.../post-24904125</a>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T04:01:53-07:00","id":1520510,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I expected a lot of these revelations. The oral culture part being ignored hurts the most, though. As JS says, it is by no means an inaccurate method and the fact the Galliard EXIST should have been a clue how important it was. While I don't agree with JS that animism is mostly an Indigenous faith, I agree how much the writing in W5 is quite literally treating the matter from not only a Eurocentric but also a VERY colonial perspective. There is this huge lack of respect for elders in communities and also this very Western view of information being separated from its people.<br /> <br /> As for the focus on SoH, I feel it is because most of us (ESPECIALLY me) have little to say about Indigenous matters concerning American soil.<br /> <br /> The Stolen Moons part is frankly insane to read. KM is given the reason why the original name is bad and PLENTY of examples of what to use instead. Instead, he focuses on the name in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> This is just how I see it, but a lot of the anti-Indigenous stuff seems to come from the context of a non-American and I'd say, Northern European person. There is this naivete towards the weight of the terms and culture I can recognize I once had as well. While the white americans of course aren't any more respectful towards Native Americans, they still have more context on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T04:38:54-07:00","id":1520512,"title":"","content":"Man, that Stolen Moons bit... KM is just so dismissive. It seems like a big part of why concepts like animism and oral history are handled so badly in this book is just a very dismissive and careless attitude. &quot;New name for Skin Dancers...? Eh, whatever, doesn't seem that big of a deal... maybe something with &quot;skin&quot; because they flay them, right?&quot; and he says that even though JS explained the issue quite clearly and gave alternative names.<br /> <br /> I don't even see the part of &quot;oral histories&quot; to be eurocentric. It's just ignorant. We wouldn't have the Illiad, for example, if oral history and culture didn't work. There are tons of versions of the Robin Hood story because that was part of an oral storytelling-tradition as well. Grimm's fairy tales are all about taking oral storytelling and writing it down but it's connected to that tradition. Even with a eurocentric perspective, the W5 corebook's take on oral history/storytelling doesn't make sense. That's why I think of the Garou in that book as &quot;amnesiacs&quot; because how else are you even supposed to explain that...?<br /> <br /> James Sambrano's first paragraph of his take on the Ghost Council also made me feel sad... Because unlike the explorers of dark knowledge with a goal to educate and sort out dangerous knowledge, the version in the W5 corebook are secretive knowledge-hoarders with an &quot;The ends justify the means&quot;-attitude... It's like night and day in how they're written about. And with JS's version I can understand how they fit into the Garou-Nation, with the version in the W5 corebook I can't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T04:50:26-07:00","id":1520514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520512#post1520512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't even see the part of &quot;oral histories&quot; to be eurocentric. It's just ignorant. We wouldn't have the Illiad, for example, if oral history and culture didn't work. There are tons of versions of the Robin Hood story because that was part of an oral storytelling-tradition as well. Grimm's fairy tales are all about taking oral storytelling and writing it down but it's connected to that tradition. Even with a eurocentric perspective, the W5 corebook's take on oral history/storytelling doesn't make sense. That's why I think of the Garou in that book as &quot;amnesiacs&quot; because how else are you even supposed to explain that...?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is Eurocentric in the sense that Illiad, Robin Hood, Kalevala and King Arthur are to us <b>now</b> as fiction and not real. But to Indigenous communities as to garou, the oral histories are true stories unless stated otherwise. And this difference clearly affects how garou oral culture is written in W5, just stories at best.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T04:59:51-07:00","id":1520515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520514#post1520514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is Eurocentric in the sense that Illiad, Robin Hood, Kalevala and King Arthur are to us <b>now</b> as fiction and not real. But to Indigenous communities as to garou, the oral histories are true stories unless stated otherwise. And this difference clearly affects how garou oral culture is written in W5, just stories at best.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but there I see the actual issue is more the limiting horizon of having an ahistorical perspective trapped in the &quot;now&quot;.<br /> <br /> In this case, the task is to take these fantasy-werewolf-people that have existed since the dawn of time and integrate them into our world somehow. But being dismissive of other cultures <i>and </i>being dismissive of one's own culture's history... then I guess, it's no wonder that all the writers of this book could think of is &quot;Who even knows what happened back then...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T05:44:27-07:00","id":1520517,"title":"","content":"Its probably worth noting a lot of 5th ed is heavily north European code for example while they got rid of the coptic aspects of setities the clan now draws heavily from western ideas on cults and corruption. Effectively they didn't really blank the setting as much make it very very white.<br /> <br /> the same applies to w5 were the tribes and werewolf society is coded on western politics eg-the extremists are evil and specific ideas on what certain things mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-13-2023, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T05:51:36-07:00","id":1520518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520512#post1520512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that Stolen Moons bit... KM is just so dismissive. It seems like a big part of why concepts like animism and oral history are handled so badly in this book is just a very dismissive and careless attitude. &quot;New name for Skin Dancers...? Eh, whatever, doesn't seem that big of a deal... maybe something with &quot;skin&quot; because they flay them, right?&quot; and he says that even though JS explained the issue quite clearly and gave alternative names.<br /> <br /> I don't even see the part of &quot;oral histories&quot; to be eurocentric. It's just ignorant. We wouldn't have the Illiad, for example, if oral history and culture didn't work. There are tons of versions of the Robin Hood story because that was part of an oral storytelling-tradition as well. Grimm's fairy tales are all about taking oral storytelling and writing it down but it's connected to that tradition. Even with a eurocentric perspective, the W5 corebook's take on oral history/storytelling doesn't make sense. That's why I think of the Garou in that book as &quot;amnesiacs&quot; because how else are you even supposed to explain that...?<br /> <br /> James Sambrano's first paragraph of his take on the Ghost Council also made me feel sad... Because unlike the explorers of dark knowledge with a goal to educate and sort out dangerous knowledge, the version in the W5 corebook are secretive knowledge-hoarders with an &quot;The ends justify the means&quot;-attitude... It's like night and day in how they're written about. And with JS's version I can understand how they fit into the Garou-Nation, with the version in the W5 corebook I can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with this post, especially the last paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T09:51:35-07:00","id":1520533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520517#post1520517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting a lot of 5th ed is heavily north European code for example while they got rid of the coptic aspects of setities the clan now draws heavily from western ideas on cults and corruption. Effectively they didn't really blank the setting as much make it very very white.<br /> <br /> the same applies to w5 were the tribes and werewolf society is coded on western politics eg-the extremists are evil and specific ideas on what certain things mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only offer my own perspective, but I could totally see this happening if the writers are trying to avoid controversy but aren't thinking globally enough. Unless you take time to learn otherwise, there is this sort of ignorance towards the racial relations in US and other such countries found here. While immigrants are nothing new and Roma and Sami exist, the default is still uniformly white. Not like in the US where whiteness expectation comes from an unconscious assumption of privilege but a sort of sense that there isn't anything else.<br /> <br /> Let's remember, while people in the US see whiteness everywhere as the same, it is not so here. Here, regardless of skin colour, everyone not native is an outsider. There is racism, but it is often not a 'your kind is lesser than me because x' but 'you are an outsider to me, your ways offend me.' Of course, the Roma and Sami get the former more, but even then an US person would just see all as white.<br /> <br /> So I feel it is very hard for a person from Sweden/Norway(outside Greenland)/Denmark/Finland to understand the complexities JS referred to. But that is why keeping an open mind is VERY important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T12:56:28-07:00","id":1520543,"title":"","content":"The link is not working, can someone summarize the fight with Stolen Moons or whatever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T13:05:37-07:00","id":1520544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520543#post1520543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The link is not working, can someone summarize the fight with Stolen Moons or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Link works fine....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T13:50:46-07:00","id":1520545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520544#post1520544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Link works fine....</div> </div> </div> </div>So it must be something on my computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T13:57:55-07:00","id":1520547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520543#post1520543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The link is not working, can someone summarize the fight with Stolen Moons or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try posting it again. Does this help? (The link preview is for the first post on that page of the post thread, not the post the link directly goes to.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition-and-the-anti-indigeneity-in-the-gaming-industry.912221/page-18#post-24904125\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...#post-24904125</a><br /> <br /> Here's the same link in code markdown so you should be able to see the entire thing to just copy and paste it into your URL bar, in case the forum shortens the link again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition-and-the-anti-indigeneity-in-the-gaming-industry.912221/page-18#post-24904125</pre> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T15:40:43-07:00","id":1520551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520533#post1520533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only offer my own perspective, but I could totally see this happening if the writers are trying to avoid controversy but aren't thinking globally enough. Unless you take time to learn otherwise, there is this sort of ignorance towards the racial relations in US and other such countries found here. While immigrants are nothing new and Roma and Sami exist, the default is still uniformly white. Not like in the US where whiteness expectation comes from an unconscious assumption of privilege but a sort of sense that there isn't anything else.<br /> <br /> Let's remember, while people in the US see whiteness everywhere as the same, it is not so here. Here, regardless of skin colour, everyone not native is an outsider. There is racism, but it is often not a 'your kind is lesser than me because x' but 'you are an outsider to me, your ways offend me.' Of course, the Roma and Sami get the former more, but even then an US person would just see all as white.<br /> <br /> So I feel it is very hard for a person from Sweden/Norway(outside Greenland)/Denmark/Finland to understand the complexities JS referred to. But that is why keeping an open mind is VERY important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah American approaches to Ethnicity are pretty odd since they tend to incorperate elements of class, which sometimes is strangely insightful but sometimes ineligant.<br /> <br /> thankfully as a brit hating poor people is far more fundamental to our socially structure unless you're playing off differant groups of poor people against each other. You can be any colour you want but God help you if you dont pronounce scone skown.<br /> <br /> But to take it back to w5 their is a fundental misconception that their ethnically neutral setting is that even stuff like the authors approach to politics and thematics works on western ideas.<br /> <br /> I cannot imagine the authors considered their works counter culture approach relies on contrasting a specific culture.<br /> <br /> on reflection I'm not even sure how you'd build an neutral state game, considering a broad variety of issues such as your own in built bias and well werewolves being a westerm pop culture product How would you even do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-13-2023, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T17:51:19-07:00","id":1520563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520517#post1520517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting a lot of 5th ed is heavily north European code for example while they got rid of the coptic aspects of setities the clan now draws heavily from western ideas on cults and corruption. Effectively they didn't really blank the setting as much make it very very white.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that it's worth noting that with the Setites, in 5e there's an on-going civil war. The North American/European segments of the clan broke away and formed their own anti-clan. You still have the coptic/gnostic Setites and they still operate heavily in other parts of the world, they're just less prominent now in North America and Europe compared to the off-shoot of the clan. Also this civil war was being set up and telegraphed in the V20 books, so it would have happened whether V5 came out or if V20 had continued on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T23:04:44-07:00","id":1520572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520551#post1520551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on reflection I'm not even sure how you'd build an neutral state game, considering a broad variety of issues such as your own in built bias and well werewolves being a westerm pop culture product How would you even do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't. Even if we look just at North Europe, you have years of colonialism, crusaders and general arguing.<br /> <br /> The best you can do is to be aware of what and WHO you write and if you aren't sure, ask the people you are writing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T00:08:41-07:00","id":1520573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520563#post1520563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that it's worth noting that with the Setites, in 5e there's an on-going civil war. The North American/European segments of the clan broke away and formed their own anti-clan. You still have the coptic/gnostic Setites and they still operate heavily in other parts of the world, they're just less prominent now in North America and Europe compared to the off-shoot of the clan. Also this civil war was being set up and telegraphed in the V20 books, so it would have happened whether V5 came out or if V20 had continued on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, but the fact remains the culturally coptic clan is now a western clan as represented in v5.<br /> what really tickles me is how the 7 corebook clans are comparatively untouched because the authors couldnt detect their coding and they presumed they came from universal archeotypes.<br /> <br /> in their attempts to wipe the setting of ethnicity they made it very very northen european. Similar to w5 really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T00:52:24-07:00","id":1520575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520572#post1520572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't. Even if we look just at North Europe, you have years of colonialism, crusaders and general arguing.<br /> <br /> The best you can do is to be aware of what and WHO you write and if you aren't sure, ask the people you are writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you do a solid job of research then you can avoid a lot of pitfalls. This is especially good if your a low budget group and can't afford advisors.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine recently spend some time reading up on late antiquity sassanid/arabian and early medieval islamic history for his homebrew setting, they wernt the primary setting point but he wanted to flesh out the setting since one of his regulars is iranian-british and tends to request playing a fantasy equivelant. Plus arabian nights style fantasy is underdone despite being awesome and thats before you start digging deeper. I'm looking forward to seeing how he incorporates it into a somewhat grim low fantasy setting considering how well fleshed out his byzantine equivelant was","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-14-2023, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T02:08:49-07:00","id":1520579,"title":"","content":"An issue the book is running into is that the writers don't really seem to have even a clear idea of what Garou-culture is like. Questions like what is happening at a Moot, how does the Galliard's duty expresses itself or what the Garou's relationship with spirits looks like... instead of exploring those things, the writing runs away from offering concrete ideas on those topics. Like this sidebar on pg 207.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Context Matters<br /> Remember that animism is a real-world belief system practiced by millions of people in one form or another both throughout history and today. Be appropriately respectful at your table. Werewolf does not suppose the Garou\u2019s specific animistic lens is the \u201ctruth\u201d of how animism works in the game world \u2014 people\u2019s faiths and perspectives are not to be reduced to game mechanics. The relationship between the Garou and the Umbra is but a single, fictional expression of animism.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Instead of actually exploring real animistic beliefs and tying them to Garou culture, this sidebar shows how the book is avoiding the topic completely. It's saying &quot;Please be respectful of real-world animistic beliefs which we won't get into in this book and if any portrayal of animism in this book comes off as offensive... well, actually it isn't even the &quot;truth&quot; in the game-setting, so there you go.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T05:10:09-07:00","id":1520584,"title":"","content":"As I noted in the Release Thoughts thread, creating a fictional form of animism that might resemble but is clearly distinct from any real world animistic belief system requires actually fully describing it in the game text. It's sort of basic &quot;show don't tell&quot; stuff: we need to see how the Garou practice animism in a way that's significantly different from existing real world beliefs as to not be offensive, not just be told that they practice a fictional religion but never actually see how it's different and if it's really different enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T12:28:00-07:00","id":1520604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520584#post1520584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I noted in the Release Thoughts thread, creating a fictional form of animism that might resemble but is clearly distinct from any real world animistic belief system requires actually fully describing it in the game text. It's sort of basic &quot;show don't tell&quot; stuff: we need to see how the Garou practice animism in a way that's significantly different from existing real world beliefs as to not be offensive, not just be told that they practice a fictional religion but never actually see how it's different and if it's really different enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they're pretty hobbled as they're using neo paganism as cosmological starting point. They'd probably have to loose the concept of gaia and reverance of nature to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> I can even see certain similarities in forsaken lore with irl faiths and that's way more meticulously written than w5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T19:54:20-07:00","id":1520640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520573#post1520573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possible, but the fact remains the culturally coptic clan is now a western clan as represented in v5.<br /> what really tickles me is how the 7 corebook clans are comparatively untouched because the authors couldnt detect their coding and they presumed they came from universal archeotypes.<br /> <br /> in their attempts to wipe the setting of ethnicity they made it very very northen european. Similar to w5 really.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Setites were always more of Conan the Barbarian, Thulsa Doom expies than a serious, legitimate coptic group. Really the coptic themes were just window dressing. And while later editions tried to expand them past their pulp roots, I don't think they ever did a terribly great job. Those pulpy Thulsa Doom vampires still exist in V5, they're just a bit less likely to be the ones that players run into rather than the Jim Jones or David Koresh types. Ultimately the Setites never represented or were supposed to represent &quot;Egyptians&quot; in the way that the Eldest and Youngest brothers represented Native Americans. They were always vampires designed around pulp fiction than any real life culture (look no further than the fact that Set is a snake).<br /> <br /> That said, remember that in V5 the Ashirra joined the Camarilla and Assamites are a full Camarilla clan. V5 also removed the Kuei-jin and introduced Camarilla vampires into many parts of Asia. So I don't know that the idea that V5 is white washing the game and removing the presence of minorities really stands up to close scrutiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T20:08:30-07:00","id":1520641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520640#post1520640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, remember that in V5 the Ashirra joined the Camarilla and Assamites are a full Camarilla clan. V5 also removed the Kuei-jin and introduced Camarilla vampires into many parts of Asia. So I don't know that the idea that V5 is white washing the game and removing the presence of minorities really stands up to close scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't only the Banu Haqim?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T21:03:41-07:00","id":1520645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520641#post1520641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't only the Banu Haqim?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ashirra and the Camarilla formed an alliance, and functionally the two groups are essentially one now. Then the Banu Haqim officially joined the Camarilla becoming a full clan alongside the Toreador and such. So if anything, V5 has been pushing the presence of non-European vampires a bit more heavily than previous editions did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T01:08:32-07:00","id":1520651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520640#post1520640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Setites were always more of Conan the Barbarian, Thulsa Doom expies than a serious, legitimate coptic group. Really the coptic themes were just window dressing. And while later editions tried to expand them past their pulp roots, I don't think they ever did a terribly great job. Those pulpy Thulsa Doom vampires still exist in V5, they're just a bit less likely to be the ones that players run into rather than the Jim Jones or David Koresh types. Ultimately the Setites never represented or were supposed to represent &quot;Egyptians&quot; in the way that the Eldest and Youngest brothers represented Native Americans. They were always vampires designed around pulp fiction than any real life culture (look no further than the fact that Set is a snake).<br /> <br /> That said, remember that in V5 the Ashirra joined the Camarilla and Assamites are a full Camarilla clan. V5 also removed the Kuei-jin and introduced Camarilla vampires into many parts of Asia. So I don't know that the idea that V5 is white washing the game and removing the presence of minorities really stands up to close scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Initially yeah but as the game developed they moved away from that. By the time of Revised they're even incorporating gnostic heresies into their outlook. It's also important to comment they represent an ancient coptic pagan heresy rather than contemporary Egyptians or even modern Coptics. If I wanted to actually address the Conan stuff it makes serpantis typhonicbeastis or give them another disciplines (probably setite sorcery or potence)<br /> <br /> Its also ultimately the same issue as w5 with the wendigo and uktena were instead of doing it right where you integrate accurate egypitian coptic outlooks while diversifying the clan they wipe the board and ended up whitewashing the clan much like they did with the uktena and wendigo<br /> <br /> The ashirra have largely been ignored in the lore and treated as carmarilla again in v5. They joined the (now stupid evil) carmarilla as effectively a way or removing ant meaningful distinction. The same applies to the kuei jin were their removal is a replacement with Western style vampires. While they were often problematic (asian hell) they did represent an understanding of cultural distinctions of folklore Western style vampires in Asia do not reflect diversity in any context. Especially as drawn from the 14 clans.<br /> <br /> The banu haqim are less severaly hit than the setites but theirs still a process of then being sanitised. also theirs the assumption the non European ethninicites have to join an western power block for legitimacy. Like the ashirra their assimilation and whitewashing is presented as positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-15-2023, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:46:01-07:00","id":1520672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520651#post1520651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Initially yeah but as the game developed they moved away from that. By the time of Revised they're even incorporating gnostic heresies into their outlook. It's also important to comment they represent an ancient coptic pagan heresy rather than contemporary Egyptians or even modern Coptics. If I wanted to actually address the Conan stuff it makes serpantis typhonicbeastis or give them another disciplines (probably setite sorcery or potence)</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said earlier, the gameline tried to move away from the pulp roots, but I don't think they ever succeded. The clan was rooted in a fantasy concept that doesn't exist in real life. And even where they tried taking the clan in a different direction, it was still pulp fantasy with a patina of a historical group of people that no longer exist. Pushing the clan in an entirely different direction isn't whitewashing anything, because again, we're dealing with a pulp fantasy group with a few ties to an ancient group of historical peoples that don't really exist anymore. Setites are absolutely not, and were never intended to be a representation of modern day Coptic Egyptians or any other existing modern day group and I don't think pushing them in that direction would have been good for anyone.<br /> <br /> Whitewashing hurts people removing people from the cultural dialogue, but nobody is being hurt by the civil war among the Followers of Set or the fact that the clan is no longer 100% bad guys out of Conan the Barbarian wearing Egytpian cosplay. Just like nobody is being hurt by the Giovanni no longer being only a bunch of Italian mafiosos. <br /> <br /> In werewolf, all of the Tribes were based on various cultural groups. But in vampire only the 4 &quot;outsider&quot; Clans were based on (negative) cultural stereotypes (Ravnos = Roma, Giovanni = Italian Mafia, Assamites = middle eastern assassins and then the Followers were based on Conan the Barbarian and only dropped in Egypt because it's a desert with snakes). This was always recognized as problematic, not just the negative stereotypes, but simply having 4 clans that were so closely tied to very specific culture or fantasy elements made it much harder to work with those clans than the 9 that weren't. I think it was a smart idea to try and strip out a lot of the cultural baggage from those 4 clans and pull them up to the same universal standard that you see in the other 9 clans.<br /> <br /> Note that I wouldn't agree with doing the same thing in Werewolf, because in Werewolf the cultural connections have been fundamental to all of the Tribes since the beginning. Werewolf and V20 are different beasts, and what might work in one wouldn't work in another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T23:34:46-07:00","id":1520747,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that JS pointed out the passage about residential &quot;schools&quot;, even if just in passing. Even though everything in that passage is correct, given the context of how they were treated by KM, that Paradox would have the nerve to drop this description of a real-world atrocity (even if it was written by Indigenous authors) into the text with zero context or actual connection to the game just to say that &quot;Look! I know we treated a real Indigenous author like crap and actively belittled everything they suggested, and removed all agency and representation from the groups actually affected by this atrocity, but! We brought it up, so we're totally not racist!&quot; It made me so angry I almost just quit reading the W5 book entirely. While I'm not against bringing up serious subjects like this in games, there's just something so gross and cynical about how it was handled here.<br /> <br /> Maybe it just hits very close to home because where I am now, there are a lot of survivors of these &quot;schools&quot; and the kind of things they went through still keeps me up at night sometimes. It's definitely a subject that deserves more respect than being used as a shield against racism accusations. But I don't blame the authors of the passage itself. Like I said, the information is correct, and this subject matter is important. Any education on the subject is better than nothing, I guess. This is on Paradox and KM for actively refusing to back this passage up with respect anywhere else, despite being told repeatedly that they should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 08-16-2023, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:09:08-07:00","id":1520755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520640#post1520640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Setites were always more of Conan the Barbarian, Thulsa Doom expies than a serious, legitimate coptic group. Really the coptic themes were just window dressing. And while later editions tried to expand them past their pulp roots, I don't think they ever did a terribly great job. Those pulpy Thulsa Doom vampires still exist in V5, they're just a bit less likely to be the ones that players run into rather than the Jim Jones or David Koresh types. Ultimately the Setites never represented or were supposed to represent &quot;Egyptians&quot; in the way that the Eldest and Youngest brothers represented Native Americans. They were always vampires designed around pulp fiction than any real life culture (look no further than the fact that Set is a snake).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard disagree on Setites &quot;never represented&quot; Egyptians. We can debate whether they did it &quot;well&quot;, but &quot;they [never] did a terribly great job&quot; is a No True Scotsmen. Whether White Wolf did the rebranding well or not, they went HARD on making Setites Egyptian, especially in Revised. Everything from the Revised Clan Book, to the iconic novel character being Hesha Ruhadze, to &quot;Setite Sorcery&quot; being just Akhu (Egyptian blood sorcery) in <i>Blood Sacrifice</i>, to the fact they're rivals to the Silent Striders AND Children of Osiris AND literal Mummies.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like Thulsa Doom snake cultists as much as the next person, and headcanon that branch as being the primordial version of &quot;Set-ism&quot; as established by Set himself.<br /> <br /> But it's really a reach to insist that the Egyptian theme isn't, for large parts of the Clan's history, a core facet of both the culture and mission statement of the Followers of Set. It wasn't the &quot;original&quot; intent, but it's the big fat middle portion between them being Conan antagonists, and the considerable deviations from the Egyptian theme in V20 and V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:33:41-07:00","id":1520758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520672#post1520672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said earlier, the gameline tried to move away from the pulp roots, but I don't think they ever succeded. The clan was rooted in a fantasy concept that doesn't exist in real life. And even where they tried taking the clan in a different direction, it was still pulp fantasy with a patina of a historical group of people that no longer exist. Pushing the clan in an entirely different direction isn't whitewashing anything, because again, we're dealing with a pulp fantasy group with a few ties to an ancient group of historical peoples that don't really exist anymore. Setites are absolutely not, and were never intended to be a representation of modern day Coptic Egyptians or any other existing modern day group and I don't think pushing them in that direction would have been good for anyone.<br /> <br /> Whitewashing hurts people removing people from the cultural dialogue, but nobody is being hurt by the civil war among the Followers of Set or the fact that the clan is no longer 100% bad guys out of Conan the Barbarian wearing Egytpian cosplay. Just like nobody is being hurt by the Giovanni no longer being only a bunch of Italian mafiosos.<br /> <br /> In werewolf, all of the Tribes were based on various cultural groups. But in vampire only the 4 &quot;outsider&quot; Clans were based on (negative) cultural stereotypes (Ravnos = Roma, Giovanni = Italian Mafia, Assamites = middle eastern assassins and then the Followers were based on Conan the Barbarian and only dropped in Egypt because it's a desert with snakes). This was always recognized as problematic, not just the negative stereotypes, but simply having 4 clans that were so closely tied to very specific culture or fantasy elements made it much harder to work with those clans than the 9 that weren't. I think it was a smart idea to try and strip out a lot of the cultural baggage from those 4 clans and pull them up to the same universal standard that you see in the other 9 clans.<br /> <br /> Note that I wouldn't agree with doing the same thing in Werewolf, because in Werewolf the cultural connections have been fundamental to all of the Tribes since the beginning. Werewolf and V20 are different beasts, and what might work in one wouldn't work in another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oddlly I prefer it a little pulpy. The attempts at more grounded in 5th have make it both blander and highlighted to absurdities (plus i find the ministry flavourless). I think we're getting off point here, we can go back and forth on how fantasy the setites where and if this is harmful or not but that isn't my point with them. My point is white wolf rewrites in 5th ed tend to make factions more Western because they can't clock their own cultural bias' the Setites becoming the ministry are an example of that. You previously had clan which was explicitly non-European which is now another European clan. This leads into w5 were the effects are now implicitly negative with all the tribes being western when push comes to shove.<br /> <br /> As a side the Giovanni got more problematic as time ground on, initially a sinister family of Venitian merchants they became mafia by revised.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-16-2023, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T06:29:32-07:00","id":1520764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520758#post1520758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Oddlly I prefer it a little pulpy. The attempts at more grounded in 5th have make it both blander and highlighted to absurdities (plus i find the ministry flavourless). I think we're getting off point here, we can go back and forth on how fantasy the setites where and if this is harmful or not but that isn't my point with them. My point is white wolf rewrites in 5th ed tend to make factions more Western because they can't clock their own cultural bias' the Setites becoming the ministry are an example of that. You previously had clan which was explicitly non-European which is now another European clan. This leads into w5 were the effects are now implicitly negative with all the tribes being western when push comes to shove.<br /> <br /> As a side the Giovanni got more problematic as time ground on, initially a sinister family of Venitian merchants they became mafia by revised.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Setites were explicitly non-European, but more than that, non-Earthian. Again, they were yoinked out of Conan stuffed into bad Egyptian cosplay, and later attempts to tie them to an extinct time period in Egypt were never successful or terribly compelling. Trying to do that just made them more limited and difficult for Storytellers to use compared to other clans like the Toreador, Ventrue, Gangrel or others who could be from anywhere and from any culture. Those Clans aren't and never were just European (like one of the most prominent Malkavians since first edition is from India). And as VtM Revised and then V20 went along the Setites, like the Giovanni, Ravnos and Assamites were pushed to be more open and inclusive like all of the other vampire clans.<br /> <br /> Again, the direction of the Setites and Giovanni wasn't caused by V5, it was already being planned back in V20 and they were dropping hints these events were coming even before Paradox purchased the rights to VtM. If V20 had continued, you would have still seen the Setite Civil War and the Family Reunion. Those were logical plot points that the V20 authors were working for in order to make all of the vampire clans fully cross-cultural and make sure they were found in every country of the world rather than limiting them to specific cultures (or non-existent ones in the case of the Setites).<br /> <br /> I don't think your argument that this was caused because the authors &quot;couldn't clock their own cultural bias&quot; but was pre-planned for a long period of time, well in advance of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:04:45-07:00","id":1520806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520764#post1520764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Setites were explicitly non-European, but more than that, non-Earthian. Again, they were yoinked out of Conan stuffed into bad Egyptian cosplay, and later attempts to tie them to an extinct time period in Egypt were never successful or terribly compelling. Trying to do that just made them more limited and difficult for Storytellers to use compared to other clans like the Toreador, Ventrue, Gangrel or others who could be from anywhere and from any culture. Those Clans aren't and never were just European (like one of the most prominent Malkavians since first edition is from India). And as VtM Revised and then V20 went along the Setites, like the Giovanni, Ravnos and Assamites were pushed to be more open and inclusive like all of the other vampire clans.<br /> <br /> Again, the direction of the Setites and Giovanni wasn't caused by V5, it was already being planned back in V20 and they were dropping hints these events were coming even before Paradox purchased the rights to VtM. If V20 had continued, you would have still seen the Setite Civil War and the Family Reunion. Those were logical plot points that the V20 authors were working for in order to make all of the vampire clans fully cross-cultural and make sure they were found in every country of the world rather than limiting them to specific cultures (or non-existent ones in the case of the Setites).<br /> <br /> I don't think your argument that this was caused because the authors &quot;couldn't clock their own cultural bias&quot; but was pre-planned for a long period of time, well in advance of V5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> i think yourl're overstating your case, the setites certainly have influences from pulpy fiction but they're strongly drawing on actual Egyptian mythology and irl mysticism as far back as revised. By that stage the snake stuff is a pulpy referance, i suppose you could argue that their tendancy towards subversion over direct force is a referance to pulp but considering all clans subvert and infiltrate its a bit of a stretch.<br /> no toreador, ventrue and gangrel are not neutral at all they can be from &quot;any culture&quot; (so could setites incidently with localised interpretations of setite mytholgy) but theyr3 obviously and heavily drawn from western ideas for example toreador are very obviously drawn dark romanticism of Anne rice novels and carmilla. I'm surprised you brought them up considering your focus on the setites and pulp.<br /> <br /> well thats not really my point about the giovanni but since you brought them The heceta are an interesting example because while you can play them as generic western fantasy necromancer they retained a number of very distinct alternatives including the giovanni (as well as jewish mythology femminists, aztecs and two types of ethnic cannabal amoung others). It's quite a clever little bit of writting in that they've managed to have its cake and eat it. Its largely why im reluctant to draw the same contrast as setites getting wiped for the ministry.<br /> <br /> I'm unclear on how it being planned as far back as v20 would negate my observation on the trend. But I think were at a slightly mismatch here since you're objection isn't that you disagree with my observation that the ministry is more whiter then the ministry (I'm actually unclear on your stance on that) but that the change is a positive and pre established in v20. Now we can go back and forth on if its a good changed (I personally find the ministry boring and has too much overlap with other clans) and I don't really care about who made the call since I'm commenting on trend here. Am I misunderstanding you and either way how does this negate the issue were 5th ed games efforts to wipe cultural backgrounds from the game actually end up creating a series of generalist western groups because they draw on a fallacious assumption of default pop culture ideas as universals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-17-2023, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T16:51:07-07:00","id":1520846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feels like the idea that it was all planned and going down a path to the V5 plot is doing a lot of heavy lifting. There was certainly a lot of serious up in regards to a reckoning for the Giovanni but I think the idea it was going to manifest the way it did is a wee stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oynx path were working towards something resembling a cappadocian/harbinger ressurgance they may have adapted their ideas to v5. The family Union was a bit silly but it got the job done and was better written than pretty much any other clan imagining in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T20:49:28-07:00","id":1520921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1520806#post1520806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unclear on how it being planned as far back as v20 would negate my observation on the trend. But I think were at a slightly mismatch here since you're objection isn't that you disagree with my observation that the ministry is more whiter then the ministry (I'm actually unclear on your stance on that) .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do actually disagree with that idea. It's not like cults are a uniquely white experience. You see religious cults in every country and every culture. I mean look at Japan where the ex-Prime Minister was just assassinated because of his links to a cult, or South Korea, where the previous President was forced out of office because of her ties to a cult.<br /> <br /> So if you look at places like Japan, South Korea, India, Africa, South America, etc, you'll see tons of cults there. The Ministry in those places would not be foreign &quot;white people&quot; bringing white people's religious beliefs, nor would they be foreign Egyptians bringing in foreign religious beliefs, but rather the Ministry in those parts of the world would be formed by local vampires with local religious beliefs. Ultimately with the Ministry you're going to see Norse or Greek cults, but you'll also see Caribbean, South America, African, Asian and cults from all over the world.<br /> <br /> And even in the US and Europe you'll see plenty of non-white cults because, again, cults aren't something that only white people get into. In fact, if you look at many major cult groups in the US like Jonestown or the Branch Dividians, you'll see that there are white members, but also a lot of non-white members too.<br /> <br /> Also note that I don't believe that there's any &quot;whitewashing&quot; going on. The Followers of Set never represented Egyptians, either modern ones or ones from thousands of years ago. They were created by a white dude who watched Conan the Barbarian and then stuck the clan based off the villain in Egypt because Egypt has sand.<br /> <br /> Later books tried to improve the cosplay but it was never successful because the core of the Followers was entirely based off completely wrong ideas about Egypt. If anything the Followers were &quot;brownwashed&quot; because fundamentally they were white people playing with snakes while dressed as Egyptians. Getting rid of that cartoony idea and replacing it with something more universal that can speak to anyone is much better for the gameline and isn't impacting non-white people because the Followers were never an authentic representation of non-white people in the first place and the base idea was simply unsalvagable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-19-2023, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T01:04:13-07:00","id":1520926,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> I agree with you that the intent was to globalise the Followers and not to whitewash them.<br /> <br /> However, Egypt is at the core of the Setites. It was from the start, because they drew from followers of Set as a whole from where they originated. They clearly show that their vision draws more on the literary and comic book Stygia of Conan lore than just the movie that has a singular Set cult without the broader context.<br /> <br /> Stygia is Ancient Egypt (except where its Ptolomeic Egypt), where the head diety is a capricious Snake God of Darkness. It is rulled by devious sorceror kings and powerful and manipulative priests that have the blessings of Set. They are expansionist, meddle with other countries and religions through cooption and assassination and seem to lie on the ruins of a nation of Lovecraft's snakepeople.<br /> <br /> So a rather specific version of Egypt was tied into the Followers from their origin. What revised did is that it tried to move away from that and make them about real world Egypt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T19:19:51-07:00","id":1521001,"title":"","content":"Again, the Setites weren't ever tied to real, actual Egypt, but to a pulp Egypt inspired by someone who wasn't all that familiar with real Egypt. Like where did the corruptive, deceptive evil snake come from? Snakes in Egypt never had that sort of symbolisms (in Egypt snakes were the symbols of divine protection and wisdom). The idea of the corruptive, deceptive evil snake comes from the Bible and that was the snake symbology that was used in Howards setting (which was loosely inspired by Egypt) and which then served as the basis for the Followers of Set. It's very important to note that since day one the Setites never represented or embodied an authentic Egypt. <br /> <br /> As such, moving the Setites away from those pulp roots isn't engaging in &quot;whitewashing&quot; or a removal of a racial or cultural minority, because the Setites were never authentic ancient Egyptians in the first place, and indeed, were never meant to be authentic ancient Egyptians when they were first created. Revised attempted to try to come up with explanations for why the Setites didn't resemble in the least actual Egyptian mythology, but no matter how many knots the writers twisted themselves into, it just never worked. At the foundation the Setites simply weren't and never were a good or authentic representation of real world ancient Egypt and, short of a complete rewrite could never be authentic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T19:42:13-07:00","id":1521003,"title":"","content":"Never mind, I know the Setites were related to Apophis or not, maybe I misunderstood because... snakes, but they picked fights with the Silent Striders, Mummies, Osiris, a tribe of Bastet, Celican I think, plus the Bone Gnawers and maybe the Assamites. Is there any module, supplement, book anything that mentions a supposed end to this confrontation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T20:52:28-07:00","id":1521007,"title":"","content":"In the lore, Set ate Apophis or somehow gained Apophis' power, and that's where the snake/evil stuff came from. Would have made more sense if the had been written as the Children of Apophis from the start, but that was how they tried to explain why Set had evil snake powers. Also it was the Bubasti, not Celican. <br /> <br /> So back in ancient Egypt, Set murdered his brother Osiris and tried to take over Egypt. Osiris' wife Isis (a powerful mage) and Osiris son Horus (who eventually became a mummy) declared war on Set. The Silent Striders, the Mokole, the Nagah and the Bubasti all ended up getting involved on Isis' side as well. The Setites basically ended up winning the conflict. They maintained control of Egypt for centuries. Set cursed the Silent Striders and forced them out of Egypt. They basically wiped out the Bubasti kinfolk and the tribe teeted on the edge of extinction ever since. Osiris (now a wraith) and Horus made more mummies to keep fighting against Set. Later the Setites and Assamites ended up entering into a conflict. Both were powerful vampire clans in the Middle East. The Assamites were mostly judges and demon hunters, and the Setites ticked enough boxes that the two clans were enemies. They also ended up at war with the Tal'mahe'Ra, a faction of immensely powerful vampires.<br /> <br /> The Setites were sort of the generic &quot;evil&quot; clan and were basically in conflict with groups from every other line - VtM, WtA, Wraith, Mage. I think Changeling was the only line in which the Setites didn't have some sort of beef or conflict with an established power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T02:12:59-08:00","id":1526971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518471-w5-anti-indigeneity-and-other-issues?p=1519134#post1519134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter\u2019s Entertainment created a blog post, presumably before it taken in house, giving a tease for what their version had in store. Based on what I\u2019ve seen setting wise from W5 I\u2019m not sure much had changed from the original direction Karim had given for the book. Besides the whole decoupling tribes from cultures thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_2000,h_1125,al_c,q_95,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: The Apocalypse - 5th Edition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A Storytelling Game of Savage Resistance Have you ever taken a moment to just stop, observe the world around you, and see the injustice of it all? You can see it, the scars and sores of the land. You can smell it, the degradation and decay in the air. You can feel it, the fever and tremors of a dying world. The question is: When will you rage? At its heart, Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a Storytelling game of Savage Resistance. What does that mean? It means that Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a gam </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth noting Werewolf: The Apocalypse Heart of the Forest was announced a couple of weeks before Justin Achilli was announced as the World of Darkness Brand Creative Lead and came out right around the time WoD announced Hunter: The Reckoning and W5 being done in house. I would imagine by the time Justin came one the game would have been mostly written without time for rewrites. Which would indicate similar to the Hunters team, any story direction would likely have come from Karim.<br /> <br /> If you watched Justin\u2019s announcement, you may remember this was when it was first publicly made known W5 would be a reimagining of WtA. WoD had stated publicly HotF would be cannon. So when Justin said one of the tribes had fallen to whatever they\u2019re calling it, anyone played HotF knew it was the Get as the game described them as Garou Fascist.<br /> <br /> I feel like I\u2019m rambling so my TLDR, it\u2019s quite possible Justin had no part in the \u201cAll Get are Fascist thing\u201d and it\u2019s been part of direction given by Karim the entire time. When the Hunters team wouldn\u2019t right it they pulled it in house to find someone who would.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny fact?<br /> <br /> HEART OF THE FOREST takes a flying **** on the Garou fascist thing too.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris get a bunch of flack from the local Garou as a bunch of N*zis and supremacists. Then you find out your character is a Get of Fenris by blood and that your ancestors were a bunch of Polish Resistance fighters.<br /> <br /> Still ruthless and bloodthirsty warriors but Get of Fenris dedicated to protecting the forest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}